}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babinsaud-del/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/babinsaud-del","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bsaud-e2e/E2E_automation/commits/d01fb7f2ef8176b30caed4e8d39e73b9adcde128/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T05:31:31Z","email":"babin.saud@innovatetech.co","name":"@babinsaud"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T05:31:31Z","email":"babin.saud@innovatetech.co","name":"@babinsaud"},"message":"Add CI QA Agent: classify Playwright failures via DeepSeek, post to PR\n\nscripts/qa-report.js reads Playwright''s JSON reporter output after each\nCI run, classifies any failures (Automation/locator, Timing/wait,\nTest-data, Environment, or Application defect) via DeepSeek''s API, and\nposts the report as a PR comment when the pushed branch has an open PR\n(otherwise prints to the workflow log). The known SecurityError/\nmicrofrontend false-positive pattern is hard-coded to always classify\nas Environment issue, never Application defect.\n\nWired into .github/workflows/e2e-tests.yml as a step after the test run\n(if: always(), so it reports on both passing and failing runs). Needs a\nDEEPSEEK_API_KEY repo secret to actually call the API.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d769cba51821d583fc0ab6bd05626f7f2a9be2a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bsaud-e2e/E2E_automation/git/trees/d769cba51821d583fc0ab6bd05626f7f2a9be2a2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bsaud-e2e/E2E_automation/git/commits/d01fb7f2ef8176b30caed4e8d39e73b9adcde128","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256758147?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babinsaud-del/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/babinsaud-del/followers","following_url":"https: