/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/a5fb0f2a7cc8834175941019836191c78571b32c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/ce027c8545aec9467cf9aa51d425bdfa3e08687b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T03:15:23Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T03:15:23Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"message":"fix(voice): whisper.sh acts on the fleet that exists, and drop a noise-level claim\n\nTWO CORRECTIONS TO THE COMMIT BEFORE THIS.\n\n`whisper_nodes()` defaulted to the worker whenever WHISPER_NODES was unset,\nso after `up --all-nodes` every other command acted on the worker alone:\n`status` reported a healthy fleet while a second engine nobody could see was\nstill holding a GPU, `url` printed one endpoint, and `down` left the head''s\nengine running. It now reads the running fleet back from ASR_BASE_URLS in\n.env, with an explicit WHISPER_NODES still winning and the worker as the\nfallback for a fresh install.\n\nAnd the docs claimed a loaded-but-idle engine costs the chat model 7.6% of\nits decode throughput. It does not — repeated single-stream baselines on this\nbox scatter over 54-74 tok/s run to run, so a ~5 tok/s difference is inside\nthe noise and should not have been stated as a measurement. The saturated\nrows (24.6 / 23.0 / 14.7 tok/s) sit far outside that band and stand\nunchanged.\n\nVerified: `status` now reports both engines ready; `url` prints both.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"70439b24f401cad15e6d01427f76210646c1cdc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/trees/70439b24f401cad15e6d01427f76210646c1cdc3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/commits/ce027c8545aec9467cf9aa51d425bdfa3e08687b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commit/ce027c8545aec9467cf9aa51d425bdfa3e08687b","node_id":"C_kwDOUWBCP9oAKGNlMDI3Yzg1NDVhZWM5NDY3Y2Y5YWE1MWQ0MjViZGZhM2UwODY4N2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commit/9d37eec610da96df78e711c8423d86e9bd8d1717","sha":"9d37eec610da96df78e711c8423d86e9bd8d1717","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/9d37eec610da96df78e711c8423d86e9bd8d1717"}],"sha":"ce027c8545aec9467cf9aa51d425bdfa3e08687b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/ce027c8545aec9467cf9aa51d425bdfa3e08687b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/9d37eec610da96df78e711c8423d86e9bd8d1717/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T03:00:39Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T03:00:46Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"message":"feat(voice): whisper-large-v3 replaces Qwen3-ASR, on both Sparks\n\nThe composer''s microphone now transcribes with openai/whisper-large-v3,\npinned at 06f233fe06e7, running as its own Compose project on the worker\nand on the head. Requests go to whichever engine has the fewest in flight.\n\nRECOVERED, NOT WRITTEN. A working whisper service was already running on\nthe worker and serving correctly, but nothing that produced it was in git:\nthe compose file and the server lived only in the worker''s\n~/.techsara-cluster. compose/compose.whisper.yaml, compose/whisper/ and\nscripts/whisper.sh are that deployment, recovered so it can be rebuilt,\nreviewed and rolled back.\n\nWHAT THE SECOND ENGINE BUYS, MEASURED. The engine serialises — server.py\nholds a _gpu_lock around every transcription — so one engine decodes one\nclip at a time and throughput is flat from 1 concurrent clip to 16. Two\nengines are therefore a clean 1.9x from two clips upward, and 1.00x at\none. A second concurrent speaker, not a faster transcript:\n\n    1 concurrent   2.12s -> 2.03s   (1.00x)\n    2 concurrent   4.00s -> 2.05s   (1.95x)\n    4 concurrent   7.99s -> 4.16s   (1.92x)\n    8 concurrent  15.99s -> 8.31s   (1.92x)\n   16 concurrent  32.02s -> 16.79s  (1.91x)\n\nAND WHAT IT COSTS. A saturated speech engine takes the chat model from\n71 tok/s to ~24 on EITHER node — the main model is tensor-parallel across\nboth Sparks and runs at the speed of its slower rank, so \"speech lives on\nthe worker so it does not disturb chat\" was a memory argument and never a\ncompute one. Both saturated: 15 tok/s. Hence ASR_MAX_CONCURRENT drops\nfrom 4 to 2 per engine: one clip decoding, one ready to start, and a\nthird caller told to retry rather than silently extending the window in\nwhich everyone''s answers are slow.\n\nThe swap is not a free upgrade and the docs say so. Whisper is ~2x slower\non a single clip and ~15x lower in throughput, because vLLM gave the old\nengine continuous batching and the transformers pipeline gives none. What\nit buys is 30 languages to 99 — including the Indic languages the old\nmodel could not transcribe at all — and the reference sequential\nlong-form decoder. On English and French, published WER favours the model\nremoved. Serving whisper under vLLM would recover batching at the cost of\nthat decoder; docs/VOICE.md records this as the next real trade.\n\nAlso:\n- whisper.sh down now takes the stopped engine back OUT of\n  ASR_BASE_URLS, and turns the feature off when none are left. Stopping\n  an engine while .env still listed it left the orchestrator retrying a\n  dead endpoint every twenty seconds forever.\n- the vllm-asr Prometheus job is removed rather than repointed: server.py\n  has no /metrics on any port, so the job could only ever report a target\n  that is permanently down, and a target that is red by construction\n  teaches people to ignore red targets.\n- SUPPORTED_LANGUAGES is derived from the model''s own tokenizer, with a\n  test asserting the two agree, so the advertised set cannot drift from\n  what the engine does. The metrics language label widens 30 -> 100.\n- no language is sent to the engine at all: this deployment code-switches\n  mid-sentence and forcing one mistranscribes the other half.\n\nBackend suite 2932 passed, 4 skipped. Verified end to end through the\norchestrator: 8 clips, 4 to each engine, 8/8 word-perfect.\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"883da20a2a2142e589eff241542a0ebff1b637d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/trees/883da20a2a2142e589eff241542a0ebff1b637d5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/commits/9d37eec610da96df78e711c8423d86e9bd8d1717","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avat