"organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/4af7f1ddc97eea36fc9c39f350a1f3b005a2fd5e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T23:08:38Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T23:08:38Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"message":"refactor(asr): remove legacy voice models and reset ASR stack","tree":{"sha":"f18f09a6c616c471ad4c89410f9e87ba3defeb64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/trees/f18f09a6c616c471ad4c89410f9e87ba3defeb64"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/commits/4af7f1ddc97eea36fc9c39f350a1f3b005a2fd5e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commit/4af7f1ddc97eea36fc9c39f350a1f3b005a2fd5e","node_id":"C_kwDOUWBCP9oAKDRhZjdmMWRkYzk3ZWVhMzZmYzljMzlmMzUwYTFmM2IwMDVhMmZkNWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commit/b12b4c1755e05c78560f1aba628c052f4960106e","sha":"b12b4c1755e05c78560f1aba628c052f4960106e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/b12b4c1755e05c78560f1aba628c052f4960106e"}],"sha":"4af7f1ddc97eea36fc9c39f350a1f3b005a2fd5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/4af7f1ddc97eea36fc9c39f350a1f3b005a2fd5e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/640479e0364e00c8ae986f1dde670fd0944baab3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T22:46:33Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T22:46:33Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"message":"fix(memory): the assistant was shown three exchanges of a sixty-message chat\n\nReported with a shared conversation: a 60-message French lesson — corrections,\ngrammar, practice, every turn context-aware — then \"how to translate\" answered\nwith a Python tutorial about googletrans. The user replied \"i was not talking\nabout coding\".\n\nROOT CAUSE. engines/chat.py built every prompt as\n`recent_turns(history, 6)` — the last six MESSAGES, three exchanges. At that\nturn those six were a goodnight exchange, and messages 4-45 were the lesson.\n\nThe 6 was not unreasonable when written; it was a defence against a small\ncontext window. It became wrong when the window grew to 1,000,000 tokens and\nnothing took over the job, because the two components that SHOULD bound\nhistory both measure themselves as a FRACTION of the window:\n\n  the conversation                       5,826 tokens = 0.58% of the window\n  usable budget on a 1M window          ~991,000 tokens\n  compaction fires above 0.80           ~793,000 tokens\n\nNo real conversation reaches that, so no rolling summary was ever written —\nconversation_summaries had zero rows for this thread. Between \"six turns\" and\n\"793,000 tokens\" there was nothing at all, and a hardcoded slice was the only\nmemory a long chat had. The full history reached the engine and the engine\nthrew it away; this was never a budget decision.\n\nTHE FIX IS THE LAYERING, not a bigger number. Bounding history belongs to\ncompaction (a rolling summary) and to context.fit_request (the physical\nwindow); an engine cutting on top of both only discards what they chose to\nkeep. So:\n\n  - CONTEXT_COMPACT_MAX_TOKENS (40,000) gives compaction an ABSOLUTE trigger\n    beside the fraction, whichever fires first. That also revives the\n    in-conversation semantic index: recall.index_folded is only reached when\n    compaction folds, which is why conversation_chunks was empty too.\n  - CHAT_HISTORY_TURNS (400) replaces the literal, in chat and in every other\n    ANSWER prompt — the same amnesia was one route away in rag, sql, search,\n    dataset, document, url, repo, crawl, vision and agent, 23 slice sites\n    whose largest n was 8.\n\nPrompts whose OUTPUT LEAVES THE BOX keep their tight windows deliberately:\nconversation_turns strips the memory blocks precisely because search queries\nand research plans travel to third parties, and _ask_sql writes SQL rather\nthan prose. A test now fails if any ANSWER prompt reintroduces a literal.\n\nTWO THINGS MADE THE WRONG ANSWER CODE-SHAPED, both fixed:\n  - CODE_INSTRUCTION is attached to every assistant turn and said, flatly,\n    \"if the request is ambiguous, state the assumption you coded against\".\n    Inside a French lesson \"how to translate\" IS ambiguous, and the model did\n    as instructed. Now scoped to requests for code.\n  - Cross-chat semantic recall has an absolute score floor (0.30) and no\n    relative one, so with nothing relevant to find it returns whatever clears\n    it — it handed this turn snippets about code. A relative floor keyed to\n    the best hit drops the tail without ever discarding the top result.\n\nAlso fixes an UnboundLocalError this uncovered: _run_step_impl imported\nsettings inside three conditional branches, which makes the name local to the\nwhole function, so any use on another branch would have raised.\n\nVERIFIED BY REPLAYING THE REAL CONVERSATION against the live model — same\nhistory, same question, only the window differs:\n  6 turns  -> \"googletrans ... Google Translate, DeepL ...\"   (the bug)\n  fixed    -> \"J''ai envie de dormir\"                          (the lesson)\n\n2,926 backend tests pass.","tree":{"sha":"099869561b099050176bc4f2446680736537e641","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/trees/099869561b099050176bc4f2446680736537e641"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/commits/640479e0364e00c8ae986f1dde670fd0944baab3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commit/640479e0364e00c8ae986f1dde670fd0944baab3","node_id":"C_kwDOUWBCP9oAKDY0MDQ3OWUwMzY0ZTAwYzhhZTk4NmYxZGRlNjcwZmQwOTQ0YmFhYjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commit/51a02a6907fc664c0e88a0f6c545e6701a0fbf0f","sha":"51a02a6907fc664c0e88a0f6c545e6701a0fbf0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/51a02a6907fc664c0e88a0f6c545e6701a0fbf0f"}],"sha":"640479e0364e00c8ae986f1dde670fd0944baab3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/640479e0364e00c8ae986f1dde670fd0944baab3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/51a02a6907fc664c0e88a0f6c545e6701a0fbf0f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T21:30:59Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T21:30:59Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"message":"fix(llm): 1,000,000 output tokens at every effort — the budget was the bug\n\nReported from the product: a long code answer stopped mid-function with\n\"This answer reached its length limit and stops here. 8,000 tokens were\nwritten.\" That notice is mine and it was telling the truth, which makes it\nworse: the answer was stopped by a budget I chose, not by anything about the\nquestion.\n\nTHE TUNING WAS PATHOLOGICAL, not merely conservative. Fast was given\nMODEL_MAX_OUTPUT (8,192) as its TOTAL, while engines/chat.py asks for 8,000\ntokens per call. So a truncated Fast answer wrote exactly one segment, found\n192 tokens left against a 512-token minimum segment, and stopped — reporting\na limit it had reached on the FIRST call. It bought nothing at all: the old\nbehaviour was silent truncation, and this was silent truncation with a notice\nattached.\n\nTHE REASONING BEHIND THE TIERING WAS ALSO BACKWARDS. I set it to stop a\npassing question costing hours of GPU. But a budget does not stop an\nexpensive question being asked — it stops a needed answer being finished.\nEverything that actually protects the loop is about QUALITY and is always on,\nwhatever the budget: the model saying it is done, a segment that repeats text\nalready written, no forward progress twice running, the segment cap, the\ndeadline.\n\nSo all three efforts now get the configured ceiling. What it costs is worth\nstating plainly: ~46 output tokens/second, so 8k is about three minutes and\n50k about eighteen. Almost nothing will reach the ceiling, because almost\neverything stops at `complete` — measured against the live model, a request\ngiven a 40,000-token budget wrote 2,011 and stopped, and the graph-algorithms\nreference this was tested with wrote 4,700 tokens, 17,343 characters and 16\ncode blocks in one segment and finished on its own.\n\nThe per-effort settings remain, so the tiering can be restored by setting any\nof CONTINUATION_BUDGET_{FAST,THINK,MAX} lower.\n\nA test now pins the SHAPE of the bug rather than the value: no effort budget\nmay land just above one of the chat engine''s per-call ceilings, because that\nis the one region where a budget converts a finished-looking answer into a\nclaim that a limit was reached.","tree":{"sha":"787a7d2732fe38adaf66640f5d5048e105af689d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/trees/787a7d2732fe38adaf66640f5d5048e105af689d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/commits/51a02a6907fc664c0e88a0f6c545e6701a0fbf0f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commit/51a02a6907fc664c0e88a0f6c545e6701a0fbf0f","node_id":"C_kwDOUWBCP9oAKDUxYTAyYTY5MDdmYzY2NGMwZTg4YTBmNmM1NDVlNjcwMWEwZmJmMGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commit/9a399a2b5582a181759f2ff4df128a6779da9c22","sha":"9a399a2b5582a181759f2ff4df128a6779da9c22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/9a399a2b5582a181759f2ff4df128a6779da9c22"}],"sha":"51a02a6907fc664c0e88a0f6c545e6701a0fbf0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/51a02a6907fc664c0e88a0f6c545e6701a0fbf0f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/9a399a2b5582a181759f2ff4df128a6779da9c22/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T21:05:52Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T21:05:52Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"message":"ci: remove the deploy-decision probe — it found what it was for\n\nIt proved the mechanism on run 34161168711: kill-switch-formatted passed,\nkill-switch-bare did not, and the deploy ran for the first time. The finding\nis in the comment on the condition, which is where it is useful; a permanent\njob whose own name says a step is \"expected to fail\" is not.\n\nThe \"Will the deploy run?\" summary in `ci-ok` STAYS. That one is not a probe:\nit reports the event, ref and kill switch on every run, so the next time a\ndeploy does not happen the run says why instead of being silent about it.","tree":{"sha":"772be80803115f2feec2c273be274091618598cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/trees/772be80803115f2feec2c273be274091618598cf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/commits/9a399a2b5582a181759f2ff4df128a6779da9c22","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commit/9a399a2b5582a181759f2ff4df128a6779da9c22","node_id":"C_kwDOUWBCP9oAKDlhMzk5YTJiNTU4MmExODE3NTlmMmZmNGRmMTI4YTY3NzlkYTljMjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commit/a1114ca537deb657441409de22c3fab606c3d5f6","sha":"a1114ca537deb657441409de22c3fab606c3d5f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/a1114ca537deb657441409de22c3fab606c3d5f6"}],"sha":"9a399a2b5582a181759f2ff4df128a6779da9c22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/9a399a2b5582a181759f2ff4df128a6779da9c22"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/a1114ca537deb657441409de22c3fab606c3d5f6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T20:54:34Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T20:54:34Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"message":"ci: an unset repository variable is null, and null != ''false'' is false\n\nTHE BUG. Three pushes to main, every suite green, deploy skipped with no\nreason each time. The instrumentation from the last commit found it: `ci-ok`,\n`ref` and `event` all passed and the kill-switch clause did not — with the\nvariable UNSET.\n\nAn unset repository variable is `null`, not an empty string. GitHub coerces\nmismatched types to a number before comparing, and ''false'' converts to NaN;\nevery comparison against NaN is false, so `vars.DEPLOY_ON_PUSH != ''false''` is\nFALSE when nothing is set. Both `==` and `!=` are false at once, which is why\nreading the condition three times did not find it — it is not wrong in any\nway that reads as wrong.\n\nTHE FIX. `format(''{0}'', vars.DEPLOY_ON_PUSH)` forces the string comparison\nthe condition was always asking for; null becomes '''', which is not in the\nfalsey list, so an unset variable deploys. The comment says why, because the\nobvious \"simplification\" is to take it back out.\n\nThe diagnostic job stays for this one run with the bare comparison kept\nbeside the fixed one: the run should show kill-switch-formatted passing and\nkill-switch-bare not, which demonstrates the mechanism rather than asserting\nit. It comes out once a deploy has actually happened.","tree":{"sha":"2f8b2f91dbef1088ecbd0660168c3b25c27c5e91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/trees/2f8b2f91dbef1088ecbd0660168c3b25c27c5e91"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/commits/a1114ca537deb657441409de22c3fab606c3d5f6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commit/a1114ca537deb657441409de22c3fab606c3d5f6","node_id":"C_kwDOUWBCP9oAKGExMTE0Y2E1MzdkZWI2NTc0NDE0MDlkZTIyYzNmYWI2MDZjM2Q1ZjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commit/91429eb3de2bd0053cde3b2122edc6e101cc6058","sha":"91429eb3de2bd0053cde3b2122edc6e101cc6058","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/91429eb3de2bd0053cde3b2122edc6e101cc6058"}],"sha":"a1114ca537deb657441409de22c3fab606c3d5f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/a1114ca537deb657441409de22c3fab606c3d5f6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/91429eb3de2bd0053cde3b2122edc6e101cc6058/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T20:44:20Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T20:44:20Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"message":"ci: make the deploy condition say which clause is false\n\nTwo pushes to main with every suite green did not deploy, and a skipped job\nreports no reason — GitHub shows \"skipped\", zero steps, nothing else. The\nstep summary already proves the inputs are right (event push, ref\nrefs/heads/main, DEPLOY_ON_PUSH unset), so the fault is in how the condition\ncomposes, and reading it has now twice failed to find it.\n\nThis evaluates each clause separately through the same expression engine and\nprints which ones pass. Shared runners, no access to the box, and it is\ndeleted once the answer is in.","tree":{"sha":"d9bab0693f190f7c60832f80b3d50f172278276a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/trees/d9bab0693f190f7c60832f80b3d50f172278276a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/commits/91429eb3de2bd0053cde3b2122edc6e101cc6058","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commit/91429eb3de2bd0053cde3b2122edc6e101cc6058","node_id":"C_kwDOUWBCP9oAKDkxNDI5ZWIzZGUyYmQwMDUzY2RlM2IyMTIyZWRjNmUxMDFjYzYwNTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commit/a4c9df81034a5ed3bb744329bb57adbdc46e17f0","sha":"a4c9df81034a5ed3bb744329bb57adbdc46e17f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/a4c9df81034a5ed3bb744329bb57adbdc46e17f0"}],"sha":"91429eb3de2bd0053cde3b2122edc6e101cc6058","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/91429eb3de2bd0053cde3b2122edc6e101cc6058"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/a4c9df81034a5ed3bb744329bb57adbdc46e17f0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T20:34:03Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T20:34:03Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"message":"ci: say why a deploy did not happen, and stop asking contains() to decide\n\nThe previous commit was supposed to make a push to main deploy. It did not:\nrun 34159100424 was the right commit, on main, by push, with every CI job\ngreen — and the deploy job evaluated its `if:` to false and reported\n\"skipped\" with zero steps and no reason. A skipped job explains nothing, so\ndiagnosing it was guesswork.\n\nTwo changes, one for each half of that.\n\nPLAIN EQUALITY INSTEAD OF contains(fromJSON(...)). The kill switch was\n`!contains(fromJSON(''[\"false\",\"0\",\"no\",\"off\"]''), vars.DEPLOY_ON_PUSH)` with\nthe variable unset. That reads correctly and I could not fault it on paper,\nwhich is the problem: a condition nobody can evaluate by reading it is a\ncondition that fails silently. Four `!=` comparisons do the same job with\nnothing to be subtle about.\n\nAND A STEP THAT SAYS WHAT THE DECISION WAS. `ci-ok` always runs, so it now\nwrites the event, the ref and the kill switch into the job summary along with\nwhether a deploy should follow. If the next push still does not deploy, the\nrun itself says which input was wrong instead of leaving it to be inferred\nfrom an empty job.\n\nNothing about the gate is relaxed: CI must still pass, the ref must still be\nmain, the preflight still refuses an unhealthy box, and a failed health gate\nstill rolls back.","tree":{"sha":"5827e7ebc918adcb6a291abc99a3a1a99e885b38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/trees/5827e7ebc918adcb6a291abc99a3a1a99e885b38"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/commits/a4c9df81034a5ed3bb744329bb57adbdc46e17f0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commit/a4c9df81034a5ed3bb744329bb57adbdc46e17f0","node_id":"C_kwDOUWBCP9oAKGE0YzlkZjgxMDM0YTVlZDNiYjc0NDMyOWJiNTdhZGJkYzQ2ZTE3ZjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commit/6d63700fc43ccfedce9b4d5f6a19fc455e58f5da","sha":"6d63700fc43ccfedce9b4d5f6a19fc455e58f5da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/6d63700fc43ccfedce9b4d5f6a19fc455e58f5da"}],"sha":"a4c9df81034a5ed3bb744329bb57adbdc46e17f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/a4c9df81034a5ed3bb744329bb57adbdc46e17f0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/6d63700fc43ccfedce9b4d5f6a19fc455e58f5da/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T20:26:21Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T20:26:21Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"message":"fix(voice): the thicker waveform bars did not fit a phone\n\ndp-bugfix/l-6 thickened the trace from 2px bars to 3px (and 3px to 6px above\nmd), which is the point of the change and reads much better. The mobile GAP\nwas left at 2px, and the geometry it was chosen for no longer held:\n\n  48 bars x 3px + 47 gaps x 2px = 238px  in a ~228px box on a 375px phone\n\nThe trace is `justify-center` inside `overflow-hidden`, so it clips at BOTH\nends. Ten pixels of overflow means a live meter that drops the newest bars —\nthe sound you are making right now — which is precisely the failure the\ncomponent''s own comment says centring must never cause. Above md it was fine\n(48x6 + 47x3 = 429px in 620px).\n\nThicker bars are what was asked for, so the gap gives way: 1px on mobile,\n191px, comfortably inside the box. Desktop is untouched.\n\nTHE TEST DID NOT CATCH IT, AND COULD NOT HAVE. It asserted the literals\n`w-[2px]` / `md:w-[3px]` — and worse, its bar-finder matched on `w-[2px]`\ntoo, so thickening the bars did not fail one assertion about width, it failed\nfive unrelated assertions with \"expected [] to have length 1\", which says\nnothing about what changed. Those five were failing on the branch itself.\n\nRewritten to pin the property the comment actually claims: the finder matches\nwhat a bar IS (a fixed-width, rounded, height-animated span), the width test\nasserts base < md rather than two pixel values, and a new test COMPUTES the\ntrace width from LEVEL_BARS and the real classes and asserts it fits both\nboxes. Verified to fail on the 2px gap with \"expected 238 to be less than or\nequal to 228\" and pass on 1px.\n\n1,791 frontend tests pass.","tree":{"sha":"087da0c89a14739d42a9c5313316a3ec741c75a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/trees/087da0c89a14739d42a9c5313316a3ec741c75a5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/commits/6d63700fc43ccfedce9b4d5f6a19fc455e58f5da","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/use