rs_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commit/b12b4c1755e05c78560f1aba628c052f4960106e","node_id":"C_kwDOUWBCP9oAKGIxMmI0YzE3NTVlMDVjNzg1NjBmMWFiYTYyOGMwNTJmNDk2MDEwNmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commit/f617545a7339af2b73b21259da116404587e6908","sha":"f617545a7339af2b73b21259da116404587e6908","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/f617545a7339af2b73b21259da116404587e6908"}],"sha":"b12b4c1755e05c78560f1aba628c052f4960106e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/b12b4c1755e05c78560f1aba628c052f4960106e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/80d8a6d3f3c916b8c71238c89e03c77b2373d73e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T19:34:57Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T19:34:57Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"message":"feat(llm): a long answer is many calls, stitched — up to 1,000,000 output tokens\n\nThe main model''s window is 1,000,000 tokens IN. Out, one completion is capped\nat a few thousand, and nothing continued past it: `llm.stream_chat_events`\nopened one stream and returned when it closed. A cut-off answer just stopped,\nand Deep Research apologised for it — \"ask about one section for the rest\".\n\n1M output is not a number to raise anywhere. At the 46 tokens/second this\nhardware actually decodes, a million tokens is about six hours, and\nGEN_WALL_CLOCK_S bounds any SINGLE call at roughly 190,000. So it is a\nsequence of bounded calls that must be stitched into one text, which is what\nthis adds.\n\nTHE SIGNAL THAT WAS MISSING. `finish_reason` had no handling in llm.py at\nall — the streaming loop read `choices[0].delta` and never looked at\n`choices[0].finish_reason`. Every engine downstream had to guess: OCR guessed\nwith a non-streaming read, Deep Research guessed by reconstructing the ceiling\nand comparing token counts, and its own docstring named the fix. It is now a\nContextVar alongside `_usage`, cleared before every call and set from every\ngeneration path, and our own guards report themselves distinctly — a\nwall-clock kill is not \"length\" and must not be resumed.\n\nWHAT THE LOOP HAD TO GET RIGHT, none of which is the loop:\n\n- The prompt cannot grow with the text, or segment 50 is a 400,000-token\n  prefill. Each continuation sees a fixed TAIL verbatim plus an OUTLINE of the\n  headings already written — which is what stops it re-covering ground it can\n  no longer see.\n- Models repeat the seam. `_strip_overlap` removes a re-emitted opening by\n  matching what we just showed them.\n- Models do not resume mid-word. Measured against the real model, two of four\n  seams came out jammed (\"narrowthe\", \"50-100candidates\"); strengthening the\n  instruction did not fix it, because the model is not doing anything\n  unreasonable. So the trailing partial word of a continuable segment is never\n  emitted: the text is cut back to a boundary and the model rewrites that word.\n  Four of four seams clean afterwards, zero duplicated sentences.\n- A loop that cannot stop is worse than a short answer, and at six hours a\n  million tokens an unattended one is expensive. It stops on: the model saying\n  it is done, the budget, a deadline, no measurable progress twice running, a\n  segment that repeats text already written, and a hard segment count. Every\n  reason is recorded, and only \"complete\" means the model decided.\n\nA CEILING IS A CAPABILITY, NOT A DEFAULT. Continuing every truncated Fast\nanswer to a million tokens would spend six hours of the only GPU here on a\npassing question, so the budget rises with the effort the person chose: Fast\ngets one call and streams byte-for-byte as it always did, and only `max`\nreaches the configured maximum. Continuation engages only where an answer was\nALREADY being cut off, so the cost lands exactly where the bug was.\n\nVerified against the live model, not a fake: 5 segments, 9,637 characters,\n2,000 tokens at 69 tok/s, clean seams. Given a 40,000-token budget it wrote\n2,011 and stopped at \"complete\" — the budget is a ceiling, not a target.\n\nThree bugs found by testing rather than after shipping: a budget that stopped\napplying whenever the server reported no usage; `output_tokens` reported as\nNone for every run because `reset_usage()` clears to None rather than zero;\nand a stale finish_reason continuing a call that had reported nothing, which\na real test caught by stubbing the generator.\n\n2,909 backend and 1,766 frontend tests pass.","tree":{"sha":"262f7c051b729f2d22e7f987475cdb83625e0ea0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/trees/262f7c051b729f2d22e7f987475cdb83625e0ea0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/commits/80d8a6d3f3c916b8c71238c89e03c77b2373d73e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"h