-Chabot/commits/6b4ffc9cf99aba216dad22d776dc470e9af33999"}],"sha":"d6dfa6d35507664ab25151e798960e51c5787ff2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/d6dfa6d35507664ab25151e798960e51c5787ff2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/6b4ffc9cf99aba216dad22d776dc470e9af33999/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T04:23:41Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T04:23:41Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"message":"feat(voice): run speech on both nodes, and send each clip to the freest one\n\nOne engine SATURATES AT EIGHT concurrent clips. Measured before writing any\nof this: throughput climbs to ~123 seconds of audio per wall-second at eight\nand then stops dead — 120.9 at 8, 122.7 at 16, 123.9 at 32 — while latency\ngrows linearly behind it, 1.0s to 1.6s to 2.7s. Past eight, people are\nqueueing.\n\nSo the fleet can be more than one engine now. `scripts/asr.sh up --all-nodes`\nstarts a second copy on the head and the orchestrator routes to whichever has\nthe fewest requests IN FLIGHT. Measured, one engine against two:\n\n     8 concurrent   1.00s -> 0.91s   (117 -> 128 s of audio per wall-second)\n    16 concurrent   1.54s -> 1.05s   (123 -> 214)\n    32 concurrent   2.70s -> 1.46s   (122 -> 241)\n\nREPLICAS, NOT SHARDS, and that is the whole design decision. Splitting one\n1.7B model across two Sparks would put every layer''s activations on a 13 Gb/s\nRoCE link that the main model''s own tensor-parallel traffic already uses, to\nsave memory that was never short — the weights are 4.4 GB and either node\nholds them twice over. Two whole copies add throughput without one byte of\ncross-node chatter, and degrade to a single engine gracefully when a node\ngoes away.\n\nLEAST ACTIVE, not round robin: clips are not the same size, so counting\nrequests SENT would hand a two-minute dictation and the next clip to the same\nengine. An endpoint that fails is stood down for twenty seconds and the clip\nis retried elsewhere — never removed, so a rebooted node rejoins by itself.\nA clip the engine REFUSES is not retried anywhere, because another engine\nwould refuse it identically and more slowly.\n\nThe concurrency pool is now per ENGINE rather than per fleet. It exists to\nbound how hard any one node is pushed while the chat model shares it, so a\nsecond node should raise the ceiling without raising the pressure on either\nmachine.\n\nWHAT THE SECOND ENGINE COSTS, since it is not free: 8.3 GiB on the head, and\nthe chat model goes from -5.8% to -6.7% under dictation load. Below eight\nconcurrent dictations it buys nothing at all, because one engine was never\nbusy. Both numbers are in docs/VOICE.md so the choice can be revisited with\nevidence rather than by feel.\n\nAlso fixed a bug that made the fleet a fleet of one: `ssh` inside\n`while read ... done < <(each_node)` was consuming the loop''s own stdin — the\nLIST OF NODES — so the first worker command swallowed the rest and the deploy\nsilently touched one machine when two were asked for.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"491bb91239636ded53bdcfbf5cb6f8305fb3eaae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/trees/491bb91239636ded53bdcfbf5cb6f8305fb3eaae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/commits/6b4ffc9cf99aba216dad22d776dc470e9af33999","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commit/6b4ffc9cf99aba216dad22d776dc470e9af33999","node_id":"C_kwDOUWBCP9oAKDZiNGZmYzljZjk5YWJhMjE2ZGFkMjJkNzc2ZGM0NzBlOWFmMzM5OTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commit/4479a74b9331638def7457b75adfd2ef958edbae"