thor":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/74aa1cd128f6eed5024b0ceed1827c389de1fce4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T03:44:15Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T03:44:15Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"message":"fix(voice): the microphone was blocked by our own Permissions-Policy\n\nEvery user got \"Microphone access is blocked. Allow it for this site in your\nbrowser settings, then try again.\" — and no browser setting could have helped,\nbecause the block was ours.\n\n`Permissions-Policy: microphone=()` is an empty ALLOWLIST, not a default. It\ntells the browser that NO origin may use the microphone, so getUserMedia is\nrefused before the person is ever prompted. The refusal arrives as\nNotAllowedError, which is exactly what a user clicking Block produces, so the\ncomposer showed the one message that sends someone hunting through settings\nthat were never the problem.\n\nThe header was correct when it was written — its own comment says \"this app\nuses no camera/mic/geolocation\" — and it was still there when the composer\ngrew a microphone yesterday. `self` is the narrowest value that works: this\norigin may record, every embed and third party still may not, and camera and\ngeolocation stay denied outright.\n\nTwo tests pin it, and they read the real config rather than a mock, because\nthe failure being guarded is precisely that file drifting away from the\nfeature.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dd89ffdae8166e76b9fff698971cd049e0f5b6fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/trees/dd89ffdae8166e76b9fff698971cd049e0f5b6fc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/commits/74aa1cd128f6eed5024b0ceed1827c389de1fce4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commit/74aa1cd128f6eed5024b0ceed1827c389de1fce4","node_id":"C_kwDOUWBCP9oAKDc0YWExY2QxMjhmNmVlZDUwMjRiMGNlZWQxODI3YzM4OWRlMWZjZTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commit/24fae04ca787801f0288602833632631484d59e9","sha":"24fae04ca787801f0288602833632631484d59e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/24fae04ca787801f0288602833632631484d59e9"}],"sha":"74aa1cd128f6eed5024b0ceed1827c389de1fce4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/74aa1cd128f6eed5024b0ceed1827c389de1fce4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/24fae04ca787801f0288602833632631484d59e9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T03:10:15Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T03:10:15Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"message":"feat(voice): dictate into the composer, transcribed on our own hardware\n\nPress the microphone, speak, press stop; a second later the words are in the\nmessage box, joined to whatever was already typed. They are NOT sent — a\ntranscript is a draft, edited like anything else, and Send stays a separate\ndeliberate act.\n\nWHERE IT RUNS, AND WHY THERE. Qwen3-ASR-1.7B (Apache-2.0, pinned) on Spark 2,\nin its own Compose project so that starting or restarting speech never comes\nnear sf-local-ai-worker, which is the main model''s tensor-parallel rank 1.\nThe node was chosen by measurement, not preference: before this existed the\nhead held 76.1 GB of allocated GPU memory to the worker''s 30.0 GB. The engine\nfits on either; only one had room to spare. It holds ~6 GiB and stays warm.\n\nNO NEW RUNTIME. The vLLM already on the worker registers\nQwen3ASRForConditionalGeneration — and Whisper, and the realtime variant. The\none thing the published image lacks is the `vllm[audio]` decoder, so\ncompose/asr/Dockerfile adds three pip packages on top of the image the cluster\nalready runs. No source build, no version drift, nothing near the chat model.\n\nNO AUDIO CONVERSION, ANYWHERE. PyAV bundles ffmpeg, so the browser''s WebM/Opus\nis decoded by the engine itself. The same 15-second clip is 2.1 MB as WAV and\n145 KB as WebM/Opus and transcribes identically, so the orchestrator needs no\naudio library at all.\n\nMEASURED ON THIS HARDWARE (2026-09-04): 5s of audio in 0.48s, 15s in 1.04s,\n30s in 2.00s, 60s in 1.85s. Eight simultaneous 15-second clips finished in\n1.10s of wall clock. The cost that actually constrains this is the CHAT\nmodel''s: four dictations in flight cost it 5.8% of its decode throughput,\neight cost 10.1%. ASR_MAX_CONCURRENT=4 is that trade-off made explicitly — the\npool exists to protect the model people are waiting on, not the speech engine,\nwhich batches happily.\n\nTHE RECORDING IS NEVER WRITTEN DOWN. The audio is posted as the request BODY,\nnot as a multipart field: `UploadFile` would hand it to Starlette''s parser,\nwhich spools every part into a SpooledTemporaryFile whose 1 MB ceiling is a\nclass attribute — any dictation past about ninety seconds would have been\nwritten to the container''s disk before a line of our own code ran. It is held\nin memory for one call and dropped. `voice_transcriptions` (V19) records who,\nhow long, which language, how fast and whether it worked, and has no column\nthat could hold a word anybody said. Failed attempts are recorded too.\n\nTWO GATES, both server-side: a signed-in user (an open ASR endpoint on a\nshared GPU is a free denial-of-service against the chat model) and\nFeature.VOICE_INPUT, per member, on the admin Access page like every other\ntool. The composer hides the button when it is off; hiding is a courtesy and\nthe route answers 403 regardless.\n\nLANGUAGES, stated honestly: the model identifies 30, including Hindi, English,\nArabic, Chinese, Japanese and Korean, plus 22 Chinese dialects. It does NOT\nsupport Gujarati, Marathi, Bengali, Tamil, Telugu, Punjabi or Urdu, and\nnothing here claims it does. Auto-detection is the default — a person\ndictating should not have to declare a language first — and mixed-language\nspeech is transcribed as spoken, never translated.\n\nThe waveform is real: every bar is one RMS reading of the microphone, so a\nmuted input reads as flat rather than being animated over. The microphone is\nreleased on every path out of recording — stop, cancel, error, unmount —\nbecause a page that keeps the capture indicator lit has broken a promise about\nhardware.\n\nVoice analytics join the super-admin console (transcriptions, minutes,\nlatency percentiles, success rate, languages), Prometheus scrapes the engine\nas job vllm-asr, and scripts/asr.sh puts the whole thing up or down without\ntouching anything else. docs/VOICE.md is the operator''s copy.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3bff6692de633e2cc80634287a0c34c69c473da6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/trees/3bff6692de633e2cc80634287a0c34c69c473da6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/commits/24fae04ca787801f0288602833632631484d59e9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commit/24fae04ca787801f0288602833632631484d59e9","node_id":"C_kwDOUWBCP9oAKDI0ZmFlMDRjYTc4NzgwMWYwMjg4NjAyODMzNjMyNjMxNDg0ZDU5ZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commit/b370810e0bee710562756944c21fb613ad294946","sha":"b370810e0bee710562756944c21fb613ad294946","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/b370810e0bee710562756944c21fb613ad294946"}],"sh