ha":"d0cfb74e0a9a14c65837ebfcfca4be1feb6b8629","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/d0cfb74e0a9a14c65837ebfcfca4be1feb6b8629"}],"sha":"42e7397b7b43815fe45ddb109e5d38de6a86ff81","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/42e7397b7b43815fe45ddb109e5d38de6a86ff81"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/d0cfb74e0a9a14c65837ebfcfca4be1feb6b8629/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T20:21:48Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T20:21:48Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"message":"fix(db): reap abandoned sessions, and alert on connections before the wall\n\nPostgreSQL refused every new connection today — \"sorry, too many clients\nalready\" — including the pgAdmin tab whose owner was trying to investigate,\nand including psql as a superuser, because the reserved slots were gone too.\n\nCause: pgAdmin holds one backend per query tab and never releases it. It had\naccumulated 55 idle sessions against `max_connections=60`; the orchestrator''s\nown pool held 3 and the exporter 1. The app was one burst from failing — its\npool is allowed to grow to 16 and there was not one free slot.\n\n- `idle_session_timeout=10min` and `idle_in_transaction_session_timeout=15min`.\n  Measured before choosing: pgAdmin opens a BATCH on reconnect (34 within a\n  minute of a restart) and then parks them forever, so the window has to be\n  short enough that its footprint plus the app''s 16 clears 60. The\n  orchestrator is unaffected in practice — its pool already checks a\n  connection''s liveness before handing it out (db.py), so a reaped idle\n  connection is replaced silently instead of surfacing as a failed request.\n  Verified: a session that goes idle is now terminated; a new one connects.\n\n- The alert that should have caught this could never fire. It read\n  `sum(pg_stat_database_numbackends) > 70` against a deployment that runs\n  `-c max_connections=60` — a threshold ABOVE the ceiling, calibrated against\n  PostgreSQL''s default rather than this server''s setting. Both alerts are now\n  a percentage of `pg_settings_max_connections`, so the number can never\n  drift from the server''s own limit again: warning at 75%, critical at 90%\n  with the query that names the offending client in its description.\n\nLive now (ALTER SYSTEM + reload, no downtime) and in compose so a rebuilt\nstack inherits it. The 55 stale sessions predated the setting and were\nterminated by hand: PostgreSQL arms the idle timer when a session ENTERS\nidle, so sessions already parked there are never retro-armed by a reload.\nUtilisation went 100% (refusing) → 6.7%.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d729fbe4ab9593124be39572334bfe9dce652306","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/trees/d729fbe4ab9593124be39572334bfe9dce652306"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/commits/d0cfb74e0a9a14c65837ebfcfca4be1feb6b8629","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commit/d0cfb74e0a9a14c65837ebfcfca4be1feb6b8629","node_id":"C_kwDOUWBCP9oAKGQwY2ZiNzRlMGE5YTE0YzY1ODM3ZWJmY2ZjYTRiZTFmZWI2Yjg2Mjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commit/6066e52e1eea6a31d0356b4be9e981a8b0433a4a","sha":"6066e52e1eea6a31d0356b4be9e981a8b0433a4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/6066e52e1eea6a31d0356b4be9e981a8b0433a4a"}],"sha":"d0cfb74e0a9a14c65837ebfcfca4be1feb6b8629","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/d0cfb74e0a9a14c65837ebfcfca4be1feb6b8629"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/6066e52e1eea6a31d0356b4be9e981a8b0433a4a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T19:18:30Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T19:18:30Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"message":"feat(admin): rebuild the Members and Access pages as an enterprise settings UI\n\nThe admin area wore the chat surface''s clothes: a rounded bordered card with\nzebra striping around the roster, tinted pills repeated down every row, a\n30px search box beside a 26px filter, and the page''s one action stranded in\nthe header. Forty members read as forty objects in a box.\n\nMEMBERS\n- The table is flat: a quiet header rule, hairline separators, one whisper\n  of a hover. No card, no striping.\n- Geometry is deterministic. Columns declare widths, layout is table-fixed,\n  cells never wrap, and the table has a real minimum width — so a long email\n  truncates instead of moving the Role column on that one row, and a narrow\n  window scrolls sideways rather than squeezing names to \"Na…\" (both were\n  measured at 1024px, and both are now covered by tests).\n- 68px rows around a 40px avatar; identity is two aligned lines.\n- Role is a control, not a menu item buried next to \"Remove\": the value with\n  a chevron for anyone who may change it, opening the same dialog (and the\n  same 409 handling) as before. The ⋯ menu keeps its copy.\n- Status is a 6px dot and a word. Roles are tinted only where the\n  distinction earns attention; 90% of rows are a plain \"Member\".\n- Dates read as dates (\"Sep 1, 2026\") and last-active as elapsed time\n  (\"4 hours ago\"), with the precise timestamp on hover.\n- One toolbar strip: search + filters left, Invite member right, every\n  control 40px on the same radius, focus ring and hover.\n\nACCESS\n- One grid, not five flex rows: `minmax(0,1fr) auto` with the switch centred\n  in its own track. All five switches now share an exact X (measured: 1065px,\n  44x24 each) and keep it when a row grows a third line of helper text.\n- One shared Switch: 44x24, 20px thumb, role=switch + aria-checked +\n  aria-describedby, disabled semantics, 160ms transform.\n- A dangling dependency explains itself (\"Needs Salesforce, which is off.\")\n  in muted helper text rather than looking like an error.\n- Save is state-aware: quiet until something differs, spinner while saving,\n  re-seeded from the server''s answer so it goes quiet again.\n\nSHARED\n- New: controls.tsx (search/select/tabs/toolbar/buttons), Switch,\n  MemberRoleControl, AccessSettingRow + AccessSettingsCard.\n- Four derived admin tokens (separator, row hover, control, switch-off) —\n  no new hex except a genuine gap in the palette, --ts-ok, which the colour\n  audit now allowlists with its reason. The off-switch track came out of the\n  light-mode pass, where a white thumb vanished into #ececec.\n- Analytics and Invitations adopt the same controls, so the admin area is\n  one system. The layout column widens to 1180px and the sidebar rows share\n  one height and icon box.\n\nFunctionality is unchanged and was driven through the real UI: search and\nboth filters still query the server, the role dialog opens, the ⋯ menu keeps\nall seven items, tabs switch, dependencies gate, save persists. Verified at\n1600/1280/1024 in both themes.\n\n1,491 frontend tests (14 new), typecheck and lint clean, production build ok.\n`npm run lint` is wired to ESLint directly — `next lint` was removed in\nNext 16, so the script had been dead since that upgrade.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0af0703579857d698eb79630a54891727aeae892","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/trees/0af0703579857d698eb79630a54891727aeae892"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/commits/6066e52e1eea6a31d0356b4be9e981a8b0433a4a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/naman