r}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/namanjain221995","id":252194973,"login":"namanjain221995","node_id":"U_kgDODwgwnQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/commits/4ca0754a6402abf18f466e4a369ce32fdf32443b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T17:53:48Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T17:53:48Z","email":"naman.jain@techsarasolutions.com","name":"naman"},"message":"feat(admin): per-member tool access, workspace usage analytics, pending-only invites\n\nThree things the owner asked for after using the admin area (2026-09-03).\n\n1. THE BUG. The Members page''s \"Pending invites\" tab listed every invitation\n   ever sent — nine rows reading \"Accepted\" under a heading promising one\n   pending. The tab now asks the server for pending only; /admin/invitations\n   keeps the full history behind an All/Pending/Accepted/Expired/Revoked\n   filter, so re-inviting a dead invite still works.\n\n2. FEATURE ACCESS (V17). Admins can now decide WHICH TOOLS each person may\n   use — photos/files, web search, deep research, Salesforce, live\n   Salesforce — as a workspace default (Admin → Access) with a per-member\n   override (Members → ⋯ → Manage access). Deliberately separate from RBAC:\n   a capability is a property of the role (\"may administer\"), a feature is a\n   property of the person (\"may use\"). Dependencies cannot dangle (deep\n   research needs the web, live needs Salesforce), only keys someone set are\n   stored so a later default change still reaches everyone who never\n   overrode it, and a super admin always keeps everything so a workspace\n   cannot lock itself out. The client is never the gate: the composer hides\n   what is off and corrects sticky prefs (a stale Salesforce mode would\n   otherwise show a trust footer the server will not honour), /chat\n   re-resolves and DOWNGRADES with one status line rather than erroring\n   mid-conversation, and the upload routes refuse with 403 — that is the\n   door bytes actually arrive through. Both changes are audited.\n\n3. ANALYTICS. /admin is now the usage report it looked like it should be:\n   7D/1M/3M/6M/12M windows, totals, a daily message chart, which tools ran,\n   and a People tab with one row per member — including the members who used\n   nothing, which is usually why the page is open. Export downloads the same\n   table as CSV (audited, and proxied so the filename survives). Built from\n   messages.meta->>''route'', so the tool columns are what actually ran.\n\nSchema V17 is additive with defaults; a code rollback needs no schema change.\n2,253 orchestrator tests and 1,465 frontend tests pass; frontend builds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"45f61dffa1b7204423810895f146c1133dc21ab9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/trees/45f61dffa1b7204423810895f146c1133dc21ab9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jayeshpra/personal-LLM-Chabot/git/commits/4ca0754a6402abf18f466e4a369ce32fdf32443b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/252194973?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/namanjain221995/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.gith