"name":"bymaksym"},"message":"chore: release 1.0.0\n\nRelease-As: 1.0.0","tree":{"sha":"694a5d8e31e9a52b9aed9dc2e37ba1f5f739f6de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/git/trees/694a5d8e31e9a52b9aed9dc2e37ba1f5f739f6de"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/git/commits/1c095742e9e7ed5b09ef809986c8974b24df6c46","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/bymaksym/LoadLine/commit/1c095742e9e7ed5b09ef809986c8974b24df6c46","node_id":"C_kwDOUWYfmtoAKDFjMDk1NzQyZTllN2VkNWIwOWVmODA5OTg2Yzg5NzRiMjRkZjZjNDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/bymaksym/LoadLine/commit/2ebe2dc5beea0268a00ded58961825c2d6b9fe4d","sha":"2ebe2dc5beea0268a00ded58961825c2d6b9fe4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/commits/2ebe2dc5beea0268a00ded58961825c2d6b9fe4d"}],"sha":"1c095742e9e7ed5b09ef809986c8974b24df6c46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/commits/1c095742e9e7ed5b09ef809986c8974b24df6c46"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/commits/2ebe2dc5beea0268a00ded58961825c2d6b9fe4d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T10:52:30Z","email":"bymaksymdev@gmail.com","name":"bymaksym"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T11:00:45Z","email":"bymaksymdev@gmail.com","name":"bymaksym"},"message":"feat: a redesigned page, savings in the report''s unit, and CI that compares each PR with main\n\nThe page:\n- One header row: the mark, a chip naming the loaded build (it goes back to the files), Search\n  with Ctrl K, the language, density and theme. It wraps on a phone instead of cutting a button off.\n- A front page with the one required file and the three optional ones as a list. Over a report the\n  drop zones fold into one line: the raw-figures caveat and the files that would add detail.\n- The summary takes about 220 px: the effective bootstrap leads alone, with a bar against both\n  thresholds, and four figures lead to their tab. One \"worst\" badge, and only on a bad figure.\n- Tabs in two groups, sticky and opaque. \"How to read this tab\" is a toggle next to the title.\n- Signals and Criteria are dense tables; Measured, Project and Compare have real empty states.\n- A legend at the foot says where each kind of figure comes from: measured, derived, declared,\n  unknown.\n- New palette: fair is an ochre so it cannot be read as the shared orange; your code inside the\n  bootstrap is hatched grey, so teal only ever means \"this screen only\".\n- A figure and its unit are joined by a narrow no-break space on the page.\n- Printing gives every view of the build, each on its own page.\n- Spanish verdicts are Bien / Regular / Mal; the date of the answers follows the page''s language.\n\nSavings:\n- In a compressed report the saving of a signal, of all of them and of --what-if was printed in raw\n  bytes next to a gzip bootstrap (\"takes 302 kB off\" a 258 kB first load). It is now carried into\n  the report''s unit at the ratio the bootstrap compresses by, and marked with ≈.\n\nfix: --what-if is answered in the summary and json formats, and the others say so on stderr\nfix: the signal count is the same in the summary, the tab and the filter\nfix: \"Fixing both would take…\" instead of \"Acting on all 2 would take…\"\ndocs: the CI recipe keeps main''s snapshot as an artifact and compares each pull request with it","tree":{"sha":"694a5d8e31e9a52b9aed9dc2e37ba1f5f739f6de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/git/trees/694a5d8e31e9a52b9aed9dc2e37ba1f5f739f6de"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/git/commits/2ebe2dc5beea0268a00ded58961825c2d6b9fe4d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/bymaksym/LoadLine/commit/2ebe2dc5beea0268a00ded58961825c2d6b9fe4d","node_id":"C_kwDOUWYfmtoAKDJlYmUyZGM1YmVlYTAyNjhhMDBkZWQ1ODk2MTgyNWMyZDZiOWZlNGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/bymaksym/LoadLine/commit/5e92dc4ec8633df3890319edacd45e9a04f0bb68","sha":"5e92dc4ec8633df3890319edacd45e9a04f0bb68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/commits/5e92dc4ec8633df3890319edacd45e9a04f0bb68"}],"sha":"2ebe2dc5beea0268a00ded58961825c2d6b9fe4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/commits/2ebe2dc5beea0268a00ded58961825c2d6b9fe4d"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/commits/5e92dc4ec8633df3890319edacd45e9a04f0bb68/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T12:05:28Z","email":"bymaksymdev@gmail.com","name":"bymaksym"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T12:05:28Z","email":"bymaksymdev@gmail.com","name":"bymaksym"},"message":"feat: a map of the bundle, --html with the build inside, and what moved since the last run\n\nThe command:\n- `--html <file>` writes the page with this build already inside it; `--open` opens it.\n- Each run is remembered in node_modules/.cache/loadline and the next one says what moved,\n  without a `--baseline`; `--no-cache` turns it off.\n- Pointed at the root of a build it finds the metafile itself, including browser-stats.json,\n  which is what Angular 22.2 writes (22.1 wrote stats.json).\n- A stats.json without `inputs` is rejected on entry instead of failing halfway through.\n\nThe page:\n- A Map tab: the bundle as a treemap, on Loadline''s own figures.\n- Duplicated packages are followed to whatever brings each copy, and a pinned version is told\n  apart from one an override can align. A new signal for a bootstrap package that only one\n  file of shared code imports.\n- Font sizes and spacing go through tokens (`--fs-*`, `--space-N`, N eighths of a rem). No\n  size moved more than 1.2 px and no fixed margin more than 1.6 px; Stylelint refuses the rest.\n- On a narrow phone the header buttons stay on screen instead of scrolling the page sideways.\n- 26 column headers get `scope=\"col\"`; four translation keys nothing read are gone.\n\nTooling:\n- ESLint: regexp (three patterns that could backtrack on a large bundle are rewritten),\n  eslint-comments, vitest, baseline-js, angular-modern, typescript-eslint strict, unicorn 76,\n  and a typed config (strictTypeChecked) for the editor, the commit and CI.\n- `src/app/core` imports only itself, and APIs missing from Node 20.19 are refused in core and\n  cli, so `npx` keeps working on the floor `engines` promises.\n- Stylelint tokens, html-validate, cspell, jscpd, checks for unused translation keys and for\n  ESLint rules that are duplicated, deprecated or fight Prettier.\n- `pnpm run check` runs every check and prints a summary; CI runs the new ones.\n- Windows: knip through a wrapper, lint-staged within the command-line limit, secretlint over\n  the whole tree, fix-all in sequence, `.claude/` ignored everywhere.\n- Dependencies updated, Angular 22.2 among them.\n\nfix: reject a stats.json without inputs before the analysis starts\nfix: keep the header buttons on screen on a narrow phone\ndocs: name browser-stats.json as what Angular 22.2 writes","tree":{"sha":"01bf12feac1d58c6c1705065259e43e5a0e21815","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/git/trees/01bf12feac1d58c6c1705065259e43e5a0e21815"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/git/commits/5e92dc4ec8633df3890319edacd45e9a04f0bb68","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/bymaksym/LoadLine/commit/5e92dc4ec8633df3890319edacd45e9a04f0bb68","node_id":"C_kwDOUWYfmtoAKDVlOTJkYzRlYzg2MzNkZjM4OTAzMTllZGFjZDQ1ZTlhMDRmMGJiNjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/bymaksym/LoadLine/commit/64e235772e2ab1e1189c2fff55b58f1c6192da1d","sha":"64e235772e2ab1e1189c2fff55b58f1c6192da1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/commits/64e235772e2ab1e1189c2fff55b58f1c