mit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T11:51:08Z","email":"bymaksymdev@gmail.com","name":"bymaksym"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T11:51:08Z","email":"bymaksymdev@gmail.com","name":"bymaksym"},"message":"ci: publish without a stored token","tree":{"sha":"adf5b224889ff815370be65d3115034fba55f335","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/git/trees/adf5b224889ff815370be65d3115034fba55f335"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/git/commits/27d7b17089527bad3e3eab05f8b37f75b7876962","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/bymaksym/LoadLine/commit/27d7b17089527bad3e3eab05f8b37f75b7876962","node_id":"C_kwDOUWYfmtoAKDI3ZDdiMTcwODk1MjdiYWQzZTNlYWIwNWY4YjM3Zjc1Yjc4NzY5NjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/bymaksym/LoadLine/commit/ba2182424d82933722953283f506e8814566ce28","sha":"ba2182424d82933722953283f506e8814566ce28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/commits/ba2182424d82933722953283f506e8814566ce28"}],"sha":"27d7b17089527bad3e3eab05f8b37f75b7876962","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/commits/27d7b17089527bad3e3eab05f8b37f75b7876962"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/commits/ba2182424d82933722953283f506e8814566ce28/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T11:33:46Z","email":"bymaksymdev@gmail.com","name":"bymaksym"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T11:33:46Z","email":"bymaksymdev@gmail.com","name":"bymaksym"},"message":"fix: publish under a scope, which is the only name npm will take\n\nnpm refuses `loadline`: its typosquatting check rejects the name for being two\nletters away from `readline`. A 404 from the registry means nobody owns a name,\nnot that it can be had — that rule only runs at publish time, so the first\nattempt is where it is found.\n\nThe installed command does not change. `bin` names the executable independently\nof the package, so `loadline` is still what gets typed; only the install string\ngains the scope.","tree":{"sha":"167bb755ef5c64bee6f66ee1804aacd2515aa53c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/git/trees/167bb755ef5c64bee6f66ee1804aacd2515aa53c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/git/commits/ba2182424d82933722953283f506e8814566ce28","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/bymaksym/LoadLine/commit/ba2182424d82933722953283f506e8814566ce28","node_id":"C_kwDOUWYfmtoAKGJhMjE4MjQyNGQ4MjkzMzcyMjk1MzI4M2Y1MDZlODgxNDU2NmNlMjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/bymaksym/LoadLine/commit/d13c54bf62c47721f5276a7b594b7a2dedcc1318","sha":"d13c54bf62c47721f5276a7b594b7a2dedcc1318","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/commits/d13c54bf62c47721f5276a7b594b7a2dedcc1318"}],"sha":"ba2182424d82933722953283f506e8814566ce28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/commits/ba2182424d82933722953283f506e8814566ce28"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/commits/d13c54bf62c47721f5276a7b594b7a2dedcc1318/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T11:06:06Z","email":"bymaksymdev@gmail.com","name":"bymaksym"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T11:06:06Z","email":"bymaksymdev@gmail.com","name":"bymaksym"},"message":"chore: sound JSON reading, BEM as a rule, and a guarded dependency path\n\nThree strands that had in common that each of them was a convention nobody\ncould break by accident and everybody could break by hand.\n\nParsing. `JSON.parse` is typed `any`, and the habit was to annotate the result\n`: unknown` and assert the shape it was hoped to be, which moves the lie one\nline down rather than removing it. `core/json/json.utils.ts` holds the two\nshallow checks that make the assertion true instead of hopeful, and lock files,\nsource maps, audit output, stored criteria and the command''s own flags now go\nthrough them. It fixes real breakage: a source map with one non-string in\n`sources` used to throw and take everything that map knew with it, and\n`{\"vulnerabilities\": \"oops\"}` used to turn into four findings named 0 to 3.\n\nNaming. `selector-class-pattern` now enforces BEM rather than being switched\noff, with the classes renamed to match. The rule only holds for a class written\nout in full — an element written as `&__size` has no class in it for the pattern\nto look at — so that half stays a reading, and the comment on the rule says so\nand says what a test would have to walk to close it.\n\nDependencies. Dependabot grouped and monthly with majors left out, because a\npull request per package per week is how Dependabot gets muted; ncu''s three-day\ncooldown and its output format moved into `.ncurc.js`, where the policy is\nwritten once instead of twice; `deps:upgrade` runs the whole cycle — update,\ntransitive update, dedupe, fix, typecheck, test, self-analysis, audit — and\n`self:check` brings CI''s three readings of Loadline''s own build down to a local\ncommand. vitest returns to ^4 and joins the Angular-coupled list: `ng test` runs\nit through `@angular/build`, whose peer range said `^4.0.8` all along.\n\nSecrets. A deny-list in `.gitignore` for what should never reach the index, and\nsecretlint over the staged files as a real pre-commit gate — no `|| true` on\nthat one — plus the whole tree in CI.\n\nAlso: `--format summary` was implemented, working and named in no help text,\nwhich is the same as not shipping it. Documented, guarded by a test that reads\nthe `--format` line of `USAGE` itself, and used for the folder reading in\n`self:check`. And \"What to fix first\" paints each row with the severity of the\nsignal it points at, so a table of four equal-looking jobs reads as what it is.","tree":{"sha":"380187009e6e4b24641e729d5ee183def657a5ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/git/trees/380187009e6e4b24641e729d5ee183def657a5ca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/git/commits/d13c54bf62c47721f5276a7b594b7a2dedcc1318","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/bymaksym/LoadLine/commit/d13c54bf62c47721f5276a7b594b7a2dedcc1318","node_id":"C_kwDOUWYfmtoAKGQxM2M1NGJmNjJjNDc3MjFmNTI3NmE3YjU5NGI3YTJkZWRjYzEzMTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/bymaksym/LoadLine/commit/8c27f94144a86d6f16c4fbd2d9d0b9cb53d5faf2","sha":"8c27f94144a86d6f16c4fbd2d9d0b9cb53d5faf2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/commits/8c27f94144a86d6f16c4fbd2d9d0b9cb53d5faf2"}],"sha":"d13c54bf62c47721f5276a7b594b7a2dedcc1318","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/commits/d13c54bf62c47721f5276a7b594b7a2dedcc1318"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/commits/8c27f94144a86d6f16c4fbd2d9d0b9cb53d5faf2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T15:38:01Z","email":"bymaksymdev@gmail.com","name":"bymaksym"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T15:38:01Z","email":"bymaksymdev@gmail.com","name":"bymaksym"},"message":"feat: loadline, weight per screen for ES module builds\n\nWhat someone opening each screen of an app actually downloads, how much of that\neverybody else pays for too, and what is worth moving elsewhere.\n\nOne analysis behind two front ends: a self-contained HTML page that runs in the\nbrowser with nothing to install and nothing uploaded, and the same code as a\ncommand for CI. It reads an esbuild metafile or the build folder on its own,\nsince ES module chunks carry their own import graph.\n\nZero runtime dependencies, no install script, Node 20.19 and nothing else.\n\nPublished from a single commit: the working history before this point was local\nand is not carried over.","tree":{"sha":"b9176235786a2740b0b3c030d41e37305d1d8559","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/git/trees/b9176235786a2740b0b3c030d41e37305d1d8559"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/git/commits/8c27f94144a86d6f16c4fbd2d9d0b9cb53d5faf2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/bymaksym/LoadLine/commit/8c27f94144a86d6f16c4fbd2d9d0b9cb53d5faf2","node_id":"C_kwDOUWYfmtoAKDhjMjdmOTQxNDRhODZkNmYxNmM0ZmJkMmQ5ZDBiOWNiNTNkNWZhZjI","parents":[],"sha":"8c27f94144a86d6f16c4fbd2d9d0b9cb53d5faf2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/commits/8c27f94144a86d6f16c4fbd2d9d0b9cb53d5faf2"}],"requestUrl":"https://api.github.com/repos/bymaksym/LoadLine/commits?per_page=100&page=1&sha=b8aef45e1c021fa62a5d094f8b0795135ba799fd&since=2025-03-31T23%3A59%3A59.000Z&until=2026-10-08T15%3A44%3A21.329Z"}');
