arred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/doqin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/doqin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/doqin/tessera/commits/160e0920476459a79966300bd58ae59d54ae7d98/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T09:07:53Z","email":"personal.azalea@gmail.com","name":"Nguyen Tuan Khang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T09:07:53Z","email":"personal.azalea@gmail.com","name":"Nguyen Tuan Khang"},"message":"Set up AI Agent + SDD workflow, default LLM trial to Groq (free tier)\n\nInitial scaffolding for the UIT.SE.66 Setup AI Agent Assistant phase (D1):\n\n- .specify/constitution.md and CLAUDE.md: immutable project rules and\n  Claude Code instructions per the Spec-Driven Development workflow\n- specs/: Spec Kit structure for the 3 MFE modules, with full spec.md\n  for shell-app and chat-module\n- packages/shared-ui: trial Button component proving constitution\n  compliance (TS strict, ESLint/Prettier, Jest/RTL at 100% coverage)\n- tools/llm-trial: LLM connectivity trial script, revised to default to\n  Groq''s free-tier OpenAI-compatible API instead of paid OpenAI/Claude\n  endpoints, since this is an unfunded PoC; only reads keys from its own\n  .env.local (never inherited shell env vars) and refuses to call a paid\n  provider without an explicit --allow-paid flag\n- Root tooling: TypeScript, ESLint 9 flat config, Prettier, Jest,\n  GitHub Actions CI (lint -> typecheck -> test)\n- docs/reference/: Project Charter, D1-D3, and Tech Stack.xlsx, bumped\n  to v2.0 to record the Groq-as-default decision (Charter Document\n  History, Tech Stack AI Integration rows, D1-D3 provider mentions)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"743ef0e5f90fe087529e0c40563ef439d46fac78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/doqin/tessera/git/trees/743ef0e5f90fe087529e0c40563ef439d46fac78"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos