sues and prints their keys; d1481leavetime keeps old leave rows all-day/UTC.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"b6cc3e0bbc908225129779504e5db8b958d70499","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/b6cc3e0bbc908225129779504e5db8b958d70499"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/1bc107bb06e4844673a177030b556aeeaa56d738","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/1bc107bb06e4844673a177030b556aeeaa56d738","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDFiYzEwN2JiMDZlNDg0NDY3M2ExNzcwMzBiNTU2YWVlYWE1NmQ3Mzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/6173db388da9b98afaff81ef5c894b85c80ca523","sha":"6173db388da9b98afaff81ef5c894b85c80ca523","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/6173db388da9b98afaff81ef5c894b85c80ca523"}],"sha":"1bc107bb06e4844673a177030b556aeeaa56d738","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/1bc107bb06e4844673a177030b556aeeaa56d738"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/6173db388da9b98afaff81ef5c894b85c80ca523/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T13:41:03Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T13:41:23Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1493] A cross-project epic shows its whole picture: open as board, partial-group chip, roadmap parity, withheld-children note\n\nThe rollup carries `by_project` (readable descendants by project key) and\n`withheld` (descendants that exist but the actor may not read — counted, not\nwalked). A new `project` grouping axis lanes an all-projects board by project.\n`/e/KEY/board` opens an epic as a synthetic all-projects board — state\ncategories across, projects down, the epic itself excluded, no saved row — from\nthe epic page''s children header and its actions menu. A project board grouped\nby epic shows \"N more in TD\" on the group header, linking there, plus the\nwithheld count; the epic page and the roadmap hover card say the same. Group\nlabels the server resolves (assignee, team, epic, project) win over the\nclient''s, and a project bucket has no unset lane.\n\nProofs: `cross-project-epic-proof.mjs` (mocked, in test:browser) and\n`cross-project-epic-live.mjs` (against a running stack, seeds and deletes its\nown projects). The leak test now uses an issue under an epic, since a subtask\ncan no longer cross projects.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"7587f2c48ca90f7f892851a9d85915e3d43f7df9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/7587f2c48ca90f7f892851a9d85915e3d43f7df9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/6173db388da9b98afaff81ef5c894b85c80ca523","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/6173db388da9b98afaff81ef5c894b85c80ca523","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDYxNzNkYjM4OGRhOWI5OGFmYWZmODFlZjVjODk0Yjg1YzgwY2E1MjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/1373768e3fdce9d823e1f5cc5c46b1e243c930ba","sha":"1373768e3fdce9d823e1f5cc5c46b1e243c930ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/1373768e3fdce9d823e1f5cc5c46b1e243c930ba"}],"sha":"6173db388da9b98afaff81ef5c894b85c80ca523","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/6173db388da9b98afaff81ef5c894b85c80ca523"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/1373768e3fdce9d823e1f5cc5c46b1e243c930ba/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T13:18:07Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T13:18:07Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1492] A subtask lives where its parent lives\n\n`_resolve_parent` takes the child''s project and refuses a subtask whose parent\nissue is elsewhere; an issue''s epic may still sit in any project. Bulk move\ntakes an issue''s subtasks along (they inherit the issue''s row gate) and reports\na subtask selected without its issue as `subtask_follows_parent`; the parent\nsearch for issues is same-project; the checklist tick reads the child''s own\nworkflow. Migration d1492subtaskhome re-homes any cross-project subtask as a\ntop-level issue in its own project and prints the keys.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"3af6238e3525408cbf92d7406cdf682550e22330","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/3af6238e3525408cbf92d7406cdf682550e22330"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/1373768e3fdce9d823e1f5cc5c46b1e243c930ba","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/1373768e3fdce9d823e1f5cc5c46b1e243c930ba","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDEzNzM3NjhlM2ZkY2U5ZDgyM2UxZjVjYzVjNDZiMWUyNDNjOTMwYmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/78d61f052c9cc249b8704dcb471b8930138baf8f","sha":"78d61f052c9cc249b8704dcb471b8930138baf8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/78d61f052c9cc249b8704dcb471b8930138baf8f"}],"sha":"1373768e3fdce9d823e1f5cc5c46b1e243c930ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/1373768e3fdce9d823e1f5cc5c46b1e243c930ba"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/78d61f052c9cc249b8704dcb471b8930138baf8f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T13:11:59Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T13:11:59Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1491] A parent you cannot read is shown as hidden, not as absent, and cannot be replaced by accident\n\n`ItemRead.parent_hidden` / `epic_hidden` say when a ref was withheld (a boolean,\nnever the id). The rail renders a hidden parent as a muted row with no picker,\nthe header carries a matching tag, and a board grouped by epic files such rows\nunder \"Epic you cannot see\" (`HIDDEN_EPIC_BUCKET`) instead of \"No epic\".\n`update_item` refuses to replace or clear a parent the actor cannot read unless\nthey hold project.manage on the child''s project; restating the current parent\nis a no-op rather than a re-resolution.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"e136e7903dd4596834edceeeae1d10480b692b90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/e136e7903dd4596834edceeeae1d10480b692b90"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/78d61f052c9cc249b8704dcb471b8930138baf8f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/78d61f052c9cc249b8704dcb471b8930138baf8f","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDc4ZDYxZjA1MmM5Y2MyNDliODcwNGRjYjQ3MWI4OTMwMTM4YmFmOGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/e13a777dfb087b2bc20206905cd4cdd08a1c5a7c","sha":"e13a777dfb087b2bc20206905cd4cdd08a1c5a7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/e13a777dfb087b2bc20206905cd4cdd08a1c5a7c"}],"sha":"78d61f052c9cc249b8704dcb471b8930138baf8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/78d61f052c9cc249b8704dcb471b8930138baf8f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/e13a777dfb087b2bc20206905cd4cdd08a1c5a7c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T13:06:01Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T13:07:10Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1490] A typed key resolves in the project it names, not the project you are on\n\n`ItemLinkCreate.target_key` (KEY-123, aliases included) joins `target_id` and\n`target_number`; the dependency add-row submits it for a prefixed key and the\nbare number for the rest. `link_search` recognises a full key and leads with\nthat row ahead of the anchor project''s own item of the same number.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"74c0e1a19ce634fbbec727cd7fee3f3c60781be9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/74c0e1a19ce634fbbec727cd7fee3f3c60781be9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/e13a777dfb087b2bc20206905cd4cdd08a1c5a7c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/e13a777dfb087b2bc20206905cd4cdd08a1c5a7c","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKGUxM2E3NzdkZmIwODdiMmJjMjAyMDY5MDVjZDRjZGQwOGExYzVhN2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/90fb65ed1bd7f596c7e9f9807c1068ce72691fa4","sha":"90fb65ed1bd7f596c7e9f9807c1068ce72691fa4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/90fb65ed1bd7f596c7e9f9807c1068ce72691fa4"}],"sha":"e13a777dfb087b2bc20206905cd4cdd08a1c5a7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/e13a777dfb087b2bc20206905cd4cdd08a1c5a7c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/90fb65ed1bd7f596c7e9f9807c1068ce72691fa4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T17:20:26Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T17:20:26Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1481] Leave keeps its hours, and a team steward records leave for their members\n\nA leave period is still inclusive calendar days in the subject''s own calendar,\nand now carries an optional wall-clock time at either end (null = the whole day\nat that end) plus the IANA zone those are read in, resolved once at creation:\nthe request''s, else the subject''s profile zone, else the actor''s, else UTC. So\n\"12:00 on the 30th until 16:00 on the 3rd\", \"Monday 16:00 until Wednesday\" and\na plain all-day span are all one form, with All day on by default. Team\nholidays stay whole days (the NON_WORKING_DAYS socket hands out dates).\n\n`service.current(now)` judges each row in its own zone, so a 16:00 start is\naway at 16:30 local and not at 11:00; the calendar carries the times and the\ntimesheet annotation splits a timed span per day so the boundary cells say\n\"from 12:00\" / \"until 16:00\". The sockets stay date-granular.\n\nThe steward permission (`may_manage_user`) had no surface: a Team leave profile\nsection now lists the teams the reader owns or manages (`teams.stewarded_teams`,\n`GET /leave/teams`), the team''s members and their leave (`GET /leave/teams/{id}`),\nand aims the same form at a member. `GET /leave/users/{id}` for the manage view.\n\nProof: web/scripts/leave-hours-proof.mjs (20 checks against the dev stack).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"11c3bb6b1be71f42dffa02671116ceb9efe416f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/11c3bb6b1be71f42dffa02671116ceb9efe416f8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/90fb65ed1bd7f596c7e9f9807c1068ce72691fa4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/90fb65ed1bd7f596c7e9f9807c1068ce72691fa4","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDkwZmI2NWVkMWJkN2Y1OTZjN2U5Zjk4MDdjMTA2OGNlNzI2OTFmYTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/9dbcae63c2049a03d4645108fdb69288525f7be0","sha":"9dbcae63c2049a03d4645108fdb69288525f7be0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/9dbcae63c2049a03d4645108fdb69288525f7be0"}],"sha":"90fb65ed1bd7f596c7e9f9807c1068ce72691fa4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/90fb65ed1bd7f596c7e9f9807c1068ce72691fa4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/9dbcae63c2049a03d4645108fdb69288525f7be0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T13:01:29Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T13:01:29Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1480] The login proof waits for the TOTP response to render before closing the local form\n\nThe checks run for the v0.49.3 candidate (GitHub 36424425872) failed at browser-login.mjs:56:\nafter the mocked TOTP submit the proof waited only for the mock to RECEIVE the request, then\npressed \"Close local account sign-in\" while the runner was still handling the 401 response,\nand the click was swallowed. It now waits for the refusal text the response produces before\npressing Close. No product change; the proof raced the page, as the canvas Delete and the\ncolumns batch proofs did before it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"7d7304e4d094b96a46c1b2fddd321cde21f28503","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/7d7304e4d094b96a46c1b2fddd321cde21f28503"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/9dbcae63c2049a03d4645108fdb69288525f7be0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/9dbcae63c2049a03d4645108fdb69288525f7be0","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDlkYmNhZTYzYzIwNDlhMDNkNDY0NTEwOGZkYjY5Mjg4NTI1ZjdiZTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/a4a468c1c97c630ebc5fb422bd793062f7375851","sha":"a4a468c1c97c630ebc5fb422bd793062f7375851","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/a4a468c1c97c630ebc5fb422bd793062f7375851"}],"sha":"9dbcae63c2049a03d4645108fdb69288525f7be0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/9dbcae63c2049a03d4645108fdb69288525f7be0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/a4a468c1c97c630ebc5fb422bd793062f7375851/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T12:47:34Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T12:47:34Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1479] Release notes range from the last published release, not the last tag\n\nThe v0.49.2 notes said \"2 changes\" for a 137-issue release: previous_tag() took v0.49.1,\nwhose publish run had failed before any release existed, so the range collapsed to the\nlast two commits. release_notes.py now walks back through the tags until the host reports\na release for one (previous_published_tag), falling back to the plain previous tag when\nthere is no host token or the host cannot be asked, so a wiki-only run keeps working and\nnotes are never blocked on the lookup. --from still overrides. The v0.49.2 body on GitHub\nand the wiki page were regenerated by hand over v0.48.0..v0.49.2.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"3e22920dc8fafa358f56992b731bad13c6bbf01b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/3e22920dc8fafa358f56992b731bad13c6bbf01b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/a4a468c1c97c630ebc5fb422bd793062f7375851","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/a4a468c1c97c630ebc5fb422bd793062f7375851","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKGE0YTQ2OGMxYzk3YzYzMGViYzVmYjQyMmJkNzkzMDYyZjczNzU4NTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/207b393d1b851db8bc7bceee5de64a1d5e32ae5b","sha":"207b393d1b851db8bc7bceee5de64a1d5e32ae5b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/207b393d1b851db8bc7bceee5de64a1d5e32ae5b"}],"sha":"a4a468c1c97c630ebc5fb422bd793062f7375851","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/a4a468c1c97c630ebc5fb422bd793062f7375851"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/207b393d1b851db8bc7bceee5de64a1d5e32ae5b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T11:58:29Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T12:06:47Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1478] An existing comment can become a resolvable thread after the fact\n\nGitHub #35: `is_thread` was decided at creation only, so a comment that\nturned out to need an answer could not be made resolvable — the author had\nto delete it and post it again as a thread, losing its history.\n\n`CommentUpdate.is_thread: bool | None` (None = unchanged). The rule lives in\nthreads.convert_thread, under the same author-or-manager gate as a body\nedit: `true` turns a TOP-LEVEL comment into an unresolved thread — a reply\nis refused with the reason (a thread is its root); `false` turns a thread\nback into a plain comment only while it is unresolved and nobody has\nanswered, else refused with the reason (a resolved thread until reopened, a\nthread with N replies), and an inline annotation is refused outright (it is\na thread by nature). The flip takes the thread-parent lock like every\nlifecycle write, so it serializes with the workflow''s resolved-threads\nguard, and the partial unresolved-threads index sees it at once.\n\nEvents: the conversion is recorded on the comment''s UPDATED event as\n`{\"field\": \"is_thread\", \"from\": false, \"to\": true}` — the same shape\nset_resolved uses for `resolved` — so automations and the audit ledger see\na thread start on this row. Not a second CREATED: that would re-notify\nevery watcher about a comment they already read. The response now carries\na real `can_resolve` (resolve_reach on the parent), so the row redraws with\nits resolve controls from the PATCH itself.\n\nUI: \"Start thread from this comment\" beside Edit on an ordinary top-level\ncomment''s hover actions (author or project manager); one PATCH\n{is_thread: true}, then the comment entity is invalidated and the card\nredraws as an unresolved thread — chip, left rule, Resolve — with no\nreload; a refusal shows on the comment. A thread and a reply offer nothing.\nMCP: `update_comment {is_thread}` does the same through the same seam.\n\nTests: tests/test_comment_thread_conversion.py (5) — conversion makes the\nguard, the unresolved feed and the event see a thread and it resolves like\none (and repeating it records nothing); a reply never converts; converting\nback needs an unresolved, unanswered thread (refused once replied, once\nresolved until reopened, and on an inline annotation); only the author or a\nmanager; the MCP path with both refusals. Proof: browser-resolvable-threads\ngains three checks — the action is offered on an ordinary comment and not\non a thread or a reply; one PATCH with exactly {is_thread} redraws it as an\nunresolved thread with resolve controls and no reload; a refused conversion\nis shown on the comment and leaves it a comment. Run twice.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"e5c924a7008c578fa9c3f285d398fad5a1e5c62d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/e5c924a7008c578fa9c3f285d398fad5a1e5c62d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/207b393d1b851db8bc7bceee5de64a1d5e32ae5b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/207b393d1b851db8bc7bceee5de64a1d5e32ae5b","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDIwN2IzOTNkMWI4NTFkYjhiYzdiY2VlZTVkZTY0YTFkNWUzMmFlNWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/f68dd3dc610da0a6bc4994327cc9a276a7c55946","sha":"f68dd3dc610da0a6bc4994327cc9a276a7c55946","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/f68dd3dc610da0a6bc4994327cc9a276a7c55946"}],"sha":"207b393d1b851db8bc7bceee5de64a1d5e32ae5b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/207b393d1b851db8bc7bceee5de64a1d5e32ae5b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/f68dd3dc610da0a6bc4994327cc9a276a7c55946/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T11:53:19Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T12:06:47Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1477] A reply is edited and deleted by its author like a comment, and comments and replies can be edited and deleted over MCP\n\nGitHub #34: a reply had no Edit and no Delete. CommentReplies computed\n`canEdit` for the author and then rendered nothing with it, while\nPATCH/DELETE /comments/{id} already took a reply''s id. The owner confirmed\nreplies could not be edited or deleted from the UI at all.\n\nUI: the inline editor a comment used was private to CommentsThread; it is\nnow components/comments/CommentEditForm.tsx, shared by a comment and a\nreply, with the draft lifted to the caller so Escape and Cancel keep it and\nreopening shows it (the reply composer''s rule), and one Save. A new\nReplyActions (Edit + Delete with useConfirm) sits in the reply''s header for\nits author or a manager — CommentReplies takes `canManage`, which the issue\npage passes from project.manage and pages leave off (author only). A reply\nnow also shows \"(edited)\". Every surface refreshes through the comment\nentity, so the reply count and the thread''s state follow a delete.\n\nServer: deleting a THREAD ROOT that still has replies used to CASCADE\n(the FK, and the UI''s \"delete this comment and its N replies\" wording).\nThat was the wrong default for a discussion — deleting the first line took\nevery answer with it — so `delete_comment` now refuses with the reason\n(\"This comment has 2 replies; delete them first\"), after the permission\ngate so a stranger learns nothing. The FK cascade stays for\n`delete_for_parent`, where the whole parent is going. The issue and page\nUIs no longer offer that delete: pressing it explains instead of sending.\n`CommentUpdate.body` is optional (None = unchanged), so an audience-only\nPATCH need not restate the text. `threads.reply_count` counts what EXISTS,\nnot what one reader may see.\n\nMCP: comments/mcptools.py contributes `update_comment` {comment_id, body?,\nvisible_to_teams?} and `delete_comment` {comment_id}, kernel_enforced=False\nlike the item tools (they name no project, so a kernel require could only\nask for the atom globally); the service enforces author-or-manager.\n`is_thread` on update_comment lands with RADD-1478. docs/modules.md\nregenerated.\n\nTests: tests/test_comment_edit_delete.py (7) — author edits/deletes own\nreply keeping parent and audience, non-author refused, project Manager\nallowed, root-with-replies refused with the reason, stranger gets 403 not\nthe count, body-less PATCH, MCP update/delete for a comment and a reply.\ntest_comment_threads.py''s cascade assertion flipped to the refusal.\nProof: browser-issue-features.mjs gains eight checks — own reply offers\nEdit/Delete, a manager edits anyone''s, Edit opens on the text, Escape\ncloses with no request and keeps the draft, Save sends one PATCH and\nredraws \"(edited)\", Delete asks then the count follows, a root with\nreplies is refused before any request, a plain member sees no actions on\nanother person''s reply. Run twice.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"dd931236c059ff0f995fbf9593b0cdb74269814a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/dd931236c059ff0f995fbf9593b0cdb74269814a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/f68dd3dc610da0a6bc4994327cc9a276a7c55946","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/f68dd3dc610da0a6bc4994327cc9a276a7c55946","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKGY2OGRkM2RjNjEwZGEwYTZiYzQ5OTQzMjdjYzlhMjc2YTdjNTU5NDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/9e0f752384a74dad1bcae6c00844fe8095081d69","sha":"9e0f752384a74dad1bcae6c00844fe8095081d69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/9e0f752384a74dad1bcae6c00844fe8095081d69"}],"sha":"f68dd3dc610da0a6bc4994327cc9a276a7c55946","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/f68dd3dc610da0a6bc4994327cc9a276a7c55946"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/9e0f752384a74dad1bcae6c00844fe8095081d69/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T11:44:49Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T12:06:47Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1476] A done to-do keeps its text readable: a filled box and a quieter colour say it is done\n\nGitHub #32: a checked task''s text was struck through, which reads as \"deleted\"\nand made the words hard to read. The state was already carried by the box —\nRADD-1296 draws it filled with the accent and a white check — so the\nstrikethrough said nothing the box did not, at the cost of legibility.\n\nThe Milkdown rule in editor.css (editor and read mode share it) now sets\n`text-decoration: none`; the lighter react-markdown renderer in lib/markdown.tsx\ndrops its `line-through` the same way. The removed-diff rule keeps its\nstrikethrough: there it means \"taken out\", which is the right meaning.\n\nColour: the brief said fg-muted, but measured against the tokens it is 4.07:1\non the light page and 4.41:1 on a light surface — under the 4.5:1 body text\nneeds. fg-secondary (6.27:1 / 6.79:1 light, higher in dark) is the quieter\ncolour that still reads, so that is what a done item''s own paragraphs get. A\nstill-open nested subtask keeps the full colour: the selector already scoped\nto the item''s own paragraphs.\n\ntask-toggle-proof.mjs now measures rather than asserts the old look: no\nstrikethrough, the text quieter than an open item''s yet >= 4.5:1, the box''s\nfill equal to the browser-resolved --accent-fill (>= 3:1 against the page)\nwith a sized, opaque check mark, in both themes; the nested child unstruck\nat full colour. Run twice against a worktree server: 19/19 both times.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"2afedf5ab5626a08ee0330a523bc57093db5c761","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/2afedf5ab5626a08ee0330a523bc57093db5c761"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/9e0f752384a74dad1bcae6c00844fe8095081d69","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/9e0f752384a74dad1bcae6c00844fe8095081d69","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDllMGY3NTIzODRhNzRkYWQxYmNhZTZjMDA4NDRmZTgwOTUwODFkNjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/045c68aa505f92513be389643271d14cd96f92ab","sha":"045c68aa505f92513be389643271d14cd96f92ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/045c68aa505f92513be389643271d14cd96f92ab"}],"sha":"9e0f752384a74dad1bcae6c00844fe8095081d69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/9e0f752384a74dad1bcae6c00844fe8095081d69"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/045c68aa505f92513be389643271d14cd96f92ab/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T10:49:45Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T10:54:46Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1471] An existing issue can be given an epic, and a subtask a new parent, from the UI\n\nUntil now `parent_id` was settable only at creation (the New item modal) or by\nhand over the API; an issue filed before its epic existed stayed loose. Three\nsurfaces now change it, all through one shared search component\n(`web/src/components/items/ParentPicker.tsx`, extracted from the modal''s inline\npicker, which now uses it too):\n\n- RADD-1472 — the issue rail. `ParentField` (`PlanningFields.tsx`, mounted at the\n  head of the field rows in `IssueProperties.tsx`) is an \"Epic\" row on an issue\n  and a \"Parent issue\" row on a subtask: search-as-you-type over the required\n  kind, the current parent as a chip with Change and Clear, a PATCH of\n  `parent_id` (null to clear). A subtask has no Clear — the server refuses an\n  orphan — and the hint says so. Gated by the `parent` field grant like every\n  other row; a refusal is the server''s own sentence in the toast.\n- RADD-1473 — \"Add existing…\" on an epic''s children section\n  (`AddExistingChildren.tsx`): multi-pick over issues with no parent, ONE bulk\n  update for all of them, refused rows listed by key and reason and kept picked\n  for the retry. No counterpart on an issue''s subtask checklist: a subtask\n  cannot exist unparented, so there is nothing existing to add.\n- RADD-1474 — the bulk bar''s \"Epic…\" (\"Parent issue…\" for a subtask-only\n  selection; `BulkParentDialog.tsx`): the kind comes from the selected rows, a\n  mixed selection or an epic is disabled with the reason, issues get \"Clear\n  epic\". Server: `ItemBulkPatch.parent_id` (omitted = unchanged, null = clear)\n  forwarded through `bulk.py`''s passthrough, so `_resolve_parent`''s kind ladder\n  and the row gate apply per row and land in `skipped` with the reason.\n  `GET /items/link-search` gains `kind` and `unparented`, so the limit is spent\n  on pickable rows (the modal used to filter the kind client-side).\n- RADD-1475 — `web/scripts/browser-parent-management.mjs` (11 checks over a\n  stateful fixture API), registered in `test:browser`; `tests/test_bulk.py`\n  covers the batch: three issues set, a subtask handed an epic refused with the\n  kind reason, a subtask not clearable, an unreadable target refused —\n  FORBIDDEN when the target''s project is closed to the reader, INVALID_TARGET\n  (\"not found\") when only the row is hidden.\n\nFound on the way: `_resolve_parent` answers a parent in a project the actor\ncannot read at all with the project gate''s 403 — only a relation-hidden row\nreads as missing, which is narrower than RADD-1455''s wording suggests. And a\nproof''s `until` must await a helper''s promise before comparing it, or the\ncheck passes (or fails) vacuously; the first draft of this proof did exactly\nthat on the bulk bar''s disabled state.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"3dde171d0a5eabd194951bd6452c6eb5c163c721","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/3dde171d0a5eabd194951bd6452c6eb5c163c721"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/045c68aa505f92513be389643271d14cd96f92ab","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/045c68aa505f92513be389643271d14cd96f92ab","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDA0NWM2OGFhNTA1ZjkyNTEzYmUzODk2NDMyNzFkMTRjZDk2ZjkyYWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/64e3d908b22d6cc9f4ecdd757f67773ef1a132b5","sha":"64e3d908b22d6cc9f4ecdd757f67773ef1a132b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/64e3d908b22d6cc9f4ecdd757f67773ef1a132b5"}],"sha":"045c68aa505f92513be389643271d14cd96f92ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/045c68aa505f92513be389643271d14cd96f92ab"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/64e3d908b22d6cc9f4ecdd757f67773ef1a132b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:53:15Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:53:15Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1453] The upgrade section is headed by the version an operator comes FROM\n\n\"Upgrading from v0.48.0\" names the one version every reader of this section is on, and stays\ntrue whichever v0.49 patch the publish pipeline finally builds; naming the target moved twice in\none night (v0.49.0 and v0.49.1 both failed to publish). The d1329verdict downgrade message and the\nbuild-log wave headings say the same.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"a1a3545ee5fc975564b538c53dc0f48de873f418","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/a1a3545ee5fc975564b538c53dc0f48de873f418"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/64e3d908b22d6cc9f4ecdd757f67773ef1a132b5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/64e3d908b22d6cc9f4ecdd757f67773ef1a132b5","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDY0ZTNkOTA4YjIyZDZjYzlmNGVjZGQ3NTdmNjc3NzNlZjFhMTMyYjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/393ed8df1eef5ea195c00cbed24e181d2c052f3a","sha":"393ed8df1eef5ea195c00cbed24e181d2c052f3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/393ed8df1eef5ea195c00cbed24e181d2c052f3a"}],"sha":"64e3d908b22d6cc9f4ecdd757f67773ef1a132b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/64e3d908b22d6cc9f4ecdd757f67773ef1a132b5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/393ed8df1eef5ea195c00cbed24e181d2c052f3a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:53:15Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:53:15Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1470] The frontend CI job installs the server, so the four contract proofs can spawn its interpreter\n\nThe v0.49.1 publish run failed with `spawnSync server/.venv/bin/python ENOENT`: browser-audit-entity-links,\nbrowser-automation-editor, browser-vcs-settings and browser-second-review derive their fixtures from the\nbackend''s own contracts through the server interpreter, and the frontend job only ran `npm ci`. The job\nnow sets up uv and runs `uv sync --locked` in server/ first, as the backend job does; no database, since\n`radd.config` imports on defaults and the fixture scripts read registries only. This release is the\nfirst time the 31-script chain has run on GitHub since v0.48.0, which is why the gap never showed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"a10c39b9c7976af951090d58b406978d24a9530b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/a10c39b9c7976af951090d58b406978d24a9530b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/393ed8df1eef5ea195c00cbed24e181d2c052f3a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/eve