ttps://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/b67a6d96b35d9ae4c48ce875f3d2c828c2cfd707/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:40:39Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:40:39Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1453] The upgrade section names v0.49.1, the version that actually ships\n\nv0.49.0 was tagged and its publish run failed on a racing browser proof before any image or\nrelease existed, so the fixed tree ships as v0.49.1. The deploy doc''s operator table, the\nd1329verdict downgrade message and the two build-log wave headings now say so; the v0.49.0 tag\nstays as the record of the failed run rather than being moved, because versions are immutable.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"a598439cfd11fc5ea54ee9c8a200696f0acd3a99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/a598439cfd11fc5ea54ee9c8a200696f0acd3a99"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/b67a6d96b35d9ae4c48ce875f3d2c828c2cfd707","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/b67a6d96b35d9ae4c48ce875f3d2c828c2cfd707","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKGI2N2E2ZDk2YjM1ZDlhZTRjNDhjZTg3NWYzZDJjODI4YzJjZmQ3MDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/d5f0890218fc576317d84b5998d80169fc46601d","sha":"d5f0890218fc576317d84b5998d80169fc46601d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/d5f0890218fc576317d84b5998d80169fc46601d"}],"sha":"b67a6d96b35d9ae4c48ce875f3d2c828c2cfd707","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/b67a6d96b35d9ae4c48ce875f3d2c828c2cfd707"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/d5f0890218fc576317d84b5998d80169fc46601d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:40:39Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:40:39Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1466] The canvas proof waits for the node''s selection before pressing Delete\n\nThe v0.49.0 publish run (GitHub 36397597495) failed in browser-automation-canvas.mjs at \"delete\ncallback reaches graph\": the proof clicked a node and sent Delete in the same breath, and on the\nrunner the key arrived before React Flow had committed the selection, so nothing was deleted. The\nsame step passed here on every run because the local machine commits the selection within the\nclick''s own task. The proof now waits for the node''s React Flow wrapper to carry `selected` before\nsending Delete — the same class of race RADD-1466 already fixed in the columns proof.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"695eb0d1daad28bb264adb58492f56336d88bd86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/695eb0d1daad28bb264adb58492f56336d88bd86"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/d5f0890218fc576317d84b5998d80169fc46601d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/d5f0890218fc576317d84b5998d80169fc46601d","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKGQ1ZjA4OTAyMThmYzU3NjMxN2Q4NGI1OTk4ZDgwMTY5ZmM0NjYwMWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/532de8b5edca632c94b79cf4d5696a5c58658ddf","sha":"532de8b5edca632c94b79cf4d5696a5c58658ddf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/532de8b5edca632c94b79cf4d5696a5c58658ddf"}],"sha":"d5f0890218fc576317d84b5998d80169fc46601d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/d5f0890218fc576317d84b5998d80169fc46601d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/532de8b5edca632c94b79cf4d5696a5c58658ddf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:28:09Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:28:10Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1441] BUILD-LOG carries the bloat-audit and pre-release review waves, and a living doc drops its work date\n\nTwo waves had no entry in the one build narrative: the bloat audit (epic RADD-1402) and the\npre-release review (epic RADD-1449). Both are written the way the preamble narrated earlier waves.\ndocs/plugin-platform.md said \"Decided 2026-09-26\" — a work timestamp in a living page, which the\nrelease pre-flight refuses; it now names the wave and epic instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"88635593e272fa13cf3decd674363078126e7b34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/88635593e272fa13cf3decd674363078126e7b34"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/532de8b5edca632c94b79cf4d5696a5c58658ddf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/532de8b5edca632c94b79cf4d5696a5c58658ddf","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDUzMmRlOGI1ZWRjYTYzMmM5NGI3OWNmNGQ1Njk2YTVjNTg2NThkZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/ac91c48e4f255e065074e0794a868a30715c4252","sha":"ac91c48e4f255e065074e0794a868a30715c4252","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/ac91c48e4f255e065074e0794a868a30715c4252"}],"sha":"532de8b5edca632c94b79cf4d5696a5c58658ddf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/532de8b5edca632c94b79cf4d5696a5c58658ddf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/ac91c48e4f255e065074e0794a868a30715c4252/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T21:19:19Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:28:10Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1446] Every replayed secret is secretbox ciphertext at rest: AI keys, storage credentials, code-host tokens and webhook secrets, mail passwords, Alertmanager tokens and TOTP seeds\n\nRADD-1424 sealed the importer credentials, the SSO client secret and the LDAP\nbind password and left the rest of the inventory plaintext. This applies the\nsame seam (`radd.secretbox`: seal on write, decrypt at the one point of use,\nlazy adoption) to every remaining column that is replayed rather than hashed:\n\n- `ai_providers.api_key` — sealed in `registry.create_provider`/`update_provider`,\n  decrypted only by `registry.resolved_from_row` (so every client call and the\n  Test button send the key).\n- `storage_hosts.access_key` / `secret_key` — sealed in `hosts.create_host`/\n  `update_host`, decrypted only when `clients.S3Client` builds the Minio client.\n  Both are now write-only: `StorageHostRead` carries `has_access_key` instead of\n  the access key, and a blank `access_key` on update keeps the stored one like\n  `secret_key` already did (`keeps_secret`).\n- the connector kit''s `api_token` / `webhook_secret` (forgejo_connections,\n  github_connections, gitlab_connections) — sealed in `ConnectorStore.create_\n  connection`/`update_connection`/`seed_from_env`; the token is decrypted only in\n  each connector''s `api_headers`, the secret only in `resolve_for_payload`, where\n  the connector''s constant-time `authenticate` gets the plaintext.\n  `vcs/setup.py::require_distinct_secret` used to ask SQL for an equal secret,\n  which two ciphertexts under fresh nonces never are; it now compares the\n  decrypted values with `hmac.compare_digest`.\n- `mail_sources.secret` / `mail_senders.secret` — sealed by the Settings → Email\n  routes and env seeding; decrypted only by the ingest route (before\n  `verify_signature`), the IMAP login and `SmtpSender`. The mail routes keep\n  their documented update contract (omitted = unchanged, \"\" = clear): the dialogs\n  drop a blank secret, so no form round-trips one.\n- `alertmanager_receivers.token` — sealed on create/update/seed; decrypted only\n  in `receiver_for_token`, still compared constant-time. A row that will not\n  decrypt is logged and matches nothing, so one damaged receiver never takes\n  the webhook down.\n- `user_totp.secret` — sealed by `totp_setup`; `service.totp_secret(row)` is the\n  one decrypt, used by every code check and by the two enrolment routes that\n  show the seed once.\n\nLegacy rows: a plaintext value reads as-is, takes its encrypted form on the\nrow''s next save (adopted before the audit snapshot, so the adoption is not a\nrecorded change), and each owner''s startup hook sweeps the stragglers — ai,\nattachments, the three connectors, mailintake, alertmanager and auth each log\nand skip on `SecretBoxError`, so a boot without a usable backup key still comes\nup on plaintext. The audit ledger already listed every column in its owner''s\n`SECRET_FIELDS`, so diffs record \"changed\" and never a value.\n\nMigration `d1446secrets` (revises `d1457undeliverable`) widens the VARCHARs that\ncannot hold the sealed form of a value at their own limit to TEXT:\nstorage_hosts.access_key, the three connections'' api_token and webhook_secret,\nalertmanager_receivers.token and user_totp.secret. The values are not migrated\nthere: the key may not exist at migration time.\n\nTests: `tests/test_secrets_at_rest_remaining.py` — one per column that the raw\ncolumn is not the plaintext and the consumer still works (the AI client''s\nAuthorization header, the Minio client''s credentials, each host''s webhook\nresolution and API headers, the ingest route handing the decrypted secret to\nthe verifier, the IMAP login, the SMTP config, the Alertmanager webhook, TOTP\nconfirm and login), the duplicate-secret guard on ciphertext, the startup\nsweeps adopting committed legacy rows, and a boot with an unusable key logging\nand leaving them alone. Existing tests that read the raw columns now decrypt.\n\nFollow-up outside this change: `web/src/components/settings/storage/HostDialog.tsx`\nstill prefills its Access key field from the read shape, so it shows blank on\nedit (saving keeps the stored key); it should read `has_access_key` like the\nsecret key field does.\n\nThe storage host dialog follows the read shape: both credential fields start empty, show a set marker from has_access_key / has_secret_key, and an empty field on update keeps the stored value (the UI half the backend-only agent flagged).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"8018038357a2c4cabbb2ee0a280783b901f3e466","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/8018038357a2c4cabbb2ee0a280783b901f3e466"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/ac91c48e4f255e065074e0794a868a30715c4252","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/ac91c48e4f255e065074e0794a868a30715c4252","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKGFjOTFjNDhlNGYyNTVlMDY1MDc0ZTA3OTRhODY4YTMwNzE1YzQyNTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/92ac732c18e01e94d64c4905f8e603023efea5de","sha":"92ac732c18e01e94d64c4905f8e603023efea5de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/92ac732c18e01e94d64c4905f8e603023efea5de"}],"sha":"ac91c48e4f255e065074e0794a868a30715c4252","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/ac91c48e4f255e065074e0794a868a30715c4252"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/92ac732c18e01e94d64c4905f8e603023efea5de/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T20:50:46Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:28:10Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1469] The segmented choice''s idle options hold 4.5:1 in the light theme\n\nAn idle option was `text-fg-muted`, which measures 4.41:1 on the light surface (4.07:1 on\nthe page background) — under the 4.5:1 text floor. It is now `text-fg-secondary`: 6.79:1\nlight / 6.39:1 dark on the surface, 6.27 / 6.99 on the page background, computed from the\ntheme tokens (zinc-400 #525c69 light, #98a1ad dark). Hover keeps `text-fg`. The control is\nthe issue composer''s Comment / Start thread switch and the reply audience since RADD-1463,\nso every comment surface carries the change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"6a184598a65265099d68e25af3504d57e33310c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/6a184598a65265099d68e25af3504d57e33310c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/92ac732c18e01e94d64c4905f8e603023efea5de","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/92ac732c18e01e94d64c4905f8e603023efea5de","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDkyYWM3MzJjMThlMDFlOTRkNjRjNDkwNWY4ZTYwMzAyM2VmZWE1ZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/b1a49e6cf9455e88a498c2497d6b9abfbf049564","sha":"b1a49e6cf9455e88a498c2497d6b9abfbf049564","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/b1a49e6cf9455e88a498c2497d6b9abfbf049564"}],"sha":"92ac732c18e01e94d64c4905f8e603023efea5de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/92ac732c18e01e94d64c4905f8e603023efea5de"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/b1a49e6cf9455e88a498c2497d6b9abfbf049564/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T20:50:46Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:28:10Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1468] The VCS settings page tags its queries with the server''s entity types, so a realtime event reaches them\n\n`hostEntities` tagged the connection and repository queries `gitlabConnection` /\n`gitlabRepo`, a spelling that existed nowhere else: the server''s entity types are\n`gitlab_connection` / `gitlab_repo` (each connector''s types.py), the same file''s\n`historyEntities` already used them, and the realtime hub invalidates a plugin''s queries by\nits server entity type VERBATIM (web/src/lib/realtime.ts). The page refreshed itself after\nits own mutations through the same helper, so one admin never noticed; another admin''s\nedit, a webhook registering a repository or a connector seeding pushed an event no query\nwas listening for. The tags are now the server''s names.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"e0497056022f672debaf8010e45bd4586007130b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/e0497056022f672debaf8010e45bd4586007130b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/b1a49e6cf9455e88a498c2497d6b9abfbf049564","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/b1a49e6cf9455e88a498c2497d6b9abfbf049564","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKGIxYTQ5ZTZjZjk0NTVlODhhNDk4YzI0OTdkNmI5YWJmYmYwNDk1NjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/52bde3fbfb19102bc9a2b37db5effd88f4bf7833","sha":"52bde3fbfb19102bc9a2b37db5effd88f4bf7833","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/52bde3fbfb19102bc9a2b37db5effd88f4bf7833"}],"sha":"b1a49e6cf9455e88a498c2497d6b9abfbf049564","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/b1a49e6cf9455e88a498c2497d6b9abfbf049564"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/52bde3fbfb19102bc9a2b37db5effd88f4bf7833/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T18:37:48Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:28:10Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1461] A manifest without a remotes list still counts as synced, so a live-document surface never waits for a remote that is not coming\n\nThe loader marked the manifest synced only inside syncPluginRemotes, which returns before\nthat when the capabilities answer carries no `remotes` list. RADD-1461 made \"not yet synced\"\nmean \"every entity type is arriving\", so a capabilities answer shaped that way (the mocked\nbrowser-page-comments fixture, or an older server) left every page in the joining state\nand its body unrendered — the proof found it on the first full run after the merge. The\nPluginRemotes shell now hands the loader an empty list once the manifest has answered, so a\nmissing list means no remotes rather than no answer. A separate commit rather than a fold\ninto 5ed9fe68 because RADD-1467 changed the same lines in between.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"4801d4ffbec69334100ce001592cc406826e0d3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/4801d4ffbec69334100ce001592cc406826e0d3b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/52bde3fbfb19102bc9a2b37db5effd88f4bf7833","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/52bde3fbfb19102bc9a2b37db5effd88f4bf7833","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDUyYmRlM2ZiZmIxOTEwMmJjOWEyYjM3ZGI1ZWZmZDg4ZjRiZjc4MzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/387d5d69eafc142682ce77c8ae1b5d53ba5f701b","sha":"387d5d69eafc142682ce77c8ae1b5d53ba5f701b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/387d5d69eafc142682ce77c8ae1b5d53ba5f701b"}],"sha":"52bde3fbfb19102bc9a2b37db5effd88f4bf7833","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/52bde3fbfb19102bc9a2b37db5effd88f4bf7833"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/387d5d69eafc142682ce77c8ae1b5d53ba5f701b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T18:12:47Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:28:10Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1467] The wave''s magic literals are enums and named tunables: CI states, node kinds, cache tags, query keys and the keep-secret sentinel each have one spelling\n\nThe 2026-09-27 review found the plugin-isolation and bloat waves had left\nbehaviour named by bare strings and numbers in both halves of the tree. Each\none now names an enum member or a constant beside its siblings; behaviour is\nunchanged, and where a vocabulary was spelled in two places it now has one.\n\nBackend\n- vcs/types.py owns the CI vocabulary: CiOutcome (moved from triggers.py,\n  which re-exports it), CiState (the outcomes plus RUNNING/UNKNOWN),\n  CI_TERMINAL, CI_SUMMARY_ORDER and CiReportKind. service.set_ci_state, the\n  GitLab PIPELINE_STATES table, GitHub''s _CI_STATES and Forgejo''s router all\n  map onto it; forgejo/types.py''s duplicate CiState is gone. GitLab''s\n  deployment outcomes are GitlabDeploymentOutcome, and the trigger''s payload\n  schema enumerates that enum instead of restating the words.\n- The node-spec vocabulary (AutomationNodeKind, NodePort, NodeArity,\n  ITEM_SUBJECT) moves into kernel/specs.py beside AutomationNodeSpec, whose\n  own defaults named it as strings; automations/types.py re-exports it, so\n  every existing import holds, and radd.kernel / radd.sdk export it so a\n  plugin that contributes a node without depending on automations can spell\n  kind=\"action\" as the enum. Every AutomationNodeSpec in the tree (ai,\n  comments, mailintake, milestones, pages, participants, releases, scripts,\n  the built-ins, the verdicts) does. TYPE_TRIGGER_EVENT and\n  TYPE_GATE_ENTERED_STATE_CATEGORY join the type keys; templates use them.\n- executor: a finding''s mode is ValidationMode. router._seed_of returns\n  graph.ITEM_SUBJECT; builtin_actions records the created subject with it.\n- The notification channel is the kernel''s NotificationChannel (with its\n  inbox/email/silent properties), since NotificationKindSpec.default_channel\n  names a member; notify''s Channel is that enum.\n- AutomationCause gains a typed `source`; scripts stamps\n  RUN_KEY_CAUSE_SOURCE on a run key instead of spreading a dict.\n- dashboards/activity keys ACTIONS by ItemEvent/CommentEvent/WorklogEvent\n  (the three keys no module emits are dropped — item.transitioned,\n  comment.resolved, comment.reopened — a state change is item.updated with a\n  state diff, as the code already computed); timelogging joins weak_depends.\n  dashboards/limits.py holds the widget geometry bounds for both schemas.\n- approvals: UNKNOWN_APPROVER_LABEL keeps the \"?\" the event payload carries.\n- secretbox.KEEP_SECRET / keeps_secret() is the one keep-the-stored-secret\n  rule; attachments hosts, jira and confluence connections, the AI provider\n  registry (UNCHANGED_CREDENTIAL is gone) and scoped settings all use it.\n- mailintake: SignatureMethod is the detect() verdict; the AI fallback gates\n  on NONE_DETECTED rather than on the sentence.\n\nFrontend\n- The SDK owns the cache-tag vocabulary: Entity, EntityTag, CacheTag (an\n  Entity member or a plugin''s server entity type verbatim, RADD-1396),\n  EntityMeta and the entityMeta helpers live in plugin-sdk/src/cache.ts;\n  invalidateEntities, QuerySource.meta and CommandSource.meta are typed on it.\n  web/src/lib/cache.ts is deleted and its 55 importers read the SDK; every\n  plugin UI''s free-string shared tag is an Entity member, and pages'' private\n  Tag object is gone.\n- QueryKeyPrefix / capabilitiesQueryKey (plugin-sdk/src/query-keys.ts) replace\n  the [\"capabilities\"], [\"plugin-query\", …] and [\"plugin-commands\", …] arrays\n  the host, the loader and the SDK each spelled; the host''s queryKeys gains\n  pluginProcesses.\n- InstanceRole moves into the SDK types; the host and useIsInstanceAdmin read\n  it. CalloutKind (and its value type) live in host-registry beside the\n  Callout contract; the host Callout and all fifteen <Callout kind=\"…\"> sites\n  use it; toast() defaults to ToastKind.success.\n- automations UI: VERDICT_BLOCK_TYPE, MANUAL_TRIGGER, NodeKind.trigger and a\n  new TRIGGER_EVENT_TYPE replace their spellings in GraphEditor,\n  RuleTestPanel, RuleEditor, node-visuals and automation-nodes.\n- dashboards UI: WIDGET_LIMITS mirrors limits.py (a pytest holds the two\n  equal) and WidgetGrid clamps, drags and validates against it; its chrome\n  and grid-gap pixels are named too.\n- Loader tunables are *_MS constants: PLUGIN_LOAD_TIMEOUT_MS,\n  MANIFEST_POLL_MS, PLUGIN_LIST_POLL_MS, PLUGIN_PROCESSES_POLL_MS,\n  SOURCE_STALE_MS, DIRECTORY_STALE_MS (paged directory), CAPABILITIES_STALE_MS,\n  COMMENT_HIGHLIGHT_MS, LAND_POLL_MS, LAND_MAX_POLLS.\n- The SDK shim, docs/modules.md and the two node tests that evaluated\n  web/src/lib/cache.ts are regenerated/repointed; docs/plugin-ui.md and\n  modules-notes.md describe the shared vocabulary.\n\nLeft for the merge (files another agent owns): the free-string tags in\nautomations/ui/src/query-lifetime.ts:20 and slas/ui/src/{timers.ts:13,\nsettings/policies.ts:97}.\n\nAt merge time the three cache tags that lived in files another agent was editing (automations query-lifetime, slas timers and policies) took their Entity members, and the widget-body parser moved out of dashboards/router.py into dashboards/widget_bodies.py so the My Work service no longer imports a router helper.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"650587e6b752b64f8b7d2bffe40862691ac2f23b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/650587e6b752b64f8b7d2bffe40862691ac2f23b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/387d5d69eafc142682ce77c8ae1b5d53ba5f701b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/387d5d69eafc142682ce77c8ae1b5d53ba5f701b","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDM4N2Q1ZDY5ZWFmYzE0MjY4MmNlNzdjOGFlMWI1ZDUzYmE1ZjcwMWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/b32ed0ea0d03bc2eec88c7047d8a3afbc7196fd9","sha":"b32ed0ea0d03bc2eec88c7047d8a3afbc7196fd9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/b32ed0ea0d03bc2eec88c7047d8a3afbc7196fd9"}],"sha":"387d5d69eafc142682ce77c8ae1b5d53ba5f701b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/387d5d69eafc142682ce77c8ae1b5d53ba5f701b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/b32ed0ea0d03bc2eec88c7047d8a3afbc7196fd9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T17:25:51Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:28:10Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1462] The SLA widget is the slas plugin''s contribution, and the bundled automations UI no longer gates on the manifest\n\nDashboards (core) named an optional plugin''s widget: `WidgetType.REPORT_SLA`,\nits config schema, its picker option, its form fields and a `weeks` draft key\nall lived in dashboards while slas drew the card. The type now rides slas''\nmanifest (`WidgetTypeSpec(key=SlaWidgetType.REPORT, config_model=SlaWidgetConfig)`,\nthe approvals pattern), so disabling slas withdraws it and a saved\n`report_sla` row reads as a missing plugin''s like any other; the key is\nunchanged, so existing rows keep working (no migration: the column is a\nString). The dashboards enum, schemas, widget-meta and config fields lose every\nSLA line; the picker''s contributed half comes from `/capabilities`.\n\nTwo generalisations were needed to keep what the builtin had:\n- `WidgetTypeSpec.config_model` (kernel): dashboards shape-checks a contributed\n  config on create, PATCH and layout save (`widgets.plugin_config`) — the same\n  422 a builtin gets — and a PATCH of a plugin widget''s config no longer\n  raises on `WidgetType(value)` (it did, for any contributed type).\n- `SlotId.dashboardWidgetConfig` (SDK): a widget type''s settings form, drawn by\n  the Add/Edit dialog in place of the host''s fields; slas contributes the\n  project scope + window form (`SlaWidgetConfigFields`, over the projects\n  picker slot).\n\n`automations/ui/query-lifetime.ts` gated every query on\n`caps.plugins.includes(\"automations\")` — a bundled core is registered only\nwhile the server loads it, so the gate only blanked the page until\ncapabilities answered — and defaulted `staleTime: 0` (refetch on every mount).\nBoth go, and so does the same gate in `node-shapes.ts`. A new boundary test\nscans the bundled packages for optional-plugin vocabulary (names and the\nwidget/view keys they own, read from the generated module map) and for\n`staleTime: 0`.\n\nVerified: pytest dashboards/sla/module contracts/modules map/federation (96),\nnode --test (199, incl. the new scan), tsc + the slas/dashboards/automations\npackages, build-all, the dashboards-package and SLA-report proofs twice each\nagainst a worktree server (the SLA proof gained a phase: the Edit widget\ndialog draws the slas form and a window change saves through its model).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"a6224d5b28e5161a1f59ecc3381434074fcb6e37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/a6224d5b28e5161a1f59ecc3381434074fcb6e37"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/b32ed0ea0d03bc2eec88c7047d8a3afbc7196fd9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/b32ed0ea0d03bc2eec88c7047d8a3afbc7196fd9","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKGIzMmVkMGVhMGQwM2JjMmVlYzg4YzcwNDdkOGEzYWZiYzcxOTZmZDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/f466b43202aa29c7c17ae3c6a4d62aaa3971d42c","sha":"f466b43202aa29c7c17ae3c6a4d62aaa3971d42c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/f466b43202aa29c7c17ae3c6a4d62aaa3971d42c"}],"sha":"b32ed0ea0d03bc2eec88c7047d8a3afbc7196fd9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/b32ed0ea0d03bc2eec88c7047d8a3afbc7196fd9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/f466b43202aa29c7c17ae3c6a4d62aaa3971d42c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T17:08:46Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:28:10Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1461] A failed collab bind hands the page back to its own editor, and a session arriving mid-edit never replaces the draft\n\nThree faults in the page''s live-session hand-off, each reproduced first in the\nmocked proof (web/scripts/browser-live-editing.mjs, phases 4-6) before the fix:\n\n1. A bind that failed (the binding chunk could not be fetched) was logged by the\n   editor and swallowed: `boundRef` stayed false, `editable` refused every\n   keystroke, and the panel kept \"Editing together\" with Done enabled. The\n   binding.ts wrapper had no catch and session.tsx pushed `unavailable` only on\n   join/socket refusals. Now `roomBinding` catches, the session leaves the room\n   and pushes `unavailable`, so `usePageEditing.legacy` flips and the page''s own\n   editor (Save with expected_version / Cancel, plain-text switch) takes over;\n   the failure is still reported to the console.\n\n2. `useLiveDocument` answered `none` while the collab remote was still loading,\n   so Edit opened the page''s own editor; when the remote landed the session\n   opened, the panel unmounted that editor and mounted a bound one, and a\n   non-empty room replaced whatever had been typed. The manifest now DECLARES\n   what a remote serves live (`PluginUiManifest.live_documents`, reported per\n   remote by /capabilities and read by the host loader), the SDK holds those\n   entity types as \"arriving\" while such a remote loads, and the surface shows\n   its joining state instead. With no remote declaring one nothing waits, so\n   the no-remote fixture does not hang.\n\n3. A session that shows up after typing began (the plugin enabled mid-edit) is\n   offered, not imposed: the page''s own editor stays, this client is present as\n   a reader, and \"Join and merge\" reopens the session as an editor with\n   `keepDraft` — the draft seeds an empty room, or is applied to a non-empty one\n   as this person''s own change (through the sync plugin, so colleagues receive\n   it and Mod-z takes it back). With nothing typed the session is joined\n   without asking. Rejected: a three-way merge — there is no base to merge\n   against once the room has moved on, and the person chose to join.\n\nThe loader test covers the arriving report; the proof runs the three new\nphases end to end against the built collab remote.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"1092fa4e58dde50a76c5dbe6502b5ae87611386c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/1092fa4e58dde50a76c5dbe6502b5ae87611386c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/f466b43202aa29c7c17ae3c6a4d62aaa3971d42c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/f466b43202aa29c7c17ae3c6a4d62aaa3971d42c","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKGY0NjZiNDMyMDJhYTI5YzdjMTdhZTNjNmE0ZDYyYWFhMzk3MWQ0MmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/c4364d4be0148915afe32acd67acb6be1fd5da5b","sha":"c4364d4be0148915afe32acd67acb6be1fd5da5b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/c4364d4be0148915afe32acd67acb6be1fd5da5b"}],"sha":"f466b43202aa29c7c17ae3c6a4d62aaa3971d42c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/f466b43202aa29c7c17ae3c6a4d62aaa3971d42c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/c4364d4be0148915afe32acd67acb6be1fd5da5b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T16:49:46Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:28:10Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1466] The plugin-columns proof no longer races the board''s second column, disabling mcp is measured to withdraw its endpoint, two dropped measurements return, and control bytes are refused\n\nbrowser-plugin-columns.mjs asserted `batches.length === 1` right after the\nboard rendered (\"the board shares the list''s read\"). The board''s rows arrive\none `/items/grouped` column at a time, and useStableItemBatches asks only for\nids no chunk of this mount holds yet — so when both columns land in one render\nthe list''s chunk is reused and nothing is requested, and when they land in two\na chunk is appended per late column. Which happens is scheduling, which is why\nit passed 5/5 alone and failed once in the 31-script chain. The proof now waits\nfor the batch count to settle and asserts the invariant either way: every\nappended chunk is a strict subset of the page (never the whole page again), no\nid and no chunk is asked twice. Three consecutive runs pass; all three took the\nshared branch, and the check text says which branch a run took.\n\ntest_mcp.py''s plugin-manager test only asserted the settings field was gone.\nA new test records the desired state through `pluginmgr.service.disable` on the\n`mcp` row, applies it the way the reconciler does (`live._disable` →\n`PluginRuntime.disable`, unmounting the routes) and probes `/api/v1/mcp`:\n401 before, 404 after, JSON not the SPA shell. It found a product gap on the\nway: the \"unknown API path must 404\" guard lived inside the GET-only SPA\ncatch-all, so a POST to a withdrawn plugin route answered 405 Method Not\nAllowed — present, in a sense. `_mount_spa` now registers an all-method\n`/api/v1/{path}` 404 guard ahead of the catch-all, and `create_app` exposes\nthe runtime as `app.state.plugin_runtime` so a test can bind it without the\nlifespan. The test runs under its own `admission.RuntimeGate` so the\nmodule-scoped app keeps answering 401 rather than 503.\n\nTwo measurements RADD-1410 dropped with automations-graph-proof and pager-proof\nare back where they belong: automations-canvas-proof asserts the saved\nbranching rule keeps both of the filter''s fork ports (API round-trip) and that\nSettings → Automations renders with that rule in its list (the white screen a\nnaive `rule.actions.length` once threw); board-navigation-proof reads the\nqueue pager''s own total span and asserts it states the seeded 201 (the\npage-number buttons glued their digits onto the nav text, which first read as\n12201). The canvas proof ran green against the local dev server; the board\nproof against the built bundle.\n\nplugin-boundaries.test.mjs refuses any tracked .ts/.tsx/.py/.mjs/.css that\ncarries a byte in 0x00–0x08 (four NULs sat in plugin-sdk/src/slots.tsx until\nfbec1008, invisible to tsc, vite and every AST scan), with the detector checked\nagainst a sample so it cannot pass vacuously, and .gitattributes marks those\nextensions `text diff` so a stray byte shows in a diff instead of \"Binary files\ndiffer\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"cc173fad344173195c97179e4a231fde0637034b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/cc173fad344173195c97179e4a231fde0637034b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/c4364d4be0148915afe32acd67acb6be1fd5da5b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/c4364d4be0148915afe32acd67acb6be1fd5da5b","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKGM0MzY0ZDRiZTAxNDg5MTVhZmUzMmFjZDY3YWNiNmJlMWZkNWRhNWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/515a1fed95b2cf64f9f780cef9dadf7c00b5dc03","sha":"515a1fed95b2cf64f9f780cef9dadf7c00b5dc03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/515a1fed95b2cf64f9f780cef9dadf7c00b5dc03"}],"sha":"c4364d4be0148915afe32acd67acb6be1fd5da5b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/c4364d4be0148915afe32acd67acb6be1fd5da5b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/515a1fed95b2cf64f9f780cef9dadf7c00b5dc03/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T16:40:36Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:28:10Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1465] The SDK is 2.0.0 with a ledger of its removed exports, every remote declares it, and the plugin docs say what the tree does\n\n`UI_API_VERSION` goes from 1.19.0 to 2.0.0: the RADD-1343 wave removed\n`paletteAnswerQuery`, `ANCHOR_CONTEXT_CHARS`, `textNodesOf`, `SlotId.sidebarNav`\n(`sidebar.nav`), `SlotId.itemAction` (`item.action`) and\n`HostComponents.SchemaForm` from the public surface, and a minor bump would have\ntold a 1.x remote it was still compatible. docs/plugin-ui.md gains the 2.0.0\nledger entry saying what went and where each job lives now.\n\n`isUiApiCompatible` already refuses a different major, so the bump alone would\nhave refused EVERY in-repo remote: sixteen builtin manifests, the acme-notes\nexample, the plugin_cli template and the capabilities router''s default all\npinned 1.x. They declare 2.0.0 now (the router''s default is a named\n`DEFAULT_UI_API_VERSION`), and so do the twenty-three mocked proofs whose\n`/capabilities` fixture feeds the real loader, plus the collab, render and AI\nsettings proofs that assert on the version. plugin-loader.test.mjs flips its\ngate cases (2.x accepted, every 1.x and 3.x refused) and gains a test that\nreads every manifest''s declared version through `isUiApiCompatible` — the\nregression that a wire constant with no compiler cannot catch. `build-all`\nbuilds the host with 20 bundled UIs and all 17 remotes.\n\nDocs: `SchemaForm` is described as the SDK''s own (RADD-1409), not host-filled;\nthe settings-section paragraph replaces the `gcTime: 0` / `staleTime: 0` advice\nwith shared keys and the SDK''s normal stale times (the loader drops a withdrawn\nplugin''s cache itself); the recipe''s tsconfig.json is spelled out and\ndocs/plugin-development.md gains the one-line tsconfig convention; the\nRADD-1395 live-provider proof moves from Remaining to Resolved in the research\nREADME.\n\nNOT done, and why: web/package.json keeps `yjs`, `y-prosemirror`, `y-protocols`\nand `y-websocket`. The collab remote''s own package.json does declare them, but\nno plugin UI package is an npm workspace — package-lock.json has zero\n`@radd-plugin-ui` entries and `@xyflow/react` (used by no host file) is a host\ndependency for the same reason — so the host manifest is the one `npm ci` that\ninstalls every remote''s third-party modules, and pruning them would break the\ncollab build on a fresh CI install. docs/plugin-development.md now states that\nconvention instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"5f5d8f3fc0b4a6798a65fa7b8ed39135902f5378","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/5f5d8f3fc0b4a6798a65fa7b8ed39135902f5378"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/515a1fed95b2cf64f9f780cef9dadf7c00b5dc03","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/515a1fed95b2cf64f9f780cef9dadf7c00b5dc03","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDUxNWExZmVkOTViMmNmNjRmOWY3ODBjZWY5ZGFkZjdjMDBiNWRjMDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/77aa6b07493d260b76af9b9bd2d91b6b3574b8cf","sha":"77aa6b07493d260b76af9b9bd2d91b6b3574b8cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/77aa6b07493d260b76af9b9bd2d91b6b3574b8cf"}],"sha":"515a1fed95b2cf64f9f780cef9dadf7c00b5dc03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/515a1fed95b2cf64f9f780cef9dadf7c00b5dc03"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/77aa6b07493d260b76af9b9bd2d91b6b3574b8cf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T16:34:56Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:28:10Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1464] Host pages read the admin role through the SDK hook, and the pins bar keys its icons on RoutePath\n\nSeven host pages (settings layout, storage, general, sign-in, users, link-types\nand the project states page) decided \"is this an instance admin\" by comparing\n`me?.instance_role === InstanceRole.admin`. `instance_role` is the account''s\ncolumn; `global_role` is what the server''s bypass answers for THIS credential,\nand it is what `useIsInstanceAdmin()` and `usePermissions` read (RADD-1392,\nRADD-1422 did the same move for the plugin pages). A page comparing the column\ncan offer what its API refuses, or hide what it allows. They all call the SDK\nhook now; the unused `useCurrentUser`/`InstanceRole` imports go with it.\n\nThe boundary test''s `instance_role` scan (RADD-1422) now covers `web/src` too.\nTwo files may name the column: `lib/types/users.ts`, which declares it, and the\nUsers page, which EDITS other accounts'' ladder — a row''s `instance_role` there\nis the feature, not a gate. The test pins that: the Users page must call the\nhook, must never read `me.instance_role`, and must still read rows (so the\nallowance cannot go stale). The issue named \"the auth query\" as an allowed\nreader; no query in `web/src/lib` reads the column, so nothing is allowed there.\n\nPinsBar''s LINK_ICONS keyed `/inbox`, `/starred`, `/timesheet`, `/reports`,\n`/portal` — and `/projects`, `/settings` — as literals beside `PageRoute.pages`;\nthey are `RoutePath.*` now, so a moved route moves the icon with it. The\n`/dashboards`, `/cycles` and `/p/` prefixes stay literal: they match families of\nparameterised routes and RoutePath has no bare constant for them.\npin-icons.test.mjs parses the table from source, so it learns to resolve\n`RoutePath.<name>` (literals and the file''s segment constants) and gains a case\nfor a pinned host page; its wiki case had failed on the unparsed rows.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"34ee9b06477c501db64141f6b9f88f2ce095eae7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/34ee9b06477c501db64141f6b9f88f2ce095eae7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/77aa6b07493d260b76af9b9bd2d91b6b3574b8cf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/77aa6b07493d260b76af9b9bd2d91b6b3574b8cf","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDc3YWE2YjA3NDkzZDI2MGI3NmFmOWI5YmQyZDkxYjZiMzU3NGI4Y2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/56b951fc5f58baaca85e398b8b864fbe4c683eb2","sha":"56b951fc5f58baaca85e398b8b864fbe4c683eb2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/56b951fc5f58baaca85e398b8b864fbe4c683eb2"}],"sha":"77aa6b07493d260b76af9b9bd2d91b6b3574b8cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/77aa6b07493d260b76af9b9bd2d91b6b3574b8cf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/56b951fc5f58baaca85e398b8b864fbe4c683eb2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T16:32:54Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:28:10Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1463] Every plugin UI, the SDK and the example draw with semantic tokens, and a boundary test refuses a raw palette class\n\nThe internal reply row and its \"Internal\" chip in CommentReplies used raw amber\n(`border-amber-400/40 bg-amber-500/5`, `bg-amber-500/15 text-amber-300`); the\ntext-amber-300 ink fails 4.5:1 in the light theme. They now use the warning\ncallout''s tokens, the same ones IssueCommentComposer already uses for the same\nmeaning — measured over the built bundle at 4.99:1 (dark) and 4.70:1 (light)\nfor the chip and the chosen audience option, 10.9/13.1 for the reply text. The\nreply audience is a SegmentedChoice (\"Public reply | Internal reply\", the issue\ncomposer''s words) instead of a native checkbox; comment-replies-proof clicks the\noption. The idle option''s `text-fg-muted` reads 4.41:1 in light — pre-existing,\nshared with the issue composer, and left as a finding.\n\nSegmentedChoice was a `role=radiogroup` where every radio was a tab stop and the\narrow keys did nothing. It now has a roving tabindex (the checked option is the\none stop) and ArrowLeft/Right/Up/Down plus Home/End move the selection and the\nfocus, as native radios do; the scratch measurement confirms exactly one option\nat tabIndex 0 before and after an ArrowLeft.\n\nSweep of the plugin UIs: the ai results, pages (NewFromTemplate, PageLinkedItems,\nPageHistory), reporting''s report-state, the SDK''s page-extensions and the host''s\nQueryBar error texts use text-status-danger-ink; pages'' PublicBadge uses the\nstatus-success pair; slas'' paused chip uses bg-elevated (bg-strong was a border\ntoken used as a fill) and PolicyForm drops `[color-scheme:dark]`; the ai\nProviderModal''s reasoning checkbox is the kit Switch (data-ai-provider-reasoning\nfor the two proofs that drive it) and PresetsSection''s delete asks through\nuseConfirm (ai-settings-page-proof answers the dialog); the acme-notes example\nloses its border-zinc-800. mailintake''s PreviewDialog only NAMED the old class\nin a comment; the comment is reworded so the scan reads code, not history.\nai/read/ReadMenu.tsx, named in the issue at lines 529/539, is 191 lines and\ncarries no raw class.\n\nplugin-boundaries.test.mjs gains the scan: every `modules/*/ui/src`, the SDK and\nexamples/ against the whole palette, `web/src` against the documented zinc/indigo\ninvariant (the issue''s premise of an existing web/src scan was wrong: none\nexisted). The pattern is asserted against samples so the test cannot pass\nvacuously; `text-black` on a fixed fill remains the one allowed exception.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"f18ca4e78d264c92c18ff62eb74348640c1386cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/f18ca4e78d264c92c18ff62eb74348640c1386cf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/56b951fc5f58baaca85e398b8b864fbe4c683eb2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/56b951fc5f58baaca85e398b8b864fbe4c683eb2","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDU2Yjk1MWZjNWY1OGJhYWNhODVlMzk4YjhiODY0ZmJlNGM2ODNlYjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/19a2425b4048831deacc9d0e28975cb43289068f","sha":"19a2425b4048831deacc9d0e28975cb43289068f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/19a2425b4048831deacc9d0e28975cb43289068f"}],"sha":"56b951fc5f58baaca85e398b8b864fbe4c683eb2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/56b951fc5f58baaca85e398b8b864fbe4c683eb2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/19a2425b4048831deacc9d0e28975cb43289068f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T16:26:13Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:28:10Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1457] An undeliverable notification is recorded as undeliverable, not as emailed\n\n`mailer.record_undeliverable` stamped `emailed_at = now` on every row the loops\ncould not carry for want of a MAIL_TRANSPORT provider, and both loops stamped\nthe same column for rows they dropped (no mailbox, refused past the retry\nladder, read first, stale, digest opted out). The record then said \"emailed\"\nabout rows nobody was sent, and a mail plugin re-enabled an hour later found\nnothing to send.\n\n`notifications.delivery` (migration `d1457undeliverable`, backfilled `sent`\nwhere `emailed_at` was set and `pending` otherwise) carries the email channel''s\nverdict as `NotificationDelivery`: pending, sent, undeliverable, dropped —\n`dropped` added beside the three the issue named, because a row given up on\nmust not be retried while a row that merely had no transport must. `emailed_at`\nis set by a SENT verdict alone (`mailer.settle` refuses any other pairing).\n`record_undeliverable` records UNDELIVERABLE, leaves `emailed_at` NULL and emits\none `notification.undeliverable` per row (declared on the manifest, in the map),\nonly for rows still pending, so a tick without a transport announces a row once.\nBoth loops select through one predicate, `mailer.eligible`: pending rows, plus —\nwhile a transport is live — undeliverable rows younger than the new\n`notify_undeliverable_retry_hours` (24), so a returning transport carries the\nrecent backlog and leaves the older rows undeliverable. No SMTP fallback returns\nto notify: the transport stays a socket.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"73eebb33395cf4afddfcf2b995aaa8bd59f5b484","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/73eebb33395cf4afddfcf2b995aaa8bd59f5b484"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/19a2425b4048831deacc9d0e28975cb43289068f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/19a2425b4048831deacc9d0e28975cb43289068f","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDE5YTI0MjViNDA0ODgzMWRlYWNjOWQwZTI4OTc1Y2I0MzI4OTA2OGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/6eae65dae31691c6dfa45b0605f9682be2782940","sha":"6eae65dae31691c6dfa45b0605f9682be2782940","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/6eae65dae31691c6dfa45b0605f9682be2782940"}],"sha":"19a2425b4048831deacc9d0e28975cb43289068f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/19a2425b4048831deacc9d0e28975cb43289068f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/6eae65dae31691c6dfa45b0605f9682be2782940/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T16:15:44Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:28:10Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1458] A transition check hears only about the moves its rule gated\n\n`workflow.checks.state_moved` called every TRANSITION_CHECK provider''s `moved()`\nafter every state change, so `ApprovalGate.moved` spent a banked approval on any\nmove into the approved target, including one through a transition row with no\n`require_approval` rule (an exact In Progress → Done row beside a gated\nwildcard). The approval an admin granted for the gated move was consumed by a\nmove nobody gated.\n\n`check_transition` now returns the plugin check keys the governing row''s rules\nnamed (empty when no row governed the move), items hands them to `state_moved`\non both the single-item and the cross-project path, and `state_moved` tells only\nthose providers, plus any that declares `observes_all_moves = True` on the\nprovider (documented on `TransitionCheckProvider`; `ApprovalGate` declares\nFalse). `items.service.merge` still ignores the return value: the merge''s\nCanceled move never told providers before either.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"93aae59f8aab4d67afdfede87da267e72170b70f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/93aae59f8aab4d67afdfede87da267e72170b70f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/6eae65dae31691c6dfa45b0605f9682be2782940","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/6eae65dae31691c6dfa45b0605f9682be2782940","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDZlYWU2NWRhZTMxNjkxYzZkZmE0NWIwNjA1Zjk2ODJiZTI3ODI5NDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/5c54f4a951b63d339fb4e9b6460ba9c26ba84ed2","sha":"5c54f4a951b63d339fb4e9b6460ba9c26ba84ed2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/5c54f4a951b63d339fb4e9b6460ba9c26ba84ed2"}],"sha":"6eae65dae31691c6dfa45b0605f9682be2782940","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/6eae65dae31691c6dfa45b0605f9682be2782940"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/5c54f4a951b63d339fb4e9b6460ba9c26ba84ed2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T16:09:58Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:28:10Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1456] Kernel sockets refuse a duplicate provider, and each socket declares whether it fails open or closed\n\n`register_plugin` wrote integrations through the generic keyed loop, so a second\nplugin on the same (socket, name) replaced the first''s provider silently, while\nentity links already raised. Consumers then picked arbitrarily: the mail\ntransport took the first provider, the subject lookup the first match, and\n`workflow.checks.providers` re-keyed every provider by its own `check`, letting\na plugin answer for another''s rules.\n\nThe registry now records which plugin owns each integration key, raises\n`ContributionConflict` naming both plugins before anything is written (a plugin\nre-registering its own key is not a conflict; an import-time\n`register_integration` on a taken key is), and refuses a second plugin on a\nsingle-provider socket. The plugin manager puts that message on the row instead\nof the bare type name. `sockets.single_provider(socket, where=)` is the one\nhelper for a consumer that needs exactly one provider: it raises\n`AmbiguousProvider` on two, and the mail transport, the subject lookups by event\ntype and by scope use it; `checks.providers()` refuses a provider whose `check`\ndiffers from its registered name. Every `Socket` member has a `SocketPolicy`\n(`fails_closed`, `single`) in `SOCKET_POLICIES`, matched to what each consumer\ndoes today, and the generated module map prints it as a fourth column of the\nSockets table with a \"Socket policies\" section explaining the two policies.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"eeb1b857d15ce409c13239c94216bac6dee95caf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/eeb1b857d15ce409c13239c94216bac6dee95caf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/5c54f4a951b63d339fb4e9b6460ba9c26ba84ed2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/5c54f4a951b63d339fb4e9b6460ba9c26ba84ed2","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDVjNTRmNGE5NTFiNjNkMzM5ZmI0ZTliNjQ2MGJhOWMyNmJhODRlZDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/ee268a42436536850ce67ab27607beffb2dbda78","sha":"ee268a42436536850ce67ab27607beffb2dbda78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/ee268a42436536850ce67ab27607beffb2dbda78"}],"sha":"5c54f4a951b63d339fb4e9b6460ba9c26ba84ed2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/5c54f4a951b63d339fb4e9b6460ba9c26ba84ed2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/ee268a42436536850ce67ab27607beffb2dbda78/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T16:04:48Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:28:09Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1460] An enable failure stops only what started, and a resume schedules each loop once\n\n`PluginRuntime.enable` stopped the plugin on every failure, so a mount that\nraised before `start_plugin` ran the shutdown hooks of a plugin that never\nstarted, and a hook that raised there replaced the mount error in the\nreconciler''s row. `stop_plugin` popped a plugin''s loop handles only after every\nshutdown hook succeeded, so a failed hook left stopped handles behind; the\nretry (or `resume`) stopped them again and `start_plugin` appended a second\ncopy of every loop to the same list.\n\nNow a plugin counts as started from its first startup hook (a start that failed\nhalfway has hooks to undo), `stop_plugin` is a no-op for a plugin whose start\nnever began, each loop handle is dropped as it stops (so a raising hook leaves\nnone behind while a raising loop keeps its handle for the retry),\n`start_plugin` schedules loops only when none survive, and a shutdown hook that\nfails during an enable rollback is logged and added as a note on the original\nerror. `mount` also removes the routes it included before a later step raised,\nsince `unmount` cannot find routes that were never recorded as the plugin''s.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"6b1d84a68b3e9ad0f6976056560fe027e0e35726","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/6b1d84a68b3e9ad0f6976056560fe027e0e35726"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/ee268a42436536850ce67ab27607beffb2dbda78","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/ee268a42436536850ce67ab27607beffb2dbda78","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKGVlMjY4YTQyNDM2NTM2ODUwY2U2N2FiMjc2MDdiZWZmYjJkYmRhNzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/38313f8bf9da53d126367565a2078819a534ee1f","sha":"38313f8bf9da53d126367565a2078819a534ee1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/38313f8bf9da53d126367565a2078819a534ee1f"}],"sha":"ee268a42436536850ce67ab27607beffb2dbda78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/ee268a42436536850ce67ab27607beffb2dbda78"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/38313f8bf9da53d126367565a2078819a534ee1f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T16:29:46Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:28:09Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1452] The trigger inspector''s latest-payload lookup is bounded, and entity search escapes LIKE wildcards\n\n`events.latest_ref` (RADD-1331) selected `payload ? subject` ordered by id\ndesc with no index behind it, so opening the inspector on a trigger whose\nsubject no event had ever carried scanned the whole ledger, once per subject.\nThe lookup is now `latest_ref_statement`: it filters by the event types that\ndeclare the subject — `EventTypeSpec.subjects`, or the event''s own entity type,\nwhich `emit` adds as a subject — through the indexed `event_type` column, and\nby a window of recent ids (`events_latest_ref_scan_rows`, a Settings field,\ndefault 50 000) over the primary key; a subject no registered type carries is\nnot queried at all. No GIN index was added: the point is not to need one.\nSeparately, the derived entity search (RADD-1327) interpolated the needle into\nan ILIKE pattern, so `a_b` matched every `aXb` and `%` matched everything. The\ncodebase already had two escape helpers — `radd.db.ilike_term` and\n`items.slq.escape_like` — so there is now one: `radd.db.escape_like` (with\n`LIKE_ESCAPE`), which `ilike_term` builds on and `items.slq.helpers`\nre-exports, so the SLQ dialects keep their import and the kernel, which may\nnot import a module, reads the same definition. The kernel search uses it, as\ndo the item link search and the three plugin SLQ fields (roadmap,\ncommented_by, logged_by) that built their own `%value%` patterns.\n`SEARCH_SCAN_FACTOR` moved to `settings.entity_search_scan_factor`. Tests: the\n`a_b`/`aXb` case fails without the fix; the compiled lookup is asserted to\ncarry the type filter, the id window and LIMIT 1, and to be None for an\nundeclared subject.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"56267ceb4e510a8e7e58dedb85ad7cec0e0b9f58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/56267ceb4e510a8e7e58dedb85ad7cec0e0b9f58"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/38313f8bf9da53d126367565a2078819a534ee1f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/38313f8bf9da53d126367565a2078819a534ee1f","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDM4MzEzZjhiZjlkYTUzZDEyNjM2NzU2NWEyMDc4ODE5YTUzNGVlMWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/b447d34bac903c1df3c24e37f5f3f02702893b58","sha":"b447d34bac903c1df3c24e37f5f3f02702893b58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/b447d34bac903c1df3c24e37f5f3f02702893b58"}],"sha":"38313f8bf9da53d126367565a2078819a534ee1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/38313f8bf9da53d126367565a2078819a534ee1f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/b447d34bac903c1df3c24e37f5f3f02702893b58/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T16:23:39Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:28:09Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1451] \"Merge/pull request updated\" fires only for changes someone would automate on\n\n`vcs.triggers.NOISE_FIELDS` was a denylist of four bookkeeping keys, so every\nother key a host stamps on an update reached the trigger: a GitLab `update`\ndelivery carrying only `head_pipeline_id`, `merge_status`, `total_time_spent`\nor `time_change` fired \"merge request updated\" on every pipeline run and every\ntime entry. The vocabulary is now an ALLOWLIST, `MrChangeField` (title,\ndescription, labels, assignees, reviewers, milestone, draft, source_branch,\ntarget_branch, commits), in the connector kit''s new `changes.py`, which every\nhost parser shares: GitLab maps its `changes` keys onto it (`milestone_id` ->\nmilestone), the GitHub shape maps `title`/`body`/`base` (and Forgejo''s `ref`)\nonto it, and anything else is dropped before `fire_ref_action`, which already\nfires nothing for an update with an empty diff. The same module owns\n`diff_entries`, which now writes only the sides the host sent: GitHub''s\n`edited` gives the old value and the pull request the new one; a push with no\n`before`/`after` carries the request''s head sha as `to` with no `from`, and a\npush with neither is the kernel''s \"it changed\" entry — never the \"old\"/\"new\"\nplaceholders the previous parser invented. The declared payload schema\nenumerates the allowlist on `changes.field`; the pinned trigger catalog is\nunchanged (labels and flags only). `time_spent_changed` keeps reading the raw\ntime keys the allowlist drops.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"b7e6b52ce0ba448ab0479d8a5bd677152b51a538","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/b7e6b52ce0ba448ab0479d8a5bd677152b51a538"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/b447d34bac903c1df3c24e37f5f3f02702893b58","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/b447d34bac903c1df3c24e37f5f3f02702893b58","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKGI0NDdkMzRiYWM5MDNjMWRmM2MyNGUzN2Y1ZjNmMDI3MDI4OTNiNTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/09cd9efd594149fcc3f8e022ec0090f4b0fa300f","sha":"09cd9efd594149fcc3f8e022ec0090f4b0fa300f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/09cd9efd594149fcc3f8e022ec0090f4b0fa300f"}],"sha":"b447d34bac903c1df3c24e37f5f3f02702893b58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/b447d34bac903c1df3c24e37f5f3f02702893b58"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/09cd9efd594149fcc3f8e022ec0090f4b0fa300f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T16:18:19Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:28:09Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1450] A skipped action no longer halts the branch, and an ownerless automation runs as the system actor\n\nbca48bfc taught the executor to take a failed action''s item out of the packet\nso the success path stops, but it keyed the filter on `not p.resolves`, which\nis also true of a SKIP (\"no assignee to watch\", \"already in that state\"): a\nskipped item was dropped as if it had failed, and a set-arity skip — which has\nno item id — emptied the whole packet, so nothing after it ever ran. The filter\nnow keys on `PlannedAction.failed`, the flag only a raised action (or an\nunknown action type) sets; skips and refusals still appear in the report and\ntheir items still reach the next node. In the engine, the comment promised\nthat rows predating `created_by_id` keep running as the system actor, while\nthe code raised \"execution account unavailable\" for any owner it could not\nload — including NULL. NULL now means the system actor; only an owner who was\nnamed and has since gone or been deactivated still fails the run closed, and\nthe model comment says so instead of the opposite. Finally `run_failed` was\nemitted outside the run''s cause, so it carried rule_id=None at depth 1; it now\ncarries the run''s own AutomationCause (rule id and chain depth). Five tests in\ntest_automation_runs.py fail without these changes; the existing success-path\nhalting test still passes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"1b701166e5200f0f6021d6a0953dde9377a9532b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/1b701166e5200f0f6021d6a0953dde9377a9532b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/09cd9efd594149fcc3f8e022ec0090f4b0fa300f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/09cd9efd594149fcc3f8e022ec0090f4b0fa300f","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDA5Y2Q5ZWZkNTk0MTQ5ZmNjM2Y4ZTAyMmVjMDA5MGY0YjBmYTMwMGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/9a7e08ef5eb4113ef68f2c1c5ca9367bf5023d86","sha":"9a7e08ef5eb4113ef68f2c1c5ca9367bf5023d86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/9a7e08ef5eb4113ef68f2c1c5ca9367bf5023d86"}],"sha":"09cd9efd594149fcc3f8e022ec0090f4b0fa300f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/09cd9efd594149fcc3f8e022ec0090f4b0fa300f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/9a7e08ef5eb4113ef68f2c1c5ca9367bf5023d86/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T16:29:47Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:28:09Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1459] Server status detail stays admin-only, and the Directory page reports a failed capabilities read\n\n`GET /capabilities` is an `Actor` route — every signed-in member and every public-project\nvisitor reads it — and since RADD-1389 each capability carried its plugin''s `detail`: the AI\nprovider name and model, \"bind account on\", the storage backend and default host, the SSO\nprovider count, the `summary` line. That is operational status for the Server status page\nand the plugin admin pages, not something the world needs to draw the shell.\n\n- capabilities/router.py: `detail` travels only when `authz.is_instance_admin(user)`; every\n  actor (the Anyone principal included) still gets the enabled flags, the plugin set, the nav,\n  the remotes and the type options — the same rows, the same flags, an empty detail. No SPA\n  surface read `detail` for a non-admin: the two readers (Server status, Directory) are admin\n  pages, so nothing else moves.\n- ldap DirectoryPage: RADD-1409 had folded the status card''s error branch into `!caps ?\n  <Spinner>`, so a failed read spun forever. The page now uses the SDK''s new\n  `useCapabilitiesQuery()` (the same shared query, with its state) and draws `QueryError` plus a\n  \"Retry status\" button when the read failed and there is no data; stale data on a refetch error\n  keeps showing rows. `useCapabilities()` derives from the new hook; the federation shim gains\n  the export.\n\nTests: test_capabilities — as a member and as the Anyone principal every `detail` is `{}` while\nthe keys, flags and owners equal the admin''s; as admin ldap/sso/ai detail is present. The two\nexisting router tests pass an in-memory admin instead of `None`, which the gate cannot take.\nbrowser-settings-ownership.mjs gains the actual ldap bundle: after `resetQueries` and a mocked\n500 the page says \"Failed to load server status\", stays mounted, shows no spinner, and Retry\nbrings the three status rows back — run locally: 13 checks passed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"c309403c8c9b2ecfd395298852a7604e18474edf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/c309403c8c9b2ecfd395298852a7604e18474edf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/9a7e08ef5eb4113ef68f2c1c5ca9367bf5023d86","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/9a7e08ef5eb4113ef68f2c1c5ca9367bf5023d86","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDlhN2UwOGVmNWViNDExM2VmNjhmMmMxYzVjYTkzNjdiZjUwMjNkODY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/f96fd18a964ac90f2e813553bd8c5c244cec2a8d","sha":"f96fd18a964ac90f2e813553bd8c5c244cec2a8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/f96fd18a964ac90f2e813553bd8c5c244cec2a8d"}],"sha":"9a7e08ef5eb4113ef68f2c1c5ca9367bf5023d86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/9a7e08ef5eb4113ef68f2c1c5ca9367bf5023d86"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/f96fd18a964ac90f2e813553bd8c5c244cec2a8d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T16:21:09Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:28:09Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1455] Bulk move, link targets and parents go through the item row gate\n\nThree item writes resolved their rows with no row gate, so a relation-qualified holder\n(`item.update@own`) could reach past their own rows, and a hidden item could be probed\nthrough a field that named it:\n\n- items/bulk.py: `bulk_move_items` checked only the project-level atom, and did so with\n  `Permission.ITEM_UPDATE in perms` — which a QUALIFIED holder fails, so `@own` could not\n  move even their own issues, while an unqualified holder moved anything. It now gates with\n  `authz.holds_base` (the RADD-823 rule) and `_move_one` applies `ensure_item_relation` for\n  item.update on the source row, exactly as `require_item_permission` does for every\n  single-item write; a refused row is reported FORBIDDEN in `skipped`, with its key, like\n  bulk_update reports one. `_selected_items` is gone: unknown ids are reported NOT_FOUND\n  instead of being dropped, so a selection is never quietly shortened.\n- items/service/links.py: `_resolve_link_target` resolves by id AND by number through\n  `require_readable_item`, so a target the actor cannot see answers the same 404 as a\n  missing one (the by-number path keeps its `PROJ-N` wording).\n- items/service/relations.py: `_resolve_parent` does the same for a chosen parent; its\n  three callers (create, update, convert) pass the actor. Convert''s keep-when-compatible\n  read of the EXISTING parent stays a bare read — it is not user input.\n\nTests (test_item_relations.py, on the RADD-817 scenario): `@own` bulk-moves their own row,\nthe stranger''s is FORBIDDEN and unmoved, an unknown id is NOT_FOUND; linking to or parenting\nunder a hidden item raises the 404 a made-up id raises, by id and by number, and a visible\nparent still works. RADD-1413''s tests still pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"a21129c87c25a539ff939c7ddbe268e320e77208","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/a21129c87c25a539ff939c7ddbe268e320e77208"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/f96fd18a964ac90f2e813553bd8c5c244cec2a8d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/f96fd18a964ac90f2e813553bd8c5c244cec2a8d","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKGY5NmZkMThhOTY0YWM5MGYyZTgxMzU1M2JkOGM1YzI0NGNlYzJhOGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/5ecd597713d64c5cd870db35401cc4db506e7508","sha":"5ecd597713d64c5cd870db35401cc4db506e7508","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/5ecd597713d64c5cd870db35401cc4db506e7508"}],"sha":"f96fd18a964ac90f2e813553bd8c5c244cec2a8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/f96fd18a964ac90f2e813553bd8c5c244cec2a8d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/5ecd597713d64c5cd870db35401cc4db506e7508/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T16:16:51Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:28:09Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1454] The admin settings list returns a secret as a set marker, never its value\n\n`GET /scoped-settings?scope=instance` — every Directory-page load — sent the decrypted\nvalue of every `secret` SettingSpec (the LDAP bind password) to the browser, because\n`list_for_scope` returned `value: effective` for every row alike. `/resolve` already refused\nsecrets (RADD-1424); the list is now consistent with it.\n\n- settings/service.py: a secret row carries `set` (a non-empty value is in effect — from a\n  row here, a wider scope or the environment) and null `value`/`default`. `set_value` reads\n  an empty secret as \"keep what is stored\" (the mail dialogs'' convention) and writes nothing;\n  `clear_value` (DELETE) is the one way to remove it.\n- settings/schemas.py, web/src/lib/types/settings.ts: `set: bool | None`, nullable value/default.\n- ScopedSettingsEditor (the host implementation the SDK''s bridged `ScopedSettings` draws):\n  a secret row shows Set / Not set and a password field that only ever carries a\n  replacement — typed, it is written on blur/Enter and empties again; left empty, nothing is\n  sent. Its Reset is labelled Clear (there is no default to print). The ldap Connection tab\n  needs no change; ldap_bind_password is the only secret spec, and the mail/AI/SSO pages\n  keep their own has_secret dialogs.\n- ldap: the spec text no longer claims the password is \"readable on this page\"; the stale\n  \"stays admin-readable\" comments in kernel/specs.py and the schema are corrected.\n\nTest: the list as admin holds no plaintext and marks the row set; PUT a replacement\nround-trips through resolve(); PUT \"\" keeps it; DELETE clears the override.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"af1fc766c23de9b87a5244f70cf44d2ceb131b05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/af1fc766c23de9b87a5244f70cf44d2ceb131b05"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/5ecd597713d64c5cd870db35401cc4db506e7508","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/5ecd597713d64c5cd870db35401cc4db506e7508","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDVlY2Q1OTc3MTNkNjRjNWNkODcwZGIzNTQwMWNjNGRiNTA2ZTc1MDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/2cbafc8dd542b004626634633175524106f3f51f","sha":"2cbafc8dd542b004626634633175524106f3f51f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/2cbafc8dd542b004626634633175524106f3f51f"}],"sha":"5ecd597713d64c5cd870db35401cc4db506e7508","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/5ecd597713d64c5cd870db35401cc4db506e7508"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/2cbafc8dd542b004626634633175524106f3f51f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T15:54:57Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:28:09Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1453] Migrations keep the mail settings rows and refuse dishonest downgrades; the deploy doc names every switch this release turns off\n\nFour behaviours migrate OFF for existing rows in this release (VCS publish-on-release,\nmove-on-merge and mirror-time per repository; the email receipt and resolution notice),\nand the notify module no longer carries an SMTP fallback. The release notes are generated\nfrom commits and cannot say so, so docs/deploy.md gains \"Upgrading past v0.48.0\": a table\nof what stops and the page that switches it back on. The local release skill carries the\nsame steps as a post-roll-out checklist.\n\nd1318mailorigin no longer deletes the mail_ack_body / mail_send_resolved rows: RADD-1368\nre-registered exactly those keys (default OFF) with no restoring migration, so the DELETE\ndestroyed a custom receipt text for nothing. d1329verdict''s downgrade raises instead of\n`pass` — the rewritten graphs are not executable by the previous image, and a silent\nsuccess would hand it graphs it cannot run. d1334review leaves act_as_id UNSET when the\nact_as email resolves to nobody and disables that automation with its name in the log,\ninstead of planting a uuid4() that fails closed at run time; it also stamps the ids that\ndo resolve into automation_versions, which the old loop skipped.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"e5413d6569851717a6a631c4d04b246b6e31ac17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/e5413d6569851717a6a631c4d04b246b6e31ac17"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/2cbafc8dd542b004626634633175524106f3f51f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/2cbafc8dd542b004626634633175524106f3f51f","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDJjYmFmYzhkZDU0MmIwMDQ2MjY2MzQ2MzMxNzU1MjQxMDZmM2Y1MWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/8236797d2051b99fd12440198d3a2721cdd2613e","sha":"8236797d2051b99fd12440198d3a2721cdd2613e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/8236797d2051b99fd12440198d3a2721cdd2613e"}],"sha":"2cbafc8dd542b004626634633175524106f3f51f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/2cbafc8dd542b004626634633175524106f3f51f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/8236797d2051b99fd12440198d3a2721cdd2613e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T14:11:19Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T14:17:48Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1448] Replies show by default, Reply is an action, and the composer opens on Comment or Start thread with one submit\n\nEvery comment surface (issue comments, a page''s discussion, inline annotations) shows a comment''s\nreplies unless its thread is resolved, and the disclosure (\"Hide 3 replies\", \"Show 3 replies ·\nresolved\") exists only where replies do. Reply is a separate action in each comment''s footer: one\nclick opens a focused composer under the replies with one primary button, Cancel or Escape closes it\nback to Reply and keeps the draft, and posting closes it onto the new reply. A discussion''s composer\nis a row of two buttons, Comment and Start thread, until one is pressed; open, it has a Comment |\nThread switch, the audience, the editor and ONE submit named for mode and audience, and Cancel keeps\nthe draft.\n\nThe kit carries it: CommentReplies given `expansion` draws the whole thread footer (disclosure,\nReply, `actions`); CommentComposer (+ CommentComposerMode) is new in the SDK; useThreadExpansion\nopens all but resolved threads; repliesLabel is the disclosure''s words. CommentActions deletes\nthrough useConfirm and IconButton and says a root takes its replies with it. On the way: a canned\nresponse was set into state the uncontrolled editor never read, so it never appeared (the editor now\nremounts on the insert); Escape needs a test of its own because ProseMirror marks every Escape\nhandled (escape.ts).\n\nProofs updated: browser-resolvable-threads, browser-page-comments, browser-issue-features,\nbrowser-editor-extensions (mocked); comment-replies-proof, page-threads-proof,\ninline-comments-proof, page-detached-comments-proof (real backend).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ\n(cherry picked from commit 8bc74a0259e6beabf3ec393edf298b8f9ca72b16)","tree":{"sha":"44da81c3139ff0696465cc63544465ad217efc0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/44da81c3139ff0696465cc63544465ad217efc0e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/8236797d2051b99fd12440198d3a2721cdd2613e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/8236797d2051b99fd12440198d3a2721cdd2613e","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDgyMzY3OTdkMjA1MWI5OWZkMTI0NDAxOThkM2EyNzIxY2RkMjYxM2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/1d0a11d5fdb68843351ba668c0c5885a42012135","sha":"1d0a11d5fdb68843351ba668c0c5885a42012135","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/1d0a11d5fdb68843351ba668c0c5885a42012135"}],"sha":"8236797d2051b99fd12440198d3a2721cdd2613e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/8236797d2051b99fd12440198d3a2721cdd2613e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/1d0a11d5fdb68843351ba668c0c5885a42012135/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:20:11Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:20:11Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1395] The live-provider editor proof is verified, and the record says so\n\nThe plugin-isolation record carried the wave''s one unverified item: the\neditor AI proof had only run with the stand-in model because the model host\nrefused connections. On 2026-09-27 a live qwen3.8-27b at localhost:8221 was\navailable; editor-ai-proof.mjs passed every check against the dev instance,\nas did the protected-blocks, provider-options and settings-page proofs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"4659bf68e5d5ef41562e9bcc8c68c4cd0806679d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/4659bf68e5d5ef41562e9bcc8c68c4cd0806679d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/1d0a11d5fdb68843351ba668c0c5885a42012135","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/1d0a11d5fdb68843351ba668c0c5885a42012135","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDFkMGExMWQ1ZmRiNjg4NDMzNTFiYTY2OGMwYzU4ODVhNDIwMTIxMzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/567f8e50db13b5b90530743f8a154ef6e5ced177","sha":"567f8e50db13b5b90530743f8a154ef6e5ced177","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/567f8e50db13b5b90530743f8a154ef6e5ced177"}],"sha":"1d0a11d5fdb68843351ba668c0c5885a42012135","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/1d0a11d5fdb68843351ba668c0c5885a42012135"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/567f8e50db13b5b90530743f8a154ef6e5ced177/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T09:36:11Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:20:11Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1435] GitLab, GitHub and Forgejo run on one connector kit in vcs, and their Settings tabs are vcs''s\n\nThe three connectors were copies of one another plus a payload parser each (1,046\nduplicate lines measured by the D2 audit). vcs, which is core and which every\nconnector already depends on, now owns what they share, bound to the ConnectorSpec\neach connector declares and provides on the vcs_connector socket:\n- vcs/connector_kit/columns.py: ConnectionColumns/RepoColumns mixins. Each connector\n  keeps its own tables (forgejo_connections, github_repos, ...), declared from them;\n  the model diff against a migrated database is empty.\n- store.py: ConnectorStore - connection/repo CRUD, audit events, the active-connection\n  snapshot and capability, env seeding (<provider>_<key> settings) and\n  resolve_for_payload (the spec-111 rule).\n- admin.py: the /<provider>/connections|repos router, built from the store and mounted\n  by the connector. schemas.py: one set of wire shapes.\n- backfill.py: the harness (report, paged client, link, quiet run) around the\n  connector''s walk. github_shape.py: the pull_request/release parser GitHub and\n  Forgejo share. manifest.py: admin event types, entity links, the socket entry.\n- vcs/receiving.py: accept (parse, authenticate, claim), deliver_push,\n  deliver_change and release_published - every receiver''s head and tail.\nA connector keeps its payload parser, its API walker, its time mirror and its spec.\nvcs now depends on automations (the system actor the kit writes as).\n\nFrontend: the gitlab/github/forgejo UI packages shipped only static wording and are\ndeleted. The wording is the spec''s; GET /vcs/connectors (global.manage) lists the\nloaded connectors and the vcs bundled page draws one tab each, so a disabled\nconnector''s tab goes with it.\n\nDrift resolved, GitHub''s behaviour taken:\n- Forgejo pull requests are PULL_REQUEST links from the webhook as from the backfill\n  (the webhook wrote MERGE_REQUEST, so re-deliveries flipped the ref type), titled\n  \"Title (#n)\" on both paths.\n- Forgejo ignores a draft release; GitLab''s release answer carries \"shipped\".\n- Every host strips a repository path before storing and matching it (Forgejo did\n  not), and refuses a JSON body that is not an object (GitHub and Forgejo 500''d).\n- The plugin descriptions follow one template and all mention time mirroring.\n\nTests: the three connectors'' tests keep their intent (imports move to the store and\nthe shared schemas; GitLab''s resolve calls pass an empty body). New\ntest_vcs_connector_kit.py runs the kit''s rules once per host through its real\nreceiver, including a payload signed for another host''s connection being refused.\nbrowser-vcs-settings is rewritten to assert the tabs follow enablement; the\nplugin-availability and second-review proofs answer /vcs/connectors instead of\nserving connector remotes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ\n(cherry picked from commit 5ae86a058184460edd35997f9b9d446b55ec0ff9)","tree":{"sha":"fa09700ab8c1698fb644bb2b2d0c5781df0fb645","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/fa09700ab8c1698fb644bb2b2d0c5781df0fb645"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/567f8e50db13b5b90530743f8a154ef6e5ced177","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/567f8e50db13b5b90530743f8a154ef6e5ced177","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDU2N2Y4ZTUwZGIxM2I1YjkwNTMwNzQzZjhhMTU0ZWY2ZTVjZWQxNzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/febbdc33bd6cbdbf3286440cb11c6ae27da31783","sha":"febbdc33bd6cbdbf3286440cb11c6ae27da31783","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/febbdc33bd6cbdbf3286440cb11c6ae27da31783"}],"sha":"567f8e50db13b5b90530743f8a154ef6e5ced177","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/567f8e50db13b5b90530743f8a154ef6e5ced177"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/febbdc33bd6cbdbf3286440cb11c6ae27da31783/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T09:37:18Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:20:11Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1425] A plugin''s automation action is drawn by its plugin and never blocked by the editor\n\nhasCoreEditor treated every `action.*` key as core, so a contributed action got no\nform, never offered its automation.node.inspector, and RuleEditor refused Save for\ngood. Automations now edits and validates only the actions it declares\n(builtin-actions.ts, checked against the server''s ActionType); any other action\nrenders its plugin''s inspector, else a \"Provided by <plugin>\" line over its schema\nform, and saving asks the server.\n\nSend email and Add participant moved to mailintake and participants in RADD-1387;\ntheir forms, the EmailRecipient roles and send_email''s role-means-per-issue rule\nfollow them. The SDK gains AutomationNodeInspectorProps. RuleCreate/RuleUpdate\ndeclare `note`, and RuleEditor''s payloads are literals so `satisfies` checks them.\nThe schedule boundary test checks the automations implementation instead of an\nempty AST.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ\n(cherry picked from commit d4664cf155acd9204da1b9850ace90f2d2497d65)","tree":{"sha":"20acf97a15cceec0ba8ec389ce018b28e516c338","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/20acf97a15cceec0ba8ec389ce018b28e516c338"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/febbdc33bd6cbdbf3286440cb11c6ae27da31783","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/febbdc33bd6cbdbf3286440cb11c6ae27da31783","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKGZlYmJkYzMzYmQ2Y2JkYmYzMjg2NDQwY2IxMWM2YWUyN2RhMzE3ODM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/51c3777abff31cae43a56435b5b92fdff470f3e5","sha":"51c3777abff31cae43a56435b5b92fdff470f3e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/51c3777abff31cae43a56435b5b92fdff470f3e5"}],"sha":"febbdc33bd6cbdbf3286440cb11c6ae27da31783","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/febbdc33bd6cbdbf3286440cb11c6ae27da31783"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/51c3777abff31cae43a56435b5b92fdff470f3e5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T09:20:05Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:20:11Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1440] docs/modules.md is generated from the plugin manifests, with one capped paragraph per module\n\nThe map was 479 KB of hand-appended rows and addenda (up to 17.7 KB each), with\nper-issue history and claims the code no longer backs. It is now 86 KB and\ngenerated by server/scripts/modules_map.py:\n\n- Structure comes from the RaddPlugin manifests and each plugin''s ui/package.json:\n  core or optional, bundled/remote/host UI, load order, depends_on and\n  weak_depends (an \"at a glance\" table), event types, permission atoms, settings\n  keys, nav items and every contribution kind. Socket providers come from the\n  manifests and socket readers from the source (Socket.X outside an\n  IntegrationSpec). A new RaddPlugin contribution field without a label stops\n  the generator.\n- Prose comes from docs/modules-notes.md: one paragraph per module (what it owns,\n  the seam others use, one trap), each verified against the code, plus the\n  cross-cutting sections that are still true (connection rules, relations and\n  row guards, event diffs, seed-only configuration, field grants, SLQ, cache\n  invalidation, known simplifications). Per-issue history is not carried over;\n  it lives in the tracker, docs/specs/ and git log.\n- tests/test_modules_map.py fails when the checked-in map differs from the\n  generator''s output, when a plugin has no paragraph or a paragraph names no\n  plugin, when a paragraph exceeds 750 characters or is not one paragraph, when\n  a section exceeds 2,500, or when an issue key appears; a third test proves\n  each check refuses its violation.\n\nresearch/plugin-isolation/README.md keeps only its review verdicts and points\nat the generated table for core/UI/depends_on.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ\n(cherry picked from commit 3dcbe89a947644514fa621b52aa9c4d49fa950ff)","tree":{"sha":"5d8c35f99d9c017aa02fbb0accd9b1b3651ed77d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/5d8c35f99d9c017aa02fbb0accd9b1b3651ed77d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/51c3777abff31cae43a56435b5b92fdff470f3e5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/51c3777abff31cae43a56435b5b92fdff470f3e5","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDUxYzM3NzdhYmZmMzFjYWU0M2E1NjQzNWI1YjkyZmRmZjQ3MGYzZTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/83ae71e2aa9036b97399366904a9375706d5d0e6","sha":"83ae71e2aa9036b97399366904a9375706d5d0e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/83ae71e2aa9036b97399366904a9375706d5d0e6"}],"sha":"51c3777abff31cae43a56435b5b92fdff470f3e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/51c3777abff31cae43a56435b5b92fdff470f3e5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/83ae71e2aa9036b97399366904a9375706d5d0e6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T09:16:47Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:20:11Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1427] Spine defects: undeclared subjects raise, backups run under their plugin, group grants read as names\n\n- events: an undeclared event subject read `settings.debug`, which Settings\n  never had, so it left `emit` as an AttributeError and the documented\n  \"degrade to a bare id in production\" never ran. It is a programming error:\n  the clear RuntimeError always, and the dead branch and its docstring go.\n- backup: runs and their stage writes were bare `asyncio.create_task`s,\n  invisible to the plugin lifecycle; they go through `kernel.runtime.spawn`,\n  so disabling `backup` waits for a run in flight. On the way: both\n  completion events passed their type positionally to the keyword-only\n  `emit`, so every successful backup/restore raised a TypeError after\n  finishing and `backup.created`/`backup.restored` never reached the ledger.\n- backup schemas: every datetime is `UtcDatetime`, so times leave with `Z`.\n- access: a group grant''s audit label names the group, like users, teams\n  and roles.\n- collection compression: the path set is `settings.api_prefix` plus the core\n  collections plus every registered list surface''s `rows_path`, so core no\n  longer names the slas plugin''s route and a disabled plugin''s path leaves.\n- realtime: `items` is core; the `settings.modules` guard (which cannot see\n  what is loaded) is gone.\n- mcp: `RADD_MCP_ENABLED` and `mcp_enabled` are removed; the plugin manager\n  is the one switch for this `core=False` plugin.\n- pluginmgr: `all_known()` resolves the core plugins once, not twice.\n- audit: a page loads only the projects its rows name, not the whole table.\n\nEach behaviour change has a test that fails before and passes after.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ\n(cherry picked from commit afc7cd923e0b8f506e34c61dd6c1033f2cf45d15)","tree":{"sha":"537db23938a7ad102ca50f1110a568aff89d8199","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/537db23938a7ad102ca50f1110a568aff89d8199"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/83ae71e2aa9036b97399366904a9375706d5d0e6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/83ae71e2aa9036b97399366904a9375706d5d0e6","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDgzYWU3MWUyYWE5MDM2Yjk3Mzk5MzY2OTA0YTkzNzU3MDZkNWQwZTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/fba429e78e555a3d7753caedd5aa6fbe3ce726d4","sha":"fba429e78e555a3d7753caedd5aa6fbe3ce726d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/fba429e78e555a3d7753caedd5aa6fbe3ce726d4"}],"sha":"83ae71e2aa9036b97399366904a9375706d5d0e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/83ae71e2aa9036b97399366904a9375706d5d0e6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/fba429e78e555a3d7753caedd5aa6fbe3ce726d4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T09:03:41Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:20:11Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1426] Abandoned submission attachments are reclaimed on a schedule, rows and bytes\n\n`forms.staging.sweep_abandoned` promised to emit `form.staging.deleted` per\nabandoned staging area so the spec-102 cascade would reclaim the rows and the\nbytes, but it only returned the ids, and nothing ever called it: every file\nattached to a form that was never submitted stayed on its storage host forever.\n\nThe sweep now emits the event for each area (never silent: the cascade\nconsumer skips silent events), and the forms plugin schedules it as a kernel\nTaskSpec (`forms.staging-sweep`, the mechanism access''s expiry sweep already\nuses; the worker-split gate comes with it). Age and cadence are settings:\n`form_staging_retention_days` (7) and `form_staging_sweep_interval_seconds`\n(3600). The test drives the scheduled task and the real cascade consumer: the\nabandoned area loses its row and its bytes, a live area keeps both.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ\n(cherry picked from commit 21699ad61ea7303d47377954e75bb0a654fa1122)","tree":{"sha":"8b3741b26cc1c596c4f2039a35694c88d8250633","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/8b3741b26cc1c596c4f2039a35694c88d8250633"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/fba429e78e555a3d7753caedd5aa6fbe3ce726d4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/fba429e78e555a3d7753caedd5aa6fbe3ce726d4","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKGZiYTQyOWU3OGU1NTVhM2Q3NzUzY2FlZGQ1YWE2ZmJlM2NlNzI2ZDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/39bfee06b39d3da5ad97e95f0bd6b8facba7e648","sha":"39bfee06b39d3da5ad97e95f0bd6b8facba7e648","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/39bfee06b39d3da5ad97e95f0bd6b8facba7e648"}],"sha":"fba429e78e555a3d7753caedd5aa6fbe3ce726d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/fba429e78e555a3d7753caedd5aa6fbe3ce726d4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/39bfee06b39d3da5ad97e95f0bd6b8facba7e648/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T09:18:42Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:20:11Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1424] Importer, SSO and LDAP credentials are secretbox ciphertext at rest\n\nThe webhook precedent (RADD-1086) applied to the four replayed secrets that\nwere still plaintext: the Jira and Confluence connection `credential`,\n`sso_providers.client_secret` and the `ldap_bind_password` setting.\n\n- Written sealed (`secretbox.seal`: encrypt, but \"\" stays \"\" so\n  `has_credential`/`configured` keep reading the column''s truthiness), read\n  decrypted at the one replay site each (`creds_of`, `idp.exchange_tokens`,\n  `settings.resolve`).\n- Lazy adoption: an untagged legacy value reads as plaintext, is encrypted on\n  the row''s next save (`secretbox.adopt`, applied before the audit snapshot so\n  the adoption is not recorded as a change) and, like webhooks, by a startup\n  sweep per owner that logs and skips when the key is unavailable.\n- Secret settings are handled generically by the settings service: sealed on\n  set_value, decrypted on resolve (an undecryptable one reads as unset instead\n  of failing the settings page and every directory sign-in).\n- Two leaks found on the way, both fixed here: `setting.changed` recorded the\n  bind password as from/to plaintext in the audit ledger (now \"changed\" only),\n  and GET /scoped-settings/resolve?key=ldap_bind_password answered ANY caller,\n  anonymous included, with the password (secret keys now 403 there; the\n  admin-gated list still returns it, RADD-846''s decision).\n- Migration d1424secrets widens both importer `credential` columns to TEXT:\n  VARCHAR(500) holds the ciphertext of at most a 341-byte credential.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ\n(cherry picked from commit 2b1b5cec8d0e4f78eae6de1b2b8e6bfef1c660cd)","tree":{"sha":"81364795be5012fc67773da186dc80d9faf2aa32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/81364795be5012fc67773da186dc80d9faf2aa32"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/39bfee06b39d3da5ad97e95f0bd6b8facba7e648","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/39bfee06b39d3da5ad97e95f0bd6b8facba7e648","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDM5YmZlZTA2YjM5ZDNkYTVhZDk3ZTk1ZjBiZDZiOGZhY2JhN2U2NDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/28961a54717a6b2f40c1d9769048eaf84a7bb49a","sha":"28961a54717a6b2f40c1d9769048eaf84a7bb49a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/28961a54717a6b2f40c1d9769048eaf84a7bb49a"}],"sha":"39bfee06b39d3da5ad97e95f0bd6b8facba7e648","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/39bfee06b39d3da5ad97e95f0bd6b8facba7e648"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/28961a54717a6b2f40c1d9769048eaf84a7bb49a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T09:03:10Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:20:11Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1441] BUILD-LOG.md is the one build narrative; CLAUDE.md keeps the working agreements and PLAN.md its design\n\nCLAUDE.md was 74 KB, 51 KB of it per-wave build history that every agent\nsession loaded before reading a rule, and the same waves were narrated a\nsecond time in PLAN.md §8/§11 and its addenda and a third time in\nBUILD-LOG.md. The audit (RADD-1402, docs area) counted 6 stale claims in the\nCLAUDE.md narrative and 29 in PLAN.md''s, all in history that no longer\ndescribed the tree.\n\nNow:\n- CLAUDE.md opens with four orientation lines and goes straight to the rules\n  (24.8 KB, 244 lines). The three live proof traps from the plugin-ownership\n  preamble moved into \"Verifying UI work\", which also points new proofs at\n  lib/cdp.mjs rather than the pre-lib render-proof.mjs.\n- BUILD-LOG.md opens with \"Waves, newest first\": the preamble''s narrative\n  split into one entry per wave, verbatim, followed by the kernel+plugin\n  migration log it started as, then PLAN.md''s §8 and §11 with Addenda 10–15,\n  moved verbatim as the closed record they had become.\n- PLAN.md keeps §1–§7 and §9–§10; §8 is a pointer to the tracker and the log.\n\nNothing was deleted: 2,035 lines of BUILD-LOG.md now hold what 270 + 1,162\nlines of CLAUDE.md + PLAN.md held.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"de3df7c22639989b2cff6499c39fe4fd971d7cc7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/de3df7c22639989b2cff6499c39fe4fd971d7cc7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/28961a54717a6b2f40c1d9769048eaf84a7bb49a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/28961a54717a6b2f40c1d9769048eaf84a7bb49a","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDI4OTYxYTU0NzE3YTZiMmY0MGMxZDk3NjkwNDhlYWY4NGE3YmI0OWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/9b0eec591dfb986bd7ce85fc35e7a39bbdb35744","sha":"9b0eec591dfb986bd7ce85fc35e7a39bbdb35744","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/9b0eec591dfb986bd7ce85fc35e7a39bbdb35744"}],"sha":"28961a54717a6b2f40c1d9769048eaf84a7bb49a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/28961a54717a6b2f40c1d9769048eaf84a7bb49a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/9b0eec591dfb986bd7ce85fc35e7a39bbdb35744/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T23:50:35Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:20:11Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1410] Proof scripts share one harness in lib/ and lose their dead, vacuous and drifted checks\n\n177 files changed, 2645 insertions(+), 5992 deletions(-) (net -3347).\n\nShared scaffolding, each copy pointed at it:\n- lib/cdp.mjs gains waitFor, waitForSelector (moved from lib/docshot), until, PAGE_API, pageFetch,\n  parsed, outputPath, and report() accepting [{name, ok, detail}]; the session loses its unread\n  sessionId and duplicate send; lib/chrome loses the unused `extra` parameter.\n- lib/proof.mjs (proofArgs, startProof/finish), lib/spa-server.mjs (serveBuiltSpa for the mocked\n  proofs), lib/automation-editor.mjs (the editor probes), lib/load-ts.mjs (importTs, evaluateTs for\n  the unit tests), lib/planning-fixture.mjs (the board/planning fixture).\n- The 7 hand-rolled CDP harnesses move to openBrowser; 34 waitFor, 35 until and ~24 in-page API\n  copies, the Node-side post/api builders, the check/report adapters and the mocked-SPA servers\n  go. Screenshots are written to $RADD_PROOF_OUTPUT_DIR or the temp dir, never the source tree.\n- Unit tests: the hand-rolled check() tests run under node:test (108 -> 192 test cases, same\n  assertions); every TS loader is lib/load-ts.\n\nDeleted: pager-proof, grouped-pagination-proof, dom-probe, browser-review-interactions (dead);\nautomations-graph-proof (a subset of automations-canvas-proof); ai-surface-proof (its one unique\ncheck, text outside the selection is untouched, now lives in browser-editor-extensions); the\nRADD-1074 half of ai-validate-node-proof; dead bindings; mock branches no endpoint serves\n(/settings/scoped, the bare /preferences alternates); vacuous checks (the no-Crepe probes,\n[data-scripts-library], [data-top-bar]); live_supported and item_key fixture arguments.\n\nDrifted proofs repaired (a proof is verification, not product behaviour):\n- 12 automation proofs opened a rule by clicking the row''s first button, which is its Enabled\n  switch; they press \"Edit <name>\" through lib/automation-editor.\n- intake-validation: verdict.warn/verdict.block nodes, no trigger mode, \"New issue\", /p/KEY,\n  \"Create issue\". ai-validate-node: the warn port, the card found by data-node-type.\n- RADD-1287 copy: \"New issue\" (editor-parity, new-item-fields, salvador-reports), \"New host\"\n  (storage-email), \"issues\" (admin-affordances), \"Filter issues\"/\"per issue\"/\"Link to issue\"\n  (automations canvas-edit, delete, arity, coverage); salvador-reports reads the title field.\n- notification-matrix drives the subscription dialog; settings-cleanup the Grant role dialog;\n  project-rail the related-projects toggle; inline-comments drops the orphan step that\n  page-detached-comments covers; browser-second-review drops the removed Email step, uses\n  automation-ui-fixture.py, loads the github remote and clicks the ingest switch; import-mapping\n  drops the removed props; the vcs-time-mirror connection check matches /GitLab/.\n- browser-issue-features and browser-second-review join test:browser (31 proofs).\n\nVariants kept (each is load-bearing):\n- Wait budgets longer than the lib default: ai-protect (500 ms), csat-mail-plugins and\n  dashboards-package (80 attempts), collab and collab-plugin (their time budgets), and\n  page-detached-comments (same wall time at 250 ms).\n- API helpers with a different result: dashboards-package (raw text for byte comparisons),\n  public-project ({status, data}, lenient json), settings-cleanup (lenient api, status-only post),\n  page-threads (bearer headers, no cookie), access-restriction (throws on non-ok), editor-ai,\n  contributed-modes, pages-package and page-templates (lenient Node-side parse).\n- Own sign-in (proofArgs only): csat-mail-plugins, contributed-modes and collab-plugin (429 retry,\n  two browsers), jira-import-page (write recorder before sign-in), and every proof that signs in as\n  several people. Own argv: proofs taking slug/key positionals, vcs-time-mirror, new-item-fields.\n- Own polling: audit-proof waitForRows (Node-side predicate), comment-links waitForInView.\n- One-line until bindings carrying a failure description: browser-plugin-columns,\n  browser-contributed-modes, browser-second-review, plugin-management.\n- automations-runs uses openRule (it reads the run chip first); automations-coverage keeps its\n  palette probe; automations-editor its clickText and context-menu probes.\n- browser-autocomplete and import-author serve their own bundles, not the built SPA; the four\n  planning proofs keep their own /settings and /stats matchers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ\n(cherry picked from commit 981b2a4bddde2c7ae578f2954e7bd324ac31f237)","tree":{"sha":"0bbdaafeade52ba01fda431cac2a37324572057b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/0bbdaafeade52ba01fda431cac2a37324572057b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/9b0eec591dfb986bd7ce85fc35e7a39bbdb35744","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/9b0eec591dfb986bd7ce85fc35e7a39bbdb35744","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDliMGVlYzU5MWRmYjk4NmJkN2NlODVmYzM1ZTdhMzliYmRiMzU3NDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/c62ce12509b6476c42eea42fb8bd3dd861228cef","sha":"c62ce12509b6476c42eea42fb8bd3dd861228cef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/c62ce12509b6476c42eea42fb8bd3dd861228cef"}],"sha":"9b0eec591dfb986bd7ce85fc35e7a39bbdb35744","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/9b0eec591dfb986bd7ce85fc35e7a39bbdb35744"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/c62ce12509b6476c42eea42fb8bd3dd861228cef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T23:50:41Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T07:54:24Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1407] Backend tests share one db fixture and user/project factories, and lose dead helpers and narrated docstrings\n\n- conftest.py holds the one rollback-only `db` fixture, replacing 166 per-file\n  copies (164 `db`, and the `db_session` copies in test_slq/test_scoped_settings)\n  plus test_page_external_identity''s, which never disposed its engine. The 19\n  deviant fixtures (Baseline stripped, commit+cleanup, seeded worlds) stay local.\n- tests/_factories.py: `make_user` / `make_project`, with conftest `admin` and an\n  `actor` alias. 45 user helpers and 18 project helpers are gone, their 365\n  call sites calling the factory. 36 admin/actor fixtures fall through to\n  conftest; 16 fixtures whose name a test reads keep a one-line local body.\n  Kept: helpers imported by other test modules, and helpers that compute a name\n  or email from their argument.\n- Deleted: tests/_events.py (no importer ever), test_permission_scope_contract''s\n  `_UNPOPULATED` and `_rendered_scopes`, and test_event_payloads'' `NOT_ITEM_SCOPED`.\n  Also every ruff F401/F811/F841/B007 finding in tests and scripts.\n- Docstrings: function docstrings over 5 lines 161 -> 0; module docstrings\n  over 10 lines 95 -> 12, and the 12 kept are script usage docs and spec\n  tables. Every trap is kept; history narration and references to deleted code\n  are cut (SETTINGS_REGISTRY, demo scripts, instance_status, the receipt\n  template, \"65 triggers\").\n\nTest IDs are identical before and after (3,238 collected). Full suite: 1 failed,\n3233 passed, 4 skipped, the same as the untouched tree. The one failure,\ntest_client_scope_audit (web/src layout.tsx:82), predates this change.\n\n225 files changed, 1795 insertions(+), 6690 deletions(-)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ\n(cherry picked from commit 5facd99404ce3bbe6cea8c35eaa4a1f113fc2e5a)","tree":{"sha":"46aa780e6d2a7883a91f2ebb64d7baca4a884d40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/46aa780e6d2a7883a91f2ebb64d7baca4a884d40"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/c62ce12509b6476c42eea42fb8bd3dd861228cef","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/c62ce12509b6476c42eea42fb8bd3dd861228cef","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKGM2MmNlMTI1MDliNjQ3NmM0MmVlYTQyZmI4YmQzZGQ4NjEyMjhjZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/95bdbae8a8b97cd0518dd5bba3236d583dd036cc","sha":"95bdbae8a8b97cd0518dd5bba3236d583dd036cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/95bdbae8a8b97cd0518dd5bba3236d583dd036cc"}],"sha":"c62ce12509b6476c42eea42fb8bd3dd861228cef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/c62ce12509b6476c42eea42fb8bd3dd861228cef"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/95bdbae8a8b97cd0518dd5bba3236d583dd036cc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T23:22:29Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T07:54:24Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1423] perfseed runs on a head database again\n\nThe seeder had drifted from the schema in five places, so it failed partway\non any database at head:\n- project_members was dropped by d929grants (RADD-929): membership is now a\n  Member grant scoped to the project (global_role_grants), and the VACUUM list\n  names global_role_grants instead;\n- states.category_key is NOT NULL: filled with the category (the builtin\n  vocabulary keys equal the categories);\n- teams.source and team_members.source no longer exist;\n- comments are polymorphic: entity_type=''item'' + entity_id replace item_id, in\n  the COPY and in the search_index comment aggregate.\nAlso the five B007/F841 findings and the unread TARGET_TYPE_NAMES constant.\n\nProof: a throwaway database (radd_perfseed_t) migrated to head with builtin\nroles, 12 users and the env storage host; before, the run died on the states\ninsert (category_key NOT NULL); after, `perfseed.py --scale 0.001 --yes`\ncommits 82 projects, 503 items, 1,796 comments, 94 attachments, 1,090\nproject-scoped Member grants and VACUUMs every table.\n\nNot fixed here: the synthetic item events still carry the pre-RADD-922\ntop-level payload (no payload[\"item\"], no `changes` on item.updated), so\nhistory/reports built from them read an old shape.\n\n1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ\n(cherry picked from commit 317f590a0130e0141dbf252b24cb9576d6adce6f)","tree":{"sha":"647235d703a51f2fa5219f05a6504f018857f1ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/647235d703a51f2fa5219f05a6504f018857f1ed"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/95bdbae8a8b97cd0518dd5bba3236d583dd036cc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/95bdbae8a8b97cd0518dd5bba3236d583dd036cc","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDk1YmRiYWU4YThiOTdjZDA1MThkZDViYmEzMjM2ZDU4M2RkMDM2Y2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/18115047d7a326032a554defc470a83e34340610","sha":"18115047d7a326032a554defc470a83e34340610","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/18115047d7a326032a554defc470a83e34340610"}],"sha":"95bdbae8a8b97cd0518dd5bba3236d583dd036cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/95bdbae8a8b97cd0518dd5bba3236d583dd036cc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/18115047d7a326032a554defc470a83e34340610/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T23:15:25Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T07:54:24Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1406] Importers, directory, AI and connectors lose their dead code, duplicate helpers and history narration\n\nBloat audit D1/D2 (epic RADD-1402), behaviour-neutral:\n\n- jiraimport: the pre-rebuild remnants go — /jira/preview now only counts\n  the JQL (the UI reads `total` alone; infer_schema, the createmeta\n  option-set download and the preview field schemas are deleted, the\n  inference tests now pin ProfileAccumulator), issuemap''s unread decode\n  (kind/category/reporter/people, the fallback-domain synthesis), unread\n  InboundProfile fields and the /resolution fetch, dead enum members,\n  NOISE_SCHEMA_KEYS, UNCHANGED_CREDENTIAL; FieldMapping folds into\n  FieldMappingEntry, provision states/issue types and run cycles/releases\n  share one find-or-create each, sprint/epic field ids live in schemakeys.\n- confluenceimport: dead client methods and value-object fields, enum\n  members, read_manifest, re-exports, PlanOptions.history_limit; rollback\n  uses ledger.records_for; one attachment-image path, one restriction walk,\n  one depth-param builder.\n- ldap/sso: one first_value and one paged service-account search, one\n  failed-import outcome, one usable-provider filter.\n- ai: the service.py facade (status() moves to features), never-firing\n  ImportError guards, single-image content builders, three SSE framings\n  (now ai/sse.py), two JSON extractors (provider.first_json), rerank\n  validation, two embed loops, the three nodes'' include schema / time /\n  feature preflight / structured ask (automation_context), SettingSpec\n  repetition (_toggle).\n- vcs/connectors/alertmanager: the four key grammars and PlannedLink\n  (vcs/keys.py), PrStatus/MrStatus (vcs.types.RefStatus), GitHub''s dead\n  CiState, unread event kinds, verify_signature aliases, _emit''s unused\n  reads, PUSH_COMMIT_LIMIT, the optional ci_completed branch.\n- Docstrings/comments trimmed to the current rule and its traps; stale ones\n  corrected. A GitLab timelog docstring and its test no longer name the\n  owner''s employer.\n\nSchemas, settings specs and trigger catalogs were compared before/after and\nare identical. Only log wording in the AI nodes'' preflight changed.\n\n142 files changed, 1603 insertions(+), 4204 deletions(-)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ\n(cherry picked from commit 5f97a3f9f064e0c1c857c0d2030abb8979847995)","tree":{"sha":"27a870249c0bb2347b302f946f23073b950ebe98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/27a870249c0bb2347b302f946f23073b950ebe98"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/18115047d7a326032a554defc470a83e34340610","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/18115047d7a326032a554defc470a83e34340610","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDE4MTE1MDQ3ZDdhMzI2MDMyYTU1NGRlZmM0NzBhODNlMzQzNDA2MTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/79c108c52530adfdf8bd3e740a423fb1d93b9a2a","sha":"79c108c52530adfdf8bd3e740a423fb1d93b9a2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/79c108c52530adfdf8bd3e740a423fb1d93b9a2a"}],"sha":"18115047d7a326032a554defc470a83e34340610","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/18115047d7a326032a554defc470a83e34340610"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/79c108c52530adfdf8bd3e740a423fb1d93b9a2a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:25:05Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T07:54:24Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1419] The provider Test button sends the row''s reasoning preference and extra parameters\n\nThe probe built its ResolvedModel from wire shape, URL, key and model only,\nso every Test sent reasoning OFF (chat_template_kwargs.enable_thinking=false)\nand none of the admin''s request_params; a provider that rejects the thinking\nflag kept failing Test after the admin turned reasoning ON.\nregistry.resolved_from_row(row, model) is now the one builder: resolve_role\nand the probe both call it, which also merges their two copies of the LOCAL\ndefault-model fallback. test_ai_registry drives the probe route through a\nmock transport and checks the payload.\n\n3 files changed, 50 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ\n(cherry picked from commit 3a3d099edb7d1123f9ef2629770a74d403f682fd)","tree":{"sha":"7f6fe3f3fea8f2079884ab7f9676319415a16e24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/7f6fe3f3fea8f2079884ab7f9676319415a16e24"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/79c108c52530adfdf8bd3e740a423fb1d93b9a2a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/79c108c52530adfdf8bd3e740a423fb1d93b9a2a","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDc5YzEwOGM1MjUzMGFkZmRmOGJkM2U3NDBhNDIzZmIxZDkzYjlhMmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/62efa6a87bc4ab1f0a74f991ac8e545426ec20a6","sha":"62efa6a87bc4ab1f0a74f991ac8e545426ec20a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/62efa6a87bc4ab1f0a74f991ac8e545426ec20a6"}],"sha":"79c108c52530adfdf8bd3e740a423fb1d93b9a2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/79c108c52530adfdf8bd3e740a423fb1d93b9a2a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/62efa6a87bc4ab1f0a74f991ac8e545426ec20a6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:22:55Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T07:54:24Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1418] The AI nodes'' \"Logged time\" section carries the item''s logged time\n\nautomation_context._worklog_line passed the project id where\ntimelogging.item_summary takes a project, and read total_seconds where the\nfield is logged_seconds; the AttributeError was swallowed, so the section\nalways read \"not tracked\" on ai.classify, ai.validate and ai.generate. It\nnow reuses summarize._worklog_digest (totals, per-person split, newest\nentries), and like Summarize it adds no line when the project does not\ntrack time or nothing is logged.\ntest_ai_automation_context logs 1h30m on an item and finds the total in\nthe prompt.\n\n2 files changed, 57 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ\n(cherry picked from commit 0a1ced197722eadc5e12960855a60235503aa28c)","tree":{"sha":"1bd6595fe618527aed5ca9b64b427c3dbfc33c98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/1bd6595fe618527aed5ca9b64b427c3dbfc33c98"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/62efa6a87bc4ab1f0a74f991ac8e545426ec20a6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/62efa6a87bc4ab1f0a74f991ac8e545426ec20a6","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDYyZWZhNmE4N2JjNGFiMWYwYTc0Zjk5MWFjOGU1NDU0MjZlYzIwYTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/f24026c4c0d49fe518c59566359454141b1aa753","sha":"f24026c4c0d49fe518c59566359454141b1aa753","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/f24026c4c0d49fe518c59566359454141b1aa753"}],"sha":"62efa6a87bc4ab1f0a74f991ac8e545426ec20a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/62efa6a87bc4ab1f0a74f991ac8e545426ec20a6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/f24026c4c0d49fe518c59566359454141b1aa753/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:20:54Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T07:54:24Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1417] A Confluence rollback removes the restriction grants its import wrote\n\nThe run recorded the PAGE id as every GRANT ledger row''s entity_id, so\nrollback''s DELETE FROM access_grants WHERE id = <page id> matched nothing\nand imported restrictions outlived the rollback. restrictions.apply now\nreturns the grant ids it wrote and the run records those.\ntest_confluence_run imports a restricted page, rolls back, and finds no\ngrant left on it.\n\n3 files changed, 41 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ\n(cherry picked from commit 84f83f0df6a1f50d2da0a55ccb908499acebd4eb)","tree":{"sha":"e6a878f3324efc254692dbe5ec5f058984fcebc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/e6a878f3324efc254692dbe5ec5f058984fcebc1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/f24026c4c0d49fe518c59566359454141b1aa753","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/f24026c4c0d49fe518c59566359454141b1aa753","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKGYyNDAyNmM0YzBkNDlmZTUxOGM1OTU2NjM1OTQ1NDE0MWIxYWE3NTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/e23f1bdff70e0eb3a2f9cecf8fc6fa0f5eba3dc3","sha":"e23f1bdff70e0eb3a2f9cecf8fc6fa0f5eba3dc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/e23f1bdff70e0eb3a2f9cecf8fc6fa0f5eba3dc3"}],"sha":"f24026c4c0d49fe518c59566359454141b1aa753","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/f24026c4c0d49fe518c59566359454141b1aa753"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/e23f1bdff70e0eb3a2f9cecf8fc6fa0f5eba3dc3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:19:26Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T07:54:24Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1416] A directory sign-in leaves the instance role alone when no admin groups are configured\n\nldap.service.provision wrote instance_role on every login, so with\nldap_admin_groups empty every admin signing in through AD was demoted to\nmember. It now re-syncs the role only when admin groups are configured,\nmatching sso.service._syncs_roles and the setting''s own description.\ntest_ldap covers both sides; test_event_reach''s promotion case now\nconfigures an admin group, since a promotion needs one.\n\n3 files changed, 49 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ\n(cherry picked from commit 19e20e0ab33d2333689212447317af694d2cb70d)","tree":{"sha":"f8ef48adea06c1157585839e66035a28ab2dc5fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/f8ef48adea06c1157585839e66035a28ab2dc5fb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/e23f1bdff70e0eb3a2f9cecf8fc6fa0f5eba3dc3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/e23f1bdff70e0eb3a2f9cecf8fc6fa0f5eba3dc3","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKGUyM2YxYmRmZjcwZTBlYjNhMmY5Y2VjZjhmYzZmYTBmNWViYTNkYzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/b1e8e321b7b2eaefd4c1a85d8df67ac1c5dc7cf7","sha":"b1e8e321b7b2eaefd4c1a85d8df67ac1c5dc7cf7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/b1e8e321b7b2eaefd4c1a85d8df67ac1c5dc7cf7"}],"sha":"e23f1bdff70e0eb3a2f9cecf8fc6fa0f5eba3dc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/e23f1bdff70e0eb3a2f9cecf8fc6fa0f5eba3dc3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/b1e8e321b7b2eaefd4c1a85d8df67ac1c5dc7cf7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:59:26Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T07:54:24Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1405] Service-desk, mail, pages and notify backends shed dead code, duplicate helpers and history narration\n\nApplies audits C1/C2 to automations, scripts, approvals, slas, forms, csat,\nnotify, mailintake, pages, collab and attachments (backend only):\n- DELETE: ScheduleConfig, TYPE_VALIDATION_FAIL/UNIVERSAL_ACTIONS/ITEM_ACTIONS,\n  gates.state_category_is, conditions._change_*, templating.render_template,\n  executor re-exports/RunBudget.exhausted/UNSPOKEN_FINDING, engine''s planning\n  re-exports, Node.ports, validation.scope_of, the Finding.mode fallback,\n  scripts.fallback_python, slas.service.ordered, providers.RawMessage/MailSource,\n  notify.default_email_types, pages.spaces.list_spaces, CollabEntity,\n  attachments._shutdown, unread parameters, and the `except ImportError`\n  guards around core modules.\n- REDUNDANT: mailintake imports notify''s mailable_user; one drop_restricted\n  filter in page_access; notify''s default-kind sets move into the tests as\n  oracles; shared helpers for the notify item prologue, slas matched-policy\n  evaluation, automations SLQ compilation, run recording and plan entries,\n  approvals electorates/summary, attachments purge, pages snapshots/bulk\n  loops/ancestor walks; forwarders and shims removed.\n- TRIM: module, class and function docstrings and comments cut to the why and\n  the traps; stale references to deleted code fixed.\nNo routes, responses or events change. Two tests that only covered deleted\nhelpers are gone; the rest of the suite is unchanged.\n\n197 files changed, 2768 insertions(+), 7978 deletions(-)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ\n(cherry picked from commit 601b29c8353b55d9a4efcc70509ab1e69dff6cdb)","tree":{"sha":"b75847761e9e4d8646d2f4798ab71e7f3d3d4e57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/b75847761e9e4d8646d2f4798ab71e7f3d3d4e57"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/b1e8e321b7b2eaefd4c1a85d8df67ac1c5dc7cf7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/b1e8e321b7b2eaefd4c1a85d8df67ac1c5dc7cf7","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKGIxZThlMzIxYjdiMmVhZWZkNGMxYTg1ZDhkZjY3YWMxYzVkYzdjZjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/3947ea2b8220bd02e9bc6eb8557420af40b5b628","sha":"3947ea2b8220bd02e9bc6eb8557420af40b5b628","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/3947ea2b8220bd02e9bc6eb8557420af40b5b628"}],"sha":"b1e8e321b7b2eaefd4c1a85d8df67ac1c5dc7cf7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/b1e8e321b7b2eaefd4c1a85d8df67ac1c5dc7cf7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/3947ea2b8220bd02e9bc6eb8557420af40b5b628/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:19:38Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T07:54:24Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1415] The label index keys its readability filter on the page id its rows carry\n\n`drop_restricted_labelled` read `row.page_id` off `PageLabelled` rows, which\nonly have `id`, so `GET /pages/by-label/{name}` raised AttributeError (a 500)\nwhenever the label had a page in a readable space. It now keys on `id`. The\nnew route test labels an open page, a page-restricted page and a page in a\nspace the reader cannot open, and expects a 200 with only the open one.\n\n2 files changed, 45 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ\n(cherry picked from commit b514e42fa3bba7b69bd56f3691987c4d0052971c)","tree":{"sha":"307fea44b8d25db5f9cab150c4889ff0617437d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/307fea44b8d25db5f9cab150c4889ff0617437d5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/3947ea2b8220bd02e9bc6eb8557420af40b5b628","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/3947ea2b8220bd02e9bc6eb8557420af40b5b628","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDM5NDdlYTJiODIyMGJkMDJlOWJjNmViODU1NzQyMGFmNDBiNWI2Mjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/f322c5e2bd4bd9e77df25265afa24a3c6611159b","sha":"f322c5e2bd4bd9e77df25265afa24a3c6611159b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/f322c5e2bd4bd9e77df25265afa24a3c6611159b"}],"sha":"3947ea2b8220bd02e9bc6eb8557420af40b5b628","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/3947ea2b8220bd02e9bc6eb8557420af40b5b628"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/f322c5e2bd4bd9e77df25265afa24a3c6611159b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:58:07Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T07:54:24Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1404] The work modules drop dead helpers, duplicated preambles and narrated docstrings without changing behaviour\n\nThe B1/B2 bloat audit applied to items, views, workflow, fields, comments,\nparticipants, weblinks, linktypes, labels, auth, projects, teams, groups,\ncycles, releases, milestones, itemtypes, timelogging, leave, reporting and\ndashboards (never their ui/).\n\nRemoved (dead): linktypes resolve_by_name/is_auto_managed,\nitems item_ids_for_projects, fields FieldSubject/FieldAccess, auth\ncheckable_at/_CHECKABLE_WIDENINGS, _DescriptionCatalog/PERMISSION_DESCRIPTIONS,\nIMPLIED_PERMISSIONS, user_for_session_token, service_accounts.list_accounts and\nthe private facade re-exports, cycles active_cycles/visible_cycles/the stale\n__all__ and list_cycles'' unused status filter, worklog_field_names,\nreporting item_state_timeline, dashboards/views list_* forwarders, discarded\nget_project lookups, never-read parameters (_validate_edge exclude_id,\n_emit share_count) and unreachable branches.\n\nConsolidated (redundant): one row-gated item-permission preamble\n(require_item_permission) and one SLQ compile/scoping path in items; the /items\nfilter params as one dependency named by ItemFilterParam; the SLQ named-relation\nand bool compilers; grants'' project/space query pairs, token minting, the\ngrant-delegate check and atom validators in auth; team member/group writes;\nthe worklog-SLQ compile and \"whose time may I see\" rule in timelogging;\nreport timeline assembly; dashboard widget row writes; plus the smaller\nper-module copies the audit listed.\n\nTrimmed: history narration, restated docs and ~40 comments/docstrings that\nhad become wrong (Baseline atoms, admin/member/viewer, view_shares, the\nparticipants reporter gate, model_fields_set claims, dead file references).\n\nNo route, parameter set, response, event or MCP input schema changes (OpenAPI\nand MCP schemas compared before/after; /items lists its filter params in a\ndifferent order).\n\n211 files changed, 2356 insertions(+), 5602 deletions(-)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ\n(cherry picked from commit ef3290099a31e665ab1e883e3b2289bed9dedbe3)","tree":{"sha":"e14ed6ba323d88ab585a70a565c70180bef528d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/e14ed6ba323d88ab585a70a565c70180bef528d3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/f322c5e2bd4bd9e77df25265afa24a3c6611159b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/f322c5e2bd4bd9e77df25265afa24a3c6611159b","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKGYzMjJjNWUyYmQ0YmQ5ZTc3ZGYyNTI2NWFmYTI0YTNjNjYxMTE1OWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/84d3f37fcbf82a6c01c6988142f8415cc8788709","sha":"84d3f37fcbf82a6c01c6988142f8415cc8788709","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/84d3f37fcbf82a6c01c6988142f8415cc8788709"}],"sha":"f322c5e2bd4bd9e77df25265afa24a3c6611159b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/f322c5e2bd4bd9e77df25265afa24a3c6611159b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/84d3f37fcbf82a6c01c6988142f8415cc8788709/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:22:23Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T07:54:23Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1414] A webhook payload withholds email_signature when the description is read-restricted\n\nThe API read blanks `description` AND `email_signature` for an actor without a\nread grant on description; the webhook redactor kept a hand-copied \"dict-level\nmirror\" that blanked only `description`, so a receiver still got the signature\ntext. The blank map now lives once in the pure items/redaction.py\n(BLANK_BUILTIN: restricted field -> the attributes it blanks) and both\nvisibility._filter_read and redact_item_payload read it. Test in\ntest_outbound_redaction.py fails before and passes after.\n\n3 files changed, 32 insertions(+), 37 deletions(-)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ\n(cherry picked from commit 48298538d552bc47f7facad9800ee8da341098f5)","tree":{"sha":"21362bc2db3af6441683ccf8f7c10ce39d5e59bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/21362bc2db3af6441683ccf8f7c10ce39d5e59bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/84d3f37fcbf82a6c01c6988142f8415cc8788709","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/84d3f37fcbf82a6c01c6988142f8415cc8788709","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDg0ZDNmMzdmY2JmODJhNmMwMWM2OTg4MTQyZjg0MTVjYzg3ODg3MDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/a2ea5a4b68a56fa89f92581280b7dab711ef0296","sha":"a2ea5a4b68a56fa89f92581280b7dab711ef0296","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/a2ea5a4b68a56fa89f92581280b7dab711ef0296"}],"sha":"84d3f37fcbf82a6c01c6988142f8415cc8788709","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/84d3f37fcbf82a6c01c6988142f8415cc8788709"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/a2ea5a4b68a56fa89f92581280b7dab711ef0296/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:20:43Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T07:54:23Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1413] Item links and stars go through the row gate every other item write uses\n\nadd_item_link/remove_item_link now call ensure_item_relation after the\nproject-level item.update check, so an @own writer (or a relation-qualified\nscoped key, and the MCP link_items/unlink_items tools that inherit this) can no\nlonger link from or unlink someone else''s item. star_item/unstar_item resolve\nthrough require_readable_item instead of a project-only item.read check, so\nunstar on a hidden item 404s like a missing one (it answered 204: an existence\noracle) and star leaves no row behind. Tests in test_item_relations.py fail\nbefore and pass after.\n\n3 files changed, 42 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ\n(cherry picked from commit 95778bd39552415ddd2fa634db73b9caa24280cc)","tree":{"sha":"4a3b0f09d6631f2fc070a93ffb5a49d223fac5ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/4a3b0f09d6631f2fc070a93ffb5a49d223fac5ce"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/a2ea5a4b68a56fa89f92581280b7dab711ef0296","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/a2ea5a4b68a56fa89f92581280b7dab711ef0296","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKGEyZWE1YTRiNjhhNTZmYTg5ZjkyNTgxMjgwYjdkYWI3MTFlZjAyOTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/3b05a926dab2b5401971316306c0764223445f55","sha":"3b05a926dab2b5401971316306c0764223445f55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/3b05a926dab2b5401971316306c0764223445f55"}],"sha":"a2ea5a4b68a56fa89f92581280b7dab711ef0296","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/a2ea5a4b68a56fa89f92581280b7dab711ef0296"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/3b05a926dab2b5401971316306c0764223445f55/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:55:55Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T07:54:23Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1409] The SDK, the plugin UIs and their packaging lose their dead code, copies and narration\n\nBloat audit F + G (epic RADD-1402), applied to web/packages/plugin-sdk, every\nmodules/*/ui package, the shared shims and the federation scripts:\n- SDK: one bridged() factory for 37 host bridges; slots.tsx uses the SDK Switch and one\n  changed() cache reset; metaContribution/ownedMetaId for the namespaced contributions; the\n  three paged-directory copies run on usePagedDirectory; optionTransport(path) replaces\n  twelve hand-written /<resource>/options transports; the dead sidebar.nav/item.action slot\n  ids, the never-provided SchemaForm override and three index leaks are gone.\n- Packaging: every plugin tsconfig extends @radd/plugin-sdk/tsconfig.plugin.json; the unused\n  react/jsx-dev-runtime and react-dom/client shims leave all four synced lists (the boundary\n  test now refuses a stale shim); unused build scripts and a repeated vite comment go.\n- Plugin UIs: the drifted copies (ai ReadMenu -> AiResultsBody, automations CheckField x7 and\n  reachable() x4, pages PageLinkList x4 and threadFor x3, jira Panel/StatusText) consolidated;\n  dead exports, props and files removed; history narration trimmed, traps kept.\n\n375 files changed, 1955 insertions(+), 5369 deletions(-)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ\n(cherry picked from commit 79db136265b5c9aa3e3d8db6b04bebab68450389)","tree":{"sha":"1b70ed87c89dfd7e7998ec91006914efc47ed6f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/1b70ed87c89dfd7e7998ec91006914efc47ed6f4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/3b05a926dab2b5401971316306c0764223445f55","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/3b05a926dab2b5401971316306c0764223445f55","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDNiMDVhOTI2ZGFiMmI1NDAxOTcxMzE2MzA2YzA3NjQyMjM0NDVmNTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/7a731de2118f7aa04a884d76914f896ddacbe908","sha":"7a731de2118f7aa04a884d76914f896ddacbe908","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/7a731de2118f7aa04a884d76914f896ddacbe908"}],"sha":"3b05a926dab2b5401971316306c0764223445f55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/3b05a926dab2b5401971316306c0764223445f55"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/7a731de2118f7aa04a884d76914f896ddacbe908/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:26:59Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T07:54:23Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1422] Plugin admin pages ask the SDK''s useIsInstanceAdmin, which reads the credential-aware role\n\nFive plugin pages (Settings -> AI, the Jira and Confluence importers, Directory, the leave\nholidays section) gated on `me.instance_role === \"admin\"`, the account''s column, while the\nSDK''s usePermissions and the host read `global_role`, what authz.is_admin answers for the\ncredential. The two can disagree, so a page could offer what its API refuses or hide what\nit allows. The SDK now exports useIsInstanceAdmin() over the one predicate usePermissions\nuses; the five pages call it and their local \"admin\" constants go. The shared SDK shim is\nregenerated, and plugin-boundaries.test.mjs refuses any `instance_role` read in a plugin UI\n(it lists the five sites on the pre-fix tree).\n\n11 files changed, 41 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ\n(cherry picked from commit 74b0dc5fce2a63dac1106c4e649eea7c6d6e8fb9)","tree":{"sha":"beccaeea9daf5fc5a54f26de1d88702f2c681fe7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/beccaeea9daf5fc5a54f26de1d88702f2c681fe7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/7a731de2118f7aa04a884d76914f896ddacbe908","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/7a731de2118f7aa04a884d76914f896ddacbe908","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDdhNzMxZGUyMTE4ZjdhYTA0YTg4NGQ3NjkxNGY4OTZkZGFjYmU5MDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/702817d4702fc880a4b6356a0b5a808d7f27647e","sha":"702817d4702fc880a4b6356a0b5a808d7f27647e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/702817d4702fc880a4b6356a0b5a808d7f27647e"}],"sha":"7a731de2118f7aa04a884d76914f896ddacbe908","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/7a731de2118f7aa04a884d76914f896ddacbe908"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/702817d4702fc880a4b6356a0b5a808d7f27647e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:24:19Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T07:54:23Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1421] Print with subpages lists pages in the tree''s order, through the one tree-walk helper\n\nThe print view carried its own descendants walk with no sibling sort, so \"print with\nsubpages\" followed the server''s (position, title) order while the rail, radd:toc and\nradd:children natural-sort. view/page-tree.ts now holds comparePagesNaturally, buildTree,\ndescendants, subtreeIds and ancestorIds; the print view, the two extension blocks, the rail\n(its tree, filter chain and selected-page trail), Move to... and the archive browser''s\n\"hidden below\" count all walk through it. Every walk is bounded against a bad row.\n\nweb/scripts/page-tree.test.mjs pins the natural order, print == rail order, the bounds, and\nthat no pages file keeps a private walk (fails on the pre-fix tree).\n\n7 files changed, 192 insertions(+), 163 deletions(-)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ\n(cherry picked from commit 788274cdbf877366dc95d6e066a0c3fb20caf9c5)","tree":{"sha":"6487a1217ad17fec26b320767f9a0b8f33455c85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/6487a1217ad17fec26b320767f9a0b8f33455c85"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/702817d4702fc880a4b6356a0b5a808d7f27647e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/702817d4702fc880a4b6356a0b5a808d7f27647e","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDcwMjgxN2Q0NzAyZmM4ODBhNGI2MzU2YTBiNWE4MDhkN2YyNzY0N2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/3e308331832e69c8b028d3007a1e4782a9167f3d","sha":"3e308331832e69c8b028d3007a1e4782a9167f3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/3e308331832e69c8b028d3007a1e4782a9167f3d"}],"sha":"702817d4702fc880a4b6356a0b5a808d7f27647e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/702817d4702fc880a4b6356a0b5a808d7f27647e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/3e308331832e69c8b028d3007a1e4782a9167f3d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:53:36Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T07:54:23Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1408] The host SPA sheds its dead code, duplicate helpers and narrated comments\n\nThe E1/E2 bloat audit applied to web/src, with no behaviour change:\n\n- Dead: roleGrantsQuery, the unpaged service-account/team/child/comment\n  queries and their keys, usePluginEnabled, selectableCycles,\n  compareChildrenOpenFirst, six request/response types nothing sends, 13\n  Permission members never read, the view sharing/transfer paths, sameLabel,\n  getDensity, the list form of a settings tab''s `plugin`, PlanningFields,\n  TeamChoices, RoadmapModel.unscheduled, the toolbar snapshot''s inTable/empty,\n  orphaned comments, and the web client''s `live_supported` plugin field (the\n  server stopped sending it).\n- One copy each: useIntakeVerdict, useImageUploader, one PersonPicker,\n  LabelChips'' quiet variant, nodeText, useDeflection, useNearViewport,\n  usePointAnchoredPanel/useAnchoredCardPosition, useUrlChipSet, the\n  roadmap''s cascade block and blocks-edge walk, groupByRef, one\n  provideHostComponents call. The view page''s duplicate \"Project reports\"\n  entry in the ⋯ menu is gone: the header''s Reports link (RADD-1290) is the\n  same destination under the same condition.\n- Trimmed history narration and restatement in comments across editor/,\n  roadmap/, items/, lib/, routes/, settings/, shell/ and index.css; every\n  trap stays. About 190 symbols used only in their own file lose `export`.\n- audit-regressions.test.mjs proves comment invalidation on the thread''s\n  real feed query instead of the deleted commentsQuery.\n\ngit diff --shortstat: 211 files changed, 1662 insertions(+), 4126 deletions(-)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ\n(cherry picked from commit 4a791e1dcad931ce81404164781e483c19e9e186)","tree":{"sha":"6a06d31abe07ea4569470684d8251319dc501a9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/6a06d31abe07ea4569470684d8251319dc501a9e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/3e308331832e69c8b028d3007a1e4782a9167f3d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committ