//api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/f09bea5a326dfd4e529e6c1dbe25cce3f1f59aef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:19:39Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T07:54:23Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1420] A pinned wiki page takes the wiki icon: the pins bar keys on the pages plugin''s own route\n\nLINK_ICONS still keyed the wiki on \"/docs\", a prefix no route has had since spec 124 moved it to\n/pages, so every pinned page fell through to the generic link icon. It now keys on\nPageRoute.pages from @radd-plugin-ui/pages/links, the constant the router mounts, so the next\nmove of that route carries the icon with it.\n\nTest: pin-icons.test.mjs (handed to the orchestrator; web/scripts is outside this area) fails\nbefore (Link2) and passes after (BookOpen).\n\n 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ\n(cherry picked from commit 0d202e5070a17440a88534bf78270c91196558d0)","tree":{"sha":"3610f47eba9a31e22010447340409464014ddc26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/3610f47eba9a31e22010447340409464014ddc26"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/f09bea5a326dfd4e529e6c1dbe25cce3f1f59aef","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"http