tps://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/6191924173d2d0b905a2d0e59a81bfbbfa189e33/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:42:24Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T07:54:23Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1403] The kernel, spine and infra modules shed dead code, duplicated helpers and history-heavy comments\n\nRemoved (nothing referenced them): SETTINGS_REGISTRY/_SettingCatalog; pluginmgr\nlive_supported, live.supported() and live.stop(); the smtp env-config fallback\n(config is now required: its one caller always passed it); the Notifier and\nAttachmentFilter socket Protocols; TaskBackend/LocalLoopBackend.enqueue;\nEntitySpec.activity; IntegrationSpec.consumes; backup list_runs; the install()\nbranch for a stored ERRORED row; realtime InvalidationEvent.silent; the retired\n`module:` export fallbacks in the loader and discovery; search.looks_like_key;\nMcpMethod.INITIALIZED; mcp PAGE_TOOLS/include_pages/pages_available (absent\nspecs already drop out of build_catalog); app.state.plugin_runtime.\n\nConsolidated, same behaviour: table-driven KernelRegistries register/unregister\nwith clear() over dataclass fields; one exception-handler loop in app.py; backup\nread models via from_attributes; PluginRead(**asdict(info)); one \"Required by\"\nguard; one schedule field table; search _scoped() and a single public\nreadable_project_ids; an indexer _tsv() helper (SQL byte-identical); access\n_actor_context and one subject loop; mcp _require_mcp_user; screens _field_rows;\nthe audit MCP schema on kernel.mcptools constants and EventSource; radd.clock.utcnow\nfor two private copies; deferred registries imports hoisted; ports_at merged.\n\nTrimmed: comments and docstrings across kernel/, radd/*.py and the fifteen\nmodules. History, narration and restatement are cut; traps and the non-obvious\nreasons stay.\n\n90 files changed, 1022 insertions(+), 2863 deletions(-)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ\n(cherry picked from commit 805f894e1f73e44e5ae254b4eedd50a18a6d959d)","tree":{"sha":"e3555447029ea1b58a43eb7bcae3046e2b876769","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/e3555447029ea1b58a43eb7bcae3046e2b876769"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/6191924173d2d0b905a2d0e59a81bfbbfa189e33","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/6191924173d2d0b905a2d0e59a81bfbbfa189e33","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDYxOTE5MjQxNzNkMmQwYjkwNWEyZDBlNTlhODFiZmJiZmExODllMzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/82dc347af524b9d39ef587d9e036ded0f9619d33","sha":"82dc347af524b9d39ef587d9e036ded0f9619d33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/82dc347af524b9d39ef587d9e036ded0f9619d33"}],"sha":"6191924173d2d0b905a2d0e59a81bfbbfa189e33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/6191924173d2d0b905a2d0e59a81bfbbfa189e33"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/82dc347af524b9d39ef587d9e036ded0f9619d33/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:23:24Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:26:14Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1412] Generated, machine-local and session-only files are ignored, and a local image build no longer copies server/.env\n\nThe repo-hygiene audit (research/bloat-audit-2026-09-27) found nothing\ntracked that should not be, no secrets in the tree or in history, and\nthree gaps in what is ignored:\n\n- docs/campaigns/ and docs/tutorials/ hold 2.7 GB of untracked generated\n  video (zips up to 990 MB, which GitHub refuses); nothing ignored them, so\n  one ''git add docs'' would have staged all of it. Ignored, with *.mp4,\n  *.mov, *.webm and *.zip as a backstop.\n- 17 proofs write their screenshot into web/scripts/ (23 PNGs, 8.5 MB,\n  untracked); **/scripts/*.png ignores them, and web/shots/ covers docshot.\n- .dockerignore let a local ''podman build'' copy server/.env (real LDAP and\n  Jira passwords) to /app/server/.env, where config.py reads it at runtime,\n  along with dangling ui/node_modules symlinks, stale ui/dist and web/var.\n  It now excludes **/.env, the regenerated UI dirs, caches, proof output,\n  .claude and .mcp.json. .containerignore was a byte-identical twin that had\n  to be edited in lockstep; podman falls back to .dockerignore.\n\nAlso: *.tsbuildinfo, *.log, coverage, editor dirs and .env.* at the root\n(replacing two nested .gitignore files that only repeated root rules);\nresearch run evidence (json/txt/png) stays local, generalising the\naudit-2026-09-09 rule; a .gitattributes marks the two checked-in generated\nfiles; the Containerfile comment named a workspaces entry that does not\nexist; the example plugin''s .gitignore learns .venv/ for when it is copied\nout as its own repo.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017KNVMcLr1XqtEqBK2LheXQ","tree":{"sha":"06bb782f4ff9e4a5a3bfcc6137f34c061f578cae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/06bb782f4ff9e4a5a3bfcc6137f34c061f578cae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/82dc347af524b9d39ef587d9e036ded0f9619d33","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/82dc347af524b9d39ef587d9e036ded0f9619d33","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDgyZGMzNDdhZjUyNGI5ZDM5ZWY1ODdkOWUwMzZkZWQwZjk2MTlkMzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/3b8121472d457e9931c7f900318aec309f8baf13","sha":"3b8121472d457e9931c7f900318aec309f8baf13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/3b8121472d457e9931c7f900318aec309f8baf13"}],"sha":"82dc347af524b9d39ef587d9e036ded0f9619d33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/82dc347af524b9d39ef587d9e036ded0f9619d33"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/3b8121472d457e9931c7f900318aec309f8baf13/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T20:41:45Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T20:55:19Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1350] The plugin-ownership record is reconciled against the finished tree\n\nresearch/plugin-isolation/README.md is the epic''s record. Its module table is rebuilt from facts\ncomputed over the tree for every module: declared core/optional, where the UI lives\n(bundled/remote/host/contract-only/none), and depends_on. It uses two honest review levels:\n- Reviewed: moved or inverted in this epic, and verified.\n- Guarded: covered by test_module_contracts and plugin-boundaries, but not re-read file by\n  file.\n\nThe stale \"findings still requiring remediation\" section is replaced by what actually remains\nand the justified exceptions:\n- the login page''s SSO/LDAP pieces;\n- notify''s SLA kinds;\n- groups'' audit link;\n- the History tab''s sentences for plugin events.\n\nThe work table now lists RADD-1366 through RADD-1401.\n\nA final sweep of host string literals against every optional plugin''s route words found two\nresidues, which RADD-1401 then removed. What remains is only the named exceptions.\n\nAlso here:\n- CLAUDE.md''s wave narrative gains this wave.\n- remus-reports-proof follows RADD-1287''s \"New issue\" label; it had failed since that rename.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"00d5392ccf8c0915a023f7f1b25a0d117aab3247","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/00d5392ccf8c0915a023f7f1b25a0d117aab3247"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/3b8121472d457e9931c7f900318aec309f8baf13","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/3b8121472d457e9931c7f900318aec309f8baf13","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDNiODEyMTQ3MmQ0NTdlOTkzMWM3ZjkwMDMxOGFlYzMwOWY4YmFmMTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/11c2b15baba2f9c0e5b22d790da8ecad2403daf4","sha":"11c2b15baba2f9c0e5b22d790da8ecad2403daf4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/11c2b15baba2f9c0e5b22d790da8ecad2403daf4"}],"sha":"3b8121472d457e9931c7f900318aec309f8baf13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/3b8121472d457e9931c7f900318aec309f8baf13"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/11c2b15baba2f9c0e5b22d790da8ecad2403daf4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T20:39:45Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T20:40:20Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1401] The public survey page is the csat plugin''s, and a mailed body reads as the mailintake plugin draws it\n\nTwo residues of optional plugins lived in the host: the tokened, unauthenticated\nrating page the survey email links to (routes/public-csat.tsx with its route,\nRoutePath, API path, types, query and key), and EmailBody, which folded a mailed\nbody''s signature and restored it through mailintake''s /mail/signatures route.\nA plugin the host carries cannot be withdrawn by disabling it.\n\nDecision: the survey page MOVES, it is not an exception\n- The two questions that decided it. Can a remote load for an anonymous\n  visitor? Yes, and it already does: /capabilities is an `Actor` route in the\n  frozen anonymous inventory, plugin bundles are static files, and spec 121''s\n  visitor shell already loads every enabled remote for the Anyone principal. So\n  a public page leaks nothing the visitor shell did not, and\n  test_anonymous_surface.py is untouched (no backend change at all). Can a page\n  contribution match a tokened path? Not before this: route.page matched exact\n  pathnames. It now takes patterns, generically.\n- What made it a small change rather than a platform one: the loader is\n  module-level and idempotent, so the public frame just mounts PluginRemotes\n  itself; and ContributedPage already knew how to wait, fail and say\n  \"unavailable\".\n- Why this differs from the login page (RADD-1380): sign-in is the way in and\n  must not wait on, or break with, optional code, so it stays the host''s and\n  still mounts no loader (signin-settings-page-proof re-run: /login loads no\n  remote). The survey page IS csat''s feature: with csat off there is no survey\n  to answer, and the link now says so instead of the host carrying dead code.\n\nWhat changed\n- SDK (UI API 1.19.0): page patterns (`$name` segments capture into `params`;\n  matchPagePath/usePageMatch, ContributedPageProps; a literal match wins); the\n  `public.page` slot; the `content.body` slot with contentBody(spec) and\n  useContentBodyClaim. Shim regenerated.\n- Host: ContributedPage matches by pattern for every page slot (and so does its\n  turned-off check) and renders only the matched owner; a root-level `/public/$`\n  route (beside /login: no shell, no gate) whose frame (PublicPage: brand +\n  reading column) runs the plugin loader and resolves the visitor first, putting\n  the api client in visitor mode so a 401 there is a refusal, never a sign-in\n  redirect. ContentBody draws every description, comment, reply and requester\n  view, unless a plugin claims the record; the claimant draws through the host''s\n  renderText (a leading part keeps its checklist live), and a missing,\n  withdrawn or throwing claimant falls back to the plain viewer.\n- csat remote: the rating page (moved, so git keeps its history) at\n  /public/csat/$token, its wire in survey.ts (query keyed under \"csat\" so\n  withdrawal drops it), toggleable: false. Raw amber/emerald became the status\n  tokens. Manifest ui_api_version 1.19.0.\n- mailintake remote: SignedBody claims records carrying email_signature and\n  owns the restore route. Manifest 1.19.0.\n- Deleted from the host: public-csat.tsx, EmailBody, lib/types/csat.ts\n  (PublicCsat*, and ItemCsat, unused since the chip moved), RoutePath.publicCsat,\n  apiPublicCsatPath, publicCsatQuery, queryKeys.publicCsat, MailContact (unused),\n  email_signature on the host''s Item/Comment/portal types, and the comments\n  that named either plugin.\n\nDecisions on the way\n- Keyed by a CLAIM, not by origin. The brief suggested matching an origin\n  field; there is none on the wire, and the stored comments.origin is NULL for\n  a person''s mailed reply by design (RADD-1318) while items have no origin at\n  all. What marks a mailed body is the signature annotation, which only\n  mailintake knows how to read — so the contribution says which records it\n  claims, and the host names nothing.\n- The Workflow page''s \"When work is done\" note (RADD-1286) named both plugins\n  and sent both settings to General, where neither lives (CSAT''s opt-in is on\n  the SLAs page, the resolution notice on Settings → Email). It stays, since the\n  usability audit checks it, but says generically that automations and plugins\n  act on done, each set up where it lives.\n- One named exception, in the boundary test: the issue History tab still words\n  csat.* and mail.* events. It is a ledger over every plugin''s events\n  (approvals, participants, vcs too) and events outlive their plugin, so this is\n  a cross-plugin mechanism for its own issue, not a csat or mail move. The test\n  fails once the rows are gone, so the exception cannot go stale.\n\nEvidence\n- plugin-boundaries.test.mjs: a new test refuses csat and mail vocabulary —\n  identifiers, literals, JSX copy and comments — across web/src, the SDK and the\n  20 bundled core packages (samples prove the pattern both ways), and asserts\n  the route, frame, pattern matching, ContentBody at all four call sites, both\n  contributions, both endpoints and both manifests. node --test\n  web/scripts/*.test.mjs: 100/100.\n- browser-csat-mail-contributions.mjs (mocked, added to test:browser, the\n  ACTUAL remotes): an anonymous visitor gets the page from the csat remote,\n  ?rating preselects, a rating posts, no redirect, and the visitor asks for\n  nothing but /auth/me, /capabilities and the survey; unknown token; csat off →\n  unavailable with no survey request; the fold, Show signature and Not a\n  signature; mailintake withdrawn live → plain body, no reload; no console\n  errors. npm run test:browser: all pass.\n- csat-mail-plugins-proof.mjs (real backend, 21 checks): a fresh anonymous\n  profile rates a resolved throwaway issue''s survey, and GET /items/{id}/csat\n  returns it; signed in, the description and a comment read folded, restore\n  drops the annotation server-side; no console errors; the project is deleted.\n- browser-issue-features.mjs now serves the mailintake remote; passes.\n  email-settings-page, sla-report, signin-settings-page and usability-audit\n  proofs pass against the same backend.\n- pytest: 3238 passed, 4 skipped. tsc -b, vite build and build-all are clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8467b2201a1dcdc22b60fd3543359a265a21926d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/8467b2201a1dcdc22b60fd3543359a265a21926d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/11c2b15baba2f9c0e5b22d790da8ecad2403daf4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/11c2b15baba2f9c0e5b22d790da8ecad2403daf4","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDExYzJiMTViYWJhMmY5YzBlNWIyMmQ3OTBkYThlY2FkMjQwM2RhZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/7c79cb5b11ebfd38cfff84951fa0536c8f1f2787","sha":"7c79cb5b11ebfd38cfff84951fa0536c8f1f2787","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/7c79cb5b11ebfd38cfff84951fa0536c8f1f2787"}],"sha":"11c2b15baba2f9c0e5b22d790da8ecad2403daf4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/11c2b15baba2f9c0e5b22d790da8ecad2403daf4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/7c79cb5b11ebfd38cfff84951fa0536c8f1f2787/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T19:43:59Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T19:44:38Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1400] The palette and the query bar take contributed modes, and Ask and natural-language SLQ are the ai plugin''s\n\nRADD-1395 left two AI surfaces in the host: the command palette''s Ask\n(GET /search/semantic) and the query bar''s natural-language ask (POST /slq/nl),\nwith lib/ai.ts, lib/types/ai.ts, aiStatusQuery and the aiProvider/aiRole tags\nserving only them. Each now has a generic contribution point (UI API 1.18.0,\ndocumented in docs/plugin-ui.md \"Modes\"), the ai remote fills both, and the host\nnames no AI at all.\n\nThe contracts:\n- palette.mode — paletteMode(spec): id (<plugin>.<name>), label, hint, icon,\n  placeholder, prompt, busyLabel, and answer(query, {signal, onText}) resolving\n  ROWS ({rows, heading?, empty?}; PaletteRow {id, title, href, badge?, icon?,\n  subtitle?, hint?}) that the palette draws, arrow-navigates and follows through\n  the router, or TEXT ({text, heading?}) streamed through onText (the whole text\n  so far). The palette owns the trailing \"label: “query” — hint\" entry, the face\n  switch, Esc/back, the debounce and navigation. An answer is one query per\n  (mode, query) keyed under the owner''s name, so withdrawal drops it.\n- query.input.mode — queryInputMode(spec): toQuery(text, {dialect, signal})\n  resolving {query, explanation}, and the dialects it serves (QueryDialect.items\n  | worklog). The bar owns the policy: the SLQ | mode toggle, mod+I cycling SLQ\n  → each mode, the empty bar opening on the first available mode, a URL-carried\n  query opening SLQ; with none available it is plain SLQ with no toggle. The\n  answer lands in the SLQ editor, applied, with the explanation below. A run\n  whose plugin is withdrawn is aborted and its draft dropped.\n\nDecisions:\n- A mode is a SLOT contribution (tagging, withdrawal, per-contribution toggles\n  and the error boundary for free) whose meta is the mode and whose render is\n  its GATE. The host draws the triggers because it owns the keyboard, so\n  availability cannot be \"render null\" as with the editor''s buttons: the\n  surface mounts the gates while open, each calls the mode''s useAvailable hook\n  and reports. A withdrawn plugin''s gate unmounts; a throwing gate is never\n  offered. The palette mounts its gates only while open, as it read the status\n  before; the bar always.\n- QueryBar''s `dialect` is the named SLQ dialect now and maps to its endpoints\n  itself (nlDialect is gone); the timesheet passes worklog, which reaches the\n  mode.\n- The natural-language mode gates on features.nl_slq as well as enabled. The\n  host gated on enabled only, offered Ask with the feature off and hid it after\n  the first 404. It still stops offering itself after a 404 until the status is\n  read again.\n- The Ask rows link pages by their permalink (/pages?pageId=): a plugin may not\n  import another plugin''s functions, and the permalink is the stable address the\n  server emits too.\n\nSurprising: one palette serves every mode, so keepPreviousData would have shown\nAsk''s rows under another mode''s face while its answer loaded. The placeholder is\nnow only ever the SAME mode''s previous answer. Clearing the input inside a mode\nshows the mode''s prompt; the old Ask kept the stale rows.\n\nDeleted from the host: lib/ai.ts, lib/types/ai.ts, the Semantic* types,\naiStatusQuery, ApiPath.aiStatus/searchSemantic/slqNl, queryKeys.aiStatus/\nsearchSemantic and the aiProvider/aiRole tags. queries/ai-search.ts is\nqueries/search.ts. plugin-boundaries.test.mjs refuses every AI identifier and\nthe /ai, /search/semantic and /slq/nl routes in web/src, the SDK and the pages\npackage, and asserts that the host asks for modes and the ai remote contributes\nboth. The residue allowlist is gone.\n\nProofs: browser-contributed-modes.mjs (mocked, in test:browser; the actual ai\nremote plus a fixture remote with a streamed-text palette mode and an\nitems-only query mode) and contributed-modes-proof.mjs (real backend, host\nchunks checked by content). The chat and embeddings providers were unreachable\nfrom the build machine, so the real-backend run used\nRADD_PROOF_STAND_IN_MODEL=1, which answers the two model-backed requests in the\nbrowser. ai-settings-page-proof now checks the plugin''s own [\"ai\", \"status\"]\ngate.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a2840c84ac1dca06db9fe71138d932c43dc6b5b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/a2840c84ac1dca06db9fe71138d932c43dc6b5b9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/7c79cb5b11ebfd38cfff84951fa0536c8f1f2787","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/7c79cb5b11ebfd38cfff84951fa0536c8f1f2787","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDdjNzljYjViMTFlYmZkMzhjZmZmODQ5NTFmYTA1MzZjOGYxZjI3ODc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/841cf418ca144a8174dcdc0514b1b18a2edaa13c","sha":"841cf418ca144a8174dcdc0514b1b18a2edaa13c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/841cf418ca144a8174dcdc0514b1b18a2edaa13c"}],"sha":"7c79cb5b11ebfd38cfff84951fa0536c8f1f2787","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/7c79cb5b11ebfd38cfff84951fa0536c8f1f2787"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/841cf418ca144a8174dcdc0514b1b18a2edaa13c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T19:04:29Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T19:05:23Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1397] Co-editing''s UI is the collab plugin''s: the page asks for a live session, and the host''s editor binds to whatever the plugin hands it\n\nThe collab client lived in the host (web/src/components/editor/collab/, Milkdown''s\nplugin-collab inside RichEditor, the SDK bridges useLiveSession/EditingNow), so a\ndisabled collab still shipped yjs and y-websocket, and the host decided the editing\nmode itself. It is now the collab plugin''s UI remote (collab/ui, UI API 1.17.0).\n\nThe crux, decided: share the EDITOR RUNTIME, not yjs. A binding is ProseMirror plugins\n(y-prosemirror) that must be built from the host''s own prosemirror-model/-state/-view —\na bundled copy''s plugin keys, instanceof checks and node classes do not match the\neditor''s. Those three are now shared singletons, loaded ON DEMAND: the host registers\nloaders (through the paths its editor imports them by) and the /shared shims top-level\nawait them, so nothing is paid until an editor exists. yjs, y-protocols and y-websocket\nstay private to the remote: no host code ever touches a Y.Doc, so there is no second\ncopy to disagree with, and the host''s chunks carry none of it (checked by content).\nMilkdown is not shared — a binding needs only ProseMirror — and @milkdown/plugin-collab\nis dropped. Option (b), a host \"live document\" mechanism handed a Y.Doc, was rejected:\nit would keep y-prosemirror in the host and force yjs to be shared.\n\nWhat the host keeps is feature-neutral:\n- RichEditor''s `binding` (EditorBinding: key, label, bind(BindableEditor, signal)).\n  Bound, the editor waits for bind, drops its history, offers no plain mode, publishes\n  every change from the current document, and unbinds before it is destroyed.\n- `liveDocuments` sources + `useLiveDocument` in the SDK: the page asks with entity\n  type, id, write access and intent; the plugin answers with role, binding, presence and\n  saving chrome, and finish(). The page owns its document and its write — the saver calls\n  the page''s own save with the session as voucher (`collab_session`), so the plugin\n  knows no page endpoint. No provider is `none` at once: an optional plugin never holds\n  up the core editor (a \"joining while bundles load\" rule blocked editing forever in a\n  fixture whose capabilities carried no remotes — the mocked suite caught it).\n- One list of shared modules (web/scripts/shared-modules.mjs) that a boundary test holds\n  the import map, the remote build''s externals, the host publisher and the shims to.\n\nSurprising: Milkdown''s listener publishes the doc of the last LOCAL transaction 200 ms\nlater. When a colleague''s change arrived in that window, it overwrote the fresher\nserialisation that held it, and the saver wrote a body without the colleague''s line\n(the old host code had the same race; collab-proof types sequentially and never hit\nit). A bound editor now publishes only from its current document. Found by the new\nmocked proof, which has a synthetic peer write while this client types.\n\nThe backend is unchanged apart from the manifest''s remote: the write guard still refuses\nunvouched writes while a room is live, and answers from no rooms when disabled.\n\nProofs: browser-live-editing.mjs (mocked, in test:browser, over a synthetic y-websocket\nroom); collab-plugin-proof.mjs (real backend). The proof harness honours\nRADD_PROOF_PORT_OFFSET so runs can use disjoint debug ports.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6c2372581d2fc0e476e1de3010f645746c3ae1fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/6c2372581d2fc0e476e1de3010f645746c3ae1fa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/841cf418ca144a8174dcdc0514b1b18a2edaa13c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/841cf418ca144a8174dcdc0514b1b18a2edaa13c","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDg0MWNmNDE4Y2ExNDRhODE3NGRjZGMwNTE0YjFiMThhMmVkYWExM2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/cbf17ee067f230cc802ed672f9531cb0fb56b242","sha":"cbf17ee067f230cc802ed672f9531cb0fb56b242","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/cbf17ee067f230cc802ed672f9531cb0fb56b242"}],"sha":"841cf418ca144a8174dcdc0514b1b18a2edaa13c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/841cf418ca144a8174dcdc0514b1b18a2edaa13c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/cbf17ee067f230cc802ed672f9531cb0fb56b242/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T18:13:22Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T18:13:22Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1399] The proof harness removes its Chrome profile, so a suite run no longer fills /tmp\n\nThe mocked browser suite hung at its first proof with no output. /tmp, a 16 GB tmpfs, was full:\nabout 900 Chrome profiles, 40-60 MB each, that browser proofs had left behind. openBrowser starts\nChrome on a profile under the temp dir (mkdtemp per run for the mocked proofs), and close()\nkilled Chrome but never removed the profile. So every run grew /tmp until Chrome could not\nstart.\n\nclose() now waits for Chrome to exit and removes a profile that lives under the temp dir. The\nprocess-exit handler does the same for a proof that throws.\n\nbrowser-resolvable-threads had failed at a different step on each full-suite run while passing\nalone, which fits Chrome slowing down as /tmp filled. Its waits now allow 20 s, and a timeout\nprints what the page showed plus the console errors instead of just a label.\n\nVerified: a full npm run test:browser passes and leaves /tmp usage unchanged (37% before and\nafter).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e4b0da87fd6149f09d475674eca8ce2795195467","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/e4b0da87fd6149f09d475674eca8ce2795195467"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/cbf17ee067f230cc802ed672f9531cb0fb56b242","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/cbf17ee067f230cc802ed672f9531cb0fb56b242","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKGNiZjE3ZWUwNjdmMjMwY2M4MDJlZDY3MmY5NTMxY2IwZmI1NmIyNDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/f9dc9f8712b3fd7dba41aa0703b8142405cd2757","sha":"f9dc9f8712b3fd7dba41aa0703b8142405cd2757","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/f9dc9f8712b3fd7dba41aa0703b8142405cd2757"}],"sha":"cbf17ee067f230cc802ed672f9531cb0fb56b242","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/cbf17ee067f230cc802ed672f9531cb0fb56b242"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/f9dc9f8712b3fd7dba41aa0703b8142405cd2757/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T17:19:32Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T18:13:03Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1395] The editor has extension points, and every editor, read-mode, issue and draft AI surface is the ai plugin''s contribution through them\n\nThe optional ai plugin''s editor and issue UI lived in the host: 26 files and\n~290 references. The editor stays HOST (Milkdown/ProseMirror, the toolbar, the\nper-block diff review, CodeMirror code blocks, radd:* nodes — issues, comments\nand the wiki share it) and opens generic points; the ai remote fills them.\n\nThe contract (UI API 1.16.0, packages/plugin-sdk/src/editor-extensions.ts,\ndocumented in docs/plugin-ui.md \"The editor''s extension points\"):\n- editor.toolbar.action {editor}: a toolbar button, drawn with the bridged\n  EditorToolbarButton.\n- editor.selection.action {editor, selection}: chrome the host PLACES over a\n  selection and keeps mounted while idle; selection is null when collapsed or\n  unfocused, so a contribution holding a popover keeps its CAPTURED range.\n- content.read.action {text, context, transform?, subject, className?}: an\n  action on rendered content (descriptions, comments, page bodies). context is\n  {entityType, entityId, parent?}; transform (present only for writers) opens\n  the editor running it (RichEditorProps.initialTransform).\n- A transform: EditorHandle.transform(t, range?). t.run(input, {signal,\n  onText}) resolves {replacement, notes?} (null = withdrawn; a rejection''s\n  message is shown). The editor splices it and opens its own review band\n  (TransformRunPanel) with Accept/Reject all, the notes and the RADD-1274\n  detached-comment count.\n- issue.rail.top (a card above the fields card) and item.draft.assist (beside a\n  draft; the host frame is empty:hidden).\n- useReadingPane() + ReadingPaneContext: a panel beside the text on the issue\n  page and, through the ReadingPane bridge, the wiki. A panel opened from a\n  contribution closes when its plugin is withdrawn (new useContributionOwner,\n  provided by Slot).\n- IssueSuggestion: the host''s peek-aware issue row with hover preview and the\n  RADD-1090 merge, for any plugin''s suggestion list.\nThe SDK names no AI: AiReadMenu, AiRun and AiResultsPane are gone.\n\nThe ai remote (server/src/radd/modules/ai/ui/src) contributes the toolbar\nbutton and Ask AI (editor/), the read menu (read/), the pane answers and\nsimilar lists (results/), the issue rail card (issue/), Similar issues beside a\ndraft (forms/) and the Profile opt-out (profile/), with its own wire\n(transport.ts, sse.ts moved from the host, queries.ts — every key under\n[\"ai\", …] so withdrawal drops them) and deactivate() aborting runs in flight.\nai-protect moved with it (editor/protect.ts): the transform masks radd:*\nfences, images and attachment links and restores them; the editor never\nlearns there was a mask. The pages package switched to ReadingPane, the\ncontent.read.action slot and EditorTransform.\n\nDecisions:\n- What stayed host and why: the editor subsystem and its review are generic\n  mechanism every document surface uses; the run band, the review-end\n  detached-comment resolution and the selection placement are the editor''s.\n  The streaming protocol, prompts, masking and error wording are AI policy.\n- The review machinery (diff + decoration fork + review state + selection\n  rect) now registers on EVERY editor instance, inert until a review opens.\n  That removed the recreate-on-AI-gate-flip; the selection rect publishes only\n  where a selection contribution exists, so plain editors re-render nothing\n  more. A plugin arriving or leaving mid-edit no longer rebuilds the editor.\n- Contributions render their own triggers (not host-drawn from title/icon):\n  the gate (instance feature, user opt-out, loaded action list) is the\n  plugin''s, and a host-drawn trigger would show while the gate is closed.\n- The host run band and review use generic hooks (data-editor-run-panel,\n  -streaming, -preview, -note, data-editor-detached-comments); the ai-owned\n  handles (radd-ai-toolbar-icon, data-ai-selection-button/-menu,\n  data-ai-toolbar-menu) are unchanged. ai-feedback/ai-protect/ai-surface\n  proofs are repointed.\n- Copy the host kept generic: \"Finish the current review first.\"; the empty\n  outcome''s \"The AI suggested no changes.\" is the transform''s emptyMessage.\n- Profile''s \"AI assistance\" opt-out is a profile.section now, so it renders\n  after the host''s own sections and disappears with the plugin.\n\nSurprising:\n- The wiki''s read-mode Summarize had not sent the page''s images since\n  RADD-1275: the popover path sent images_of, but the wiki answers in the pane\n  (RADD-772, earlier), whose text-summary request never carried it. The pane\n  request carries it now — a behaviour change, and the one RADD-1275 meant.\n- A readiness race worth knowing for proofs: the read menu''s Summarize entry\n  waits on the whole editor-AI gate, including GET /ai/editor/actions; under\n  load the menu can open showing only \"Find similar issues\". Same as before the\n  move; the live proof now waits for the composer''s AI button first.\n- The comment composer is a rich editor with its own toolbar, and a rendered\n  comment shares the .radd-rich-editor class; proofs must scope to one editor.\n\nWhat remains (not moved; no half-moves):\n- The command palette''s Ask mode (GET /search/semantic, gated on\n  aiStatus.features.semantic_search) and the query bar''s natural-language ask\n  (POST /slq/nl, gated on aiStatus.enabled). Each needs a contribution point\n  of its own — a palette MODE with its entries in the palette''s keyboard\n  navigation, and a query-bar input mode whose availability decides the SLQ/Ask\n  toggle, the ⌘I shortcut and the default-to-Ask-on-an-empty-bar policy — which\n  is a design of its own, not this issue''s. What they read stays host and is\n  frozen by plugin-boundaries.test.mjs: lib/ai.ts (aiErrorText, isAiGone),\n  lib/types/ai.ts (AiStatus, AiFeature.semanticSearch, NlQueryRequest/Response),\n  aiStatusQuery + queryKeys.aiStatus + ApiPath.aiStatus, and the\n  Entity.aiProvider/aiRole tags its meta declares.\n- Out of scope and untouched: the storage routing chain''s \"AI classifier\"\n  rule label (storage settings) and Server status''s \"ai\" category order.\n\nVerification:\n- tsc -b, vite build, build-all (20 bundled + 19 remotes); node --test\n  web/scripts/*.test.mjs 95/95, including the new boundary test that refuses\n  AI vocabulary (identifiers, data-ai-* attributes, /ai/ endpoints) in web/src,\n  the SDK and the pages package outside the listed residue, and asserts the\n  host places each point and the ai remote contributes each.\n- npm run test:browser passes, with the new mocked\n  web/scripts/browser-editor-extensions.mjs (the actual ai remote; host\n  per-block review with Reject/Accept all; a mocked model that DROPS the\n  radd:media fence — masked going out, kept in the saved description; the\n  reading pane; withdrawal from an open editor and a rendered comment with no\n  reload and no /ai or /plugins/ai request; re-listing restores each control\n  once).\n- Backend: 3237 passed, 4 skipped (only the ai manifest''s ui_api_version and a\n  comment changed).\n- Real backend (:8115): ai-provider-options, page-detached-comments,\n  comment-replies and task-toggle proofs pass. The new\n  web/scripts/editor-ai-proof.mjs passes end to end with\n  RADD_PROOF_STAND_IN_MODEL=1; its live-provider run could not reach the chat\n  provider from the sandbox (ConnectError) and needs a run from a shell with a\n  route to it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1c5877cba4097f21057a475ae87253fee69e6ee6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/1c5877cba4097f21057a475ae87253fee69e6ee6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/f9dc9f8712b3fd7dba41aa0703b8142405cd2757","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/f9dc9f8712b3fd7dba41aa0703b8142405cd2757","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKGY5ZGM5Zjg3MTJiM2ZkN2RiYTQxYWEwNzAzYjgxNDI0MDVjZDI3NTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/bde1a8ee783b3af35a8efa7211995ea4ccb134d7","sha":"bde1a8ee783b3af35a8efa7211995ea4ccb134d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/bde1a8ee783b3af35a8efa7211995ea4ccb134d7"}],"sha":"f9dc9f8712b3fd7dba41aa0703b8142405cd2757","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/f9dc9f8712b3fd7dba41aa0703b8142405cd2757"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/bde1a8ee783b3af35a8efa7211995ea4ccb134d7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T17:04:24Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T17:05:21Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1396] The SLA settings page and queue views are the slas plugin''s, and the host names no SLA code\n\nRADD-1386 and RADD-1394 moved the SLA report and timers into the optional slas\nplugin; the project''s SLA settings page, the spec-64 queue views and the SLA\ntypes, queries and constants they needed still lived in web/src. Disabling slas\nleft a Settings tab that 404''d its endpoints and a queue view that asked a dead\n/sla-queue-items.\n\nWhat a queue is. Spec 64 calls it a view TYPE, and it is one, but its surface is\nthe host''s list: only its ROWS (live-urgency order over the whole match set),\nits default columns, a refresh cadence and a counted sidebar section differ. So\nthe kernel''s ViewTypeSpec gained `list_surface=ViewListSpec(rows_path, columns,\nrefresh_seconds)`, `sidebar_section` and `icon`, and slas registers `slas.queue`\nover its own `/sla-queue-items`. The host draws any such type with its ordinary\nlist (selection, bulk, columns, paging, SLQ bar) and names no plugin. Rejected:\nthe `view.type` slot, which would make slas re-implement the list in a remote,\nand a \"list preset with an SLA sort\", because the urgency order is Python-side\nlive evaluation, not an SLQ ORDER BY. The stored type is namespaced like\n`slas.timer` was: migration d1396slaqueue rewrites views.view_type ''queue'' to\n''slas.queue'' (downgrade restores it). `GET /views` swapped `exclude_type` for\n`sectioned` (read from the registry, so a disabled plugin''s views are ordinary\nagain and open to MissingPluginType, fetching nothing). A list-surface type\nshows the Display menu: its columns are the view''s since spec 108, which is\nnewer than spec 64''s \"fixed column set\".\n\nThe settings page. Project settings had no plugin page slot, so it got one, the\nSettings way: SlotId.projectSettingsPage matched on a segment, listed by\n`NavItemSpec(section=NavSection.PROJECT_SETTINGS, path=<segment>)` whose\n`requires` atoms are checked IN the project. One list\n(lib/project-settings-nav.ts) feeds the sub-nav, the index redirect and the\nsidebar''s Settings link. The page, form and \"met when\" field moved verbatim into\nslas/ui/src/settings (TeamAudience through the teams contract, priorities\nthrough items/metadata, csat''s section through the SDK''s ScopedSettings). UI API\n1.16.0.\n\nThe screens row. `sla` (\"SLA timers\") has placed nothing since RADD-1394 made\nthe SLA card an issue-rail contribution. Deleted, with its stored rows (same\nmigration), rather than making screen rows contributable: the participants,\napprovals and CSAT cards are not screen rows either, and a framework for one row\nis speculative.\n\nRealtime: a plugin tags queries with its server entity type verbatim\n(\"sla_policy\") and the host subscribes any tag it does not map itself, so the\nhost''s `slaPolicy` entity and `sla_policy` mapping went with the rest.\n\nSurprising:\n- queue.py sorted a timezone-AWARE \"no deadline\" sentinel beside the naive\n  due_at stamps, so any queue holding a ticking timer and an untimed issue\n  answered 500 (since RADD-1201; the existing test only mixed a BREACHED item\n  with untimed ones, which never compares the dates). Found by the new proof;\n  fixed with a naive NO_DUE and a regression test that fails on the old code.\n- lib/queue.ts''s orderBySlaUrgency was dead, and PROJECT_HOMED_SECTIONS too.\n- The sidebar''s project Settings link appeared for a release.update-only holder\n  and landed on \"no project settings to manage\"; it now follows the real list.\n- One SLA mirror remains in web/src on purpose: notify''s own sla_breach /\n  sla_due_soon notification kinds (the core notify module owns them). The\n  boundary test names that exception; moving them is notify''s change.\n- usability-audit-proof hardcodes a project id that exists only on the shared\n  dev DB, so it cannot run on a clean one (its SLA steps are covered by the\n  policy-edit and met-rules proofs, which pass).\n\nVerified: tsc, vite build and build-all clean; node --test 94/94 (the\nboundary test finds 180 violations on the previous tree, 0 now); pytest 3238\npassed, 4 skipped; npm run test:browser passes; migration up/down/up on a\nthrowaway DB; new real-backend proof sla-settings-queue-proof.mjs 22/22 on a\nseparate database, plus sla-policy-edit, sla-met-rules, sla-columns and\nsla-report proofs; the mocked board-navigation proof now covers the plugin rows\nendpoint, ignored axes and the missing-type notice.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8f183f0a6d0360b8b85b0f8f417219f853e23ebb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/8f183f0a6d0360b8b85b0f8f417219f853e23ebb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/bde1a8ee783b3af35a8efa7211995ea4ccb134d7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/bde1a8ee783b3af35a8efa7211995ea4ccb134d7","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKGJkZTFhOGVlNzgzYjNhZjM1YThlZmE3MjExOTk1ZWE0Y2NiMTM0ZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/1e30d63a10115fd2bb65ee2933b09126dd832ad6","sha":"1e30d63a10115fd2bb65ee2933b09126dd832ad6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/1e30d63a10115fd2bb65ee2933b09126dd832ad6"}],"sha":"bde1a8ee783b3af35a8efa7211995ea4ccb134d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/bde1a8ee783b3af35a8efa7211995ea4ccb134d7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/1e30d63a10115fd2bb65ee2933b09126dd832ad6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T15:44:45Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T16:10:41Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1392] Pages is a core plugin, and the wiki''s UI lives in its bundled package\n\nDecided 2026-09-26: the wiki is core. pages drops `core=False` and its\nmanifest remote; its ui/package.json is `\"radd\": {\"bundled\": true}` (no\nvite config), so the host imports it at build time and registers it at\nboot like audit, vcs and reporting (RADD-1373).\n\nWhat moved into server/src/radd/modules/pages/ui/src:\n- routes/: the spaces index (also the permalink resolver), a space and its\n  page, the print view (+ page-print.css);\n- view/: every former web/src/components/pages/* file. PageView (688 lines)\n  split into PageView, PageMeta, PageReading, ChangeUrlDialog and a\n  usePageEditing hook; PageTree lost NewPageButton, the inline rail lost\n  useInlineAnchors, ArchivedPagesPanel its pure rows, extensions.tsx its\n  list blocks (ListExtensions);\n- settings/: Settings → Page spaces with PageTemplatesSection, SpaceForm\n  and SpaceAccessPanel, contributed as a `settings.page` slot;\n- sidebar/SidebarSpaces: the new `sidebar.section` slot (match \"pages\");\n- queries.ts, types.ts, endpoints.ts, links.ts (spec 124''s one place a\n  page URL is built, now carrying `PageRoute`), line-diff.ts, the spaces\n  directory hook, and useSpacePermissions over the SDK''s scope check.\n\nThe host still routes. router.tsx mounts the package''s `./index-page`,\n`./space-page` and `./print-page` exports lazily at `PageRoute`''s paths;\nnothing new matches routes (the page address stays a splat). The host''s\nother page consumers (pins bar, palette, inbox, the issue''s Pages row,\ndeflection, the editor''s insert menu, usePermissions'' space checks, the\ncollab saver) import the package''s `./links`, `./queries`, `./types` and\n`./endpoints` exports, and the host copies of those (lib/page-links,\nlib/queries/pages, lib/types/pages, the page ApiPath/api*Path constants,\nRoutePath''s page entries, the page query keys) are deleted. The Page\nspaces nav row stays a host row: it gates on page.manage in ANY space,\nwhich a NavItemSpec cannot express.\n\nWhat stayed host, and why: the editor subsystem (RichEditor/RichViewer,\nMilkdown, the AI menu and results panel, collab''s client), the comment\nkit, the access editors, the menus, the Escape stack and the sidebar\nchrome. Issues and comments use all of them, and collab is an optional\nplugin whose UI is a separate issue. The package reaches them through the\nSDK host bridge, UI API 1.15.0:\n- host-document.tsx: RichEditor (`attachTo` names the attachment parent;\n  `live` is an opaque LiveRoom), RichViewer, Markdown, AiReadMenu + AiRun,\n  AiResultsPane, EditingNow and useLiveSession. The collab wiring stays in\n  the host''s bridge: useLiveSession IS useCollabSession, and the editor\n  adapter maps the room to the editor''s collab config.\n- host-comments.tsx: useCommentFeed, CommentReplies, CommentHistory,\n  CopyCommentLink, the thread badge/filter/resolve button, linked-comment\n  landing, thread expansion, commentHref, repliesLabel, threadRuleClass,\n  sendTaskToggle, and the CommentRow shape.\n- host-kit.tsx: DropdownMenu, Popover, useDismiss (the host''s one Escape\n  stack), AccessGrantsEditor, ScopedAccess, StateCategoryDot,\n  SidebarSection and SidebarLink.\nShared STATE moved into the SDK instead of behind a bridge: the `radd:*`\nregistry and its contexts (a context only reaches a consumer through the\nsame object, so MarkdownSourceCtx left lib/markdown), markdown-outline,\ntext-quote anchoring and dom-text (its projection registry is written by\nthe host''s code block and read by the wiki''s rail). The ten first-party\n`radd:*` blocks register at boot from extension-registry.tsx with their\nrenderers loaded on first use, since an issue description renders them\ntoo; test_page_extensions.py now holds the registry AND the renderer maps\nto the kernel in both directions. Also: auth contributes the people\ndirectory as the `auth.people` query source (page authors and avatars);\nPageLabels reads the `labels.catalog` source instead of importing labels''\nimplementation; SDK usePermissions reads `global_role` (the server''s\ncredential-aware bypass, what the host''s checker reads) before\n`instance_role`; the host''s Callout and DropdownMenu accept any icon\ncomponent; RequestPanelBody renders a requester''s conversation with the\nhost viewer instead of the wiki''s PageBody.\n\nSurprising, found on the way:\n- A bridged hook must return stable values. useCommentFeed first returned\n  a new array per render; the inline rail''s anchor scan depends on it, so\n  it re-rendered forever (production shows no error, only CPU). That loop\n  runs at default priority and starved Suspense''s retry lane: lazy host\n  surfaces opened by a click (the Restrict dialog''s grants editor, a\n  discussion thread''s replies) kept their fallback after the chunk had\n  arrived, until an unrelated update. Memoising the list fixed both;\n  import-author-proof caught it in dev as \"Maximum update depth exceeded\".\n- The AI results pane cannot be a lazy bridge: its children are the page,\n  and a lazy wrapper renders them as its Suspense fallback first, then again\n  inside the loaded pane. When the chunk arrived after Edit was pressed, the\n  remount threw the open edit session away (the new proof caught it). The\n  host pane is eager and lazy-loads only the panel.\n- useCollabSession is now provided at startup, so its yjs/y-websocket\n  transport is imported when a room is first joined rather than with it.\n- Mocked proofs used Pages as the example optional remote. No optional\n  plugin contributes an option directory, so browser-option-contributions\n  keeps its failed-remote coverage with a fixture remote contributing one\n  through the same SDK contract; browser-automation-editor now says Pages\n  is bundled.\n- Tests that named pages as optional or scanned only web/src: test_kernel''s\n  optional list names collab; test_module_contracts'' non-vacuity set names\n  collab; test_client_scope_audit reads plugin packages'' atom constants\n  (PagePermission), so the wiki''s one deliberately-global gate stays audited;\n  test_page_extensions reads the package; anchoring/line-diff/audit\n  regression tests read the moved files; import-author-proof renders the\n  package''s components through the host bridges.\n- Two stale real-backend proofs fixed while verifying: comment-replies\n  (RADD-1335''s Reply button opens the composer; its cleanup could not\n  delete a non-empty space) and page-templates (the top bar''s New page,\n  RADD-1236, was clicked instead of the tree''s; the created page was\n  archived, not deleted).\n\nVerification: tsc + vite build + build-all (19 bundled, 19 remotes); node\n--test web/scripts/*.test.mjs; npm run test:browser; the full backend\nsuite; ruff. Against a real backend: pages-package-proof.mjs (new, 27\nchecks), page-paths, page-detached-comments, comment-replies, collab (20),\npage-archive, page-templates, task-toggle, page-print — all passing, every\nrow they created removed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"eed553a5af40198d4aa616f403ca4fcee855bcc9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/eed553a5af40198d4aa616f403ca4fcee855bcc9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/1e30d63a10115fd2bb65ee2933b09126dd832ad6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/1e30d63a10115fd2bb65ee2933b09126dd832ad6","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDFlMzBkNjNhMTAxMTVmZDJiYjY1ZWUyOTMzYjA5MTI2ZGQ4MzJhZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/13be95be91234e51240d3512df94d3035a7fdd9a","sha":"13be95be91234e51240d3512df94d3035a7fdd9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/13be95be91234e51240d3512df94d3035a7fdd9a"}],"sha":"1e30d63a10115fd2bb65ee2933b09126dd832ad6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/1e30d63a10115fd2bb65ee2933b09126dd832ad6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/13be95be91234e51240d3512df94d3035a7fdd9a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T14:45:27Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T14:48:38Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1393] Dashboards is a core plugin whose UI is the bundled dashboards package, and plugins put widgets on My Work by contributing them\n\nWhy. Dashboards was the last optional plugin My Work depended on, and it\ncould not become core while it reached an optional one: My Work''s widget\nkinds were a hardcoded set, and its suggested layout imported\napprovals.service.pending_for_user behind `\"approvals\" in registries.plugins`\n- exactly what test_core_modules_never_reach_optional_plugins (RADD-1349)\nrefuses. So the reach is inverted first, then dashboards is flipped.\n\nBackend. WidgetTypeSpec gains `personal` (the widget shows the viewer''s own\nwork: offered and accepted on My Work, refused on a shared dashboard with\n\"is a My Work widget\") and `suggest`, an async (session, user) -> bool that\nputs the type on a person''s suggested defaults. dashboards/personal.py keeps\nonly My Work''s own kinds and reads the registry for the rest; /capabilities\nwidget_types carries `personal`. approvals contributes \"Awaiting my approval\"\n(key \"approvals\", the value layouts already store, so nobody''s My Work\nchanges) with suggest=service.has_pending. dashboards drops core=False and\nweak_depends on approvals.\n\nDecision: forms'' request widgets stay My Work''s own cases. forms is core, so\ndashboards may reach it, and its widgets render from host components that\nthe Portal shares; making them contributions would mean moving the requests\nUI into forms'' package as well. The rule is now one sentence: core modules''\nwidgets are My Work''s cases, optional plugins contribute.\n\nA widget already on someone''s layout whose plugin is switched off keeps its\nplace when they save (matched by id and type); only a NEW one of an\nunregistered type is refused. Without that, a collapse click (which saves)\nfailed for anyone holding an approvals widget while approvals was off.\n\nFrontend. server/src/radd/modules/dashboards/ui is a bundled package: the\npage (./page, lazily imported by the host router, which keeps the route), My\nWork''s canvas (./my-work: MyWorkCanvas owns /dashboards/my-work/*, WidgetBody\ndraws builtin, \"My activity\", report and slot-contributed widgets), the\nsidebar''s directory hook and New dashboard dialog (./sidebar), the summary\nquery nav-facts reads (./queries) and the wire types (./types). My Work''s\n404 fallback is gone - the plugin can no longer be off - and its switch lost\nthe approvals case, which renders through dashboard.widget from the approvals\nremote (AwaitingApproval.tsx, UI API 1.15.0).\n\nWhat only the shell owns reaches the package through the SDK host bridge,\nUI API 1.15.0: SlqField, PageQueryFilter, ViewSelect, SharingDialog,\nReportWidget, ItemKeyLink, ItemPeek, MissingPluginType (implemented in\nweb/src/host-surfaces.tsx; the heavy ones lazy, so none of it joins the\nentry chunk). usePagedDirectory gained `enabled`.\n\nSurprising. The widget grid sized report charts through reporting''s\nChartHeightContext, a React context that a plugin may not import from\nanother plugin (a context is not a contract). It moved into the SDK as part\nof the dashboard.widget contract, and reporting''s charts read it there. The\nproof pins it: a 460px widget draws a 280px plot, not either chart default.\nAlso, the canvas''s discard prompt was window.confirm inside useBlocker; it is\nthe SDK''s confirm dialog now (TanStack accepts an async shouldBlockFn).\n\nVerified: tsc + vite + build-all; node tests 93/93 (a new boundary test\nrefuses dashboard components and /dashboards/my-work|summary and /approvals\nvocabulary in web/src); pytest 3237 passed, 4 skipped, incl.\ntest_my_work_contributed_widgets.py (withdrawn approvals is neither offered\nnor suggested and a new one is refused, an existing one survives a save,\nregistered it is suggested to whoever has a pending approval and refused on\nshared dashboards); npm run test:browser; real backend:\ndashboards-package-proof.mjs (27 checks: a pending approval puts the widget\non the suggested layout, the remote draws the row, its key links and a click\npeeks, a sidebar-created dashboard gets an Issue count widget equal to\n/items/count, a host report card at the granted plot height, delete, chunk\nprovenance, no console errors, My Work byte-for-byte unchanged),\nsla-report-proof.mjs, approval-rule-editor-proof.mjs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7bbf08dbaac177010d918669a4473fe913b5ab97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/7bbf08dbaac177010d918669a4473fe913b5ab97"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/13be95be91234e51240d3512df94d3035a7fdd9a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/13be95be91234e51240d3512df94d3035a7fdd9a","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDEzYmU5NWJlOTEyMzRlNTEyNDBkMzUxMmRmOTRkMzAzNWE3ZmRkOWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/13b739c331d582cf8c380213ecc24f3fdc0bf356","sha":"13b739c331d582cf8c380213ecc24f3fdc0bf356","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/13b739c331d582cf8c380213ecc24f3fdc0bf356"}],"sha":"13be95be91234e51240d3512df94d3035a7fdd9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/13be95be91234e51240d3512df94d3035a7fdd9a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/13b739c331d582cf8c380213ecc24f3fdc0bf356/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T14:35:27Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T14:36:00Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1394] Plugins contribute list columns and card cells, and the SLA timers are the slas plugin''s\n\nSLA timers were part of the host''s own column and card vocabulary although slas\nis an optional plugin with its own remote: an `sla` builtin column, an `sla`\ncard-cell case, `slaByItem` threaded from view.tsx through ViewList, ViewBoard,\nViewSwimlanes, BoardCard and ColumnCells, a rail panel in IssueProperties, and\nthe chips, types and queries under web/src. No plugin could add a column or a\ncard cell at all.\n\nThe surface (UI API 1.15.0) reuses what exists instead of adding a registry:\n\n- `itemAttribute({id, label, width, minWidth, source, sample?, render})` returns\n  an ordinary contribution to the new `item.attribute` slot, keyed by `match` =\n  the id. Plugin tagging, withdrawal, the per-contribution toggles and the error\n  boundary come from the slot registry. What the host needs before rendering\n  (label, widths, source) rides a new generic `SlotContribution.meta`.\n- `source` names one of the plugin''s own `querySources`; the host calls it with\n  `{ids}` (at most ITEM_ATTRIBUTE_BATCH_MAX = 200) and gets `{[itemId]: value}`\n  for the items that have one. `useContributedQueries` (new) gives many\n  requests exactly `useContributedQuery`''s identity, so reads are shared and a\n  withdrawn owner''s in-flight read is aborted by the loader, as before.\n- The host (`lib/item-attribute-data.ts`) asks each SHOWN attribute once per page\n  of rows, in stable batches, and provides the values through a context, so no\n  prop threads a plugin''s data. Lists, board cards, swimlanes and the card\n  designer (palette group \"From plugins\", preview of the declared `sample`) take\n  contributed attributes beside their builtins.\n\nDecisions:\n\n- Namespace, no exception: an attribute id and its source must be\n  `<plugin>.<name>` of the registering plugin. `useItemAttributes()` skips\n  anything else (a builtin, `cf.*`, a bare name, another plugin''s prefix), and\n  cells render through the new `<Slot owner=…>`, so a second plugin registering\n  the same key draws nothing. The SLA column is therefore `slas.timer`, and\n  migration d1394slacols rewrites stored `sla` ids in views.columns,\n  views.card_layout and card_layout_presets (downgrade restores them). A\n  declared exception for the bare `sla` would have been a permanent hole in the\n  rule, unverifiable against future builtins.\n- Degradation matches a deleted custom field: a withdrawn attribute''s id stays\n  in the saved view and layout, the list skips it, the Columns editor shows\n  `<id> (unavailable)`, and the designer''s stale note names it.\n- The rail''s SLA section is contributed through issue.panel.section (order 40),\n  where rail cards already arrive.\n\nThe slas remote now owns the batch client (`slas.timers`, re-read every minute,\ntagged item+slaPolicy), the per-item timers query, SlaRowChip/SlaTimerChip and\nthe rail panel. The host dropped the `sla` column, cell case, card slot,\nslaByItem threading, SlaChips.tsx, and the SLA timer types, queries, query keys,\npaths and constants nothing else used. Queue views (lib/queue.ts) and the SLA\nsettings page are a separate issue and untouched; the queue default columns now\nname `slas.timer`.\n\nSurprising on the way: the chips'' raw red/amber/emerald-300 text was the\ndark-theme shade only, so they moved to the status ink tier (measured 5.1-7.1:1\nin both themes). The screens module still lists an arrangeable `sla` row\n(ScreenBuiltinField.SLA, \"SLA timers\" in the screens editor) that no longer\nplaces anything, since the section is a plugin card now; that belongs with the\nsettings/queue follow-up.\n\nProofs: web/scripts/browser-plugin-columns.mjs (mocked API, real slas remote\nplus a rogue plugin: one batch per page shared by list and board, namespace\nrefusals, withdrawal aborts the in-flight batch and leaves the saved id\nunavailable, re-listing reads once) and web/scripts/sla-columns-proof.mjs (real\nbackend: list, board and rail equal the endpoints; drawn from /plugins/slas/;\ncleaned up). Boundary test: no SLA vocabulary on the host surfaces.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"93da3d10fb74cbf2dd207ce20ca92512a397154a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/93da3d10fb74cbf2dd207ce20ca92512a397154a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/13b739c331d582cf8c380213ecc24f3fdc0bf356","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/13b739c331d582cf8c380213ecc24f3fdc0bf356","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDEzYjczOWMzMzFkNTgyY2Y4YzM4MDIxM2VjYzI0ZjNmZGMwYmYzNTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/98d482bf3c14a69a3a68b925ad3bd33ba663ffeb","sha":"98d482bf3c14a69a3a68b925ad3bd33ba663ffeb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/98d482bf3c14a69a3a68b925ad3bd33ba663ffeb"}],"sha":"13b739c331d582cf8c380213ecc24f3fdc0bf356","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/13b739c331d582cf8c380213ecc24f3fdc0bf356"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/98d482bf3c14a69a3a68b925ad3bd33ba663ffeb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T12:31:23Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T12:31:23Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1349] A core module never reaches an optional plugin, and a test says so\n\nThe backend review found 25 places where a core module imported an optional plugin:\n- workflow and items → approvals;\n- notify → pages, participants and mailintake;\n- search → pages and ai;\n- reporting → slas and csat;\n- automations → leave, mailintake and participants;\n- attachments → ai.\n\nThe guards around them could not see a plugin being disabled at runtime. `except ImportError`\nnever fires, because plugin code is always importable, and `settings.modules` is boot\nconfiguration.\n\nRADD-1383–1387 inverted every one: the core dispatches a hook or reads a kernel socket, and the\nplugin registers. One declared-but-unused edge was left, automations → pages, and it is deleted.\n\ntest_core_modules_never_reach_optional_plugins now refuses the whole class: a core plugin may not\ndeclare an optional plugin in depends_on or weak_depends, or import one. Optional → optional weak\nedges (slas → csat) stay legal. It fails with the dead edge restored. CLAUDE.md rule 1 carries\nthe rule.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"074b93e2e3740c88266289912b3d36e7f2b7b667","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/074b93e2e3740c88266289912b3d36e7f2b7b667"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/98d482bf3c14a69a3a68b925ad3bd33ba663ffeb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/98d482bf3c14a69a3a68b925ad3bd33ba663ffeb","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDk4ZDQ4MmJmM2MxNGE2OWEzYTY4YjkyNWFkM2JkMzNiYTY2M2ZmZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/22707311ccfe26a4b00c88567f3d714a98d3b854","sha":"22707311ccfe26a4b00c88567f3d714a98d3b854","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/22707311ccfe26a4b00c88567f3d714a98d3b854"}],"sha":"98d482bf3c14a69a3a68b925ad3bd33ba663ffeb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/98d482bf3c14a69a3a68b925ad3bd33ba663ffeb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/22707311ccfe26a4b00c88567f3d714a98d3b854/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T12:24:49Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T12:24:49Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1391] A team-restricted internal comment notifies only its teams\n\nSpec 50 lets an internal comment be narrowed to teams, and notify''s consumer has a check for it:\nconsumer._allowed reads planned.detail[\"visible_to_teams\"]. The planner never put it there. It\ncopied the comment''s excerpt and visibility only, so the check saw no teams and returned True for\nevery holder of comment.read_internal on the project. Their inbox row carried the comment''s\nEXCERPT. The mail re-check (can_read_comment) refused those rows, so the leak was the in-app\ninbox.\n\nThe planner now carries visible_to_teams from the comment event into every COMMENTED and\nMENTIONED row it plans. The existing check then does what spec 50 intended.\n\nRejected: re-reading the comment in the consumer. The detail is the record of the audience at\nposting time, and the check already existed; it had simply never been fed.\n\nThe RADD-1385 notify rework found it; the page path already used can_read_comment. The new test\nfails without the fix:\n- a team member is notified;\n- an outsider who holds read_internal is refused;\n- a project manager is notified;\n- the same outsider is admitted when the comment is not narrowed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e26a74551ec6cf86ef1faea8528ce420824b7690","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/e26a74551ec6cf86ef1faea8528ce420824b7690"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/22707311ccfe26a4b00c88567f3d714a98d3b854","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/22707311ccfe26a4b00c88567f3d714a98d3b854","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDIyNzA3MzExY2NmZTI2YTRiMDBjODg1NjdmM2Q3MTRhOThkM2I4NTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/0a9e7fd205716f6eadb067733b135195911d0134","sha":"0a9e7fd205716f6eadb067733b135195911d0134","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/0a9e7fd205716f6eadb067733b135195911d0134"}],"sha":"22707311ccfe26a4b00c88567f3d714a98d3b854","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/22707311ccfe26a4b00c88567f3d714a98d3b854"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/0a9e7fd205716f6eadb067733b135195911d0134/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T12:17:01Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T12:19:54Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1387] Automations and storage routing reach leave, mailintake, participants and ai only through what those plugins contribute\n\nWhy: two CORE modules called OPTIONAL plugins directly. automations imported\nleave.service (round-robin''s away check), mailintake.service (Send email and\nits `contact` role) and participants.service (Add participant), each gated on\n`X in settings.modules`; attachments'' llm routing rule lazily imported\nai.client/features/types. settings.modules is BOOT config: a plugin disabled\nin the plugin manager leaves the kernel registries but stays in that tuple,\nso these calls kept running against a withdrawn plugin.\n\nWhat changed:\n- Kernel: a PERSON_AVAILABILITY socket (`PersonAvailabilityProvider.\n  away_user_ids(session, day, user_ids)`) — the per-person sibling of\n  NON_WORKING_DAYS, which answers for the instance. leave provides it\n  (`leave/availability.py`, over `calendar()` so team holidays expand to\n  members); round-robin unions every provider, none registered = nobody away.\n  LEAVE_MODULE and leave_service() are deleted.\n- Send email is mailintake''s node (`mailintake/automation_email.py`):\n  planner, applier, dry run, template tokens, the RADD-1265\n  outbound_configured check, the role-forces-per-item write check, the\n  RADD-1318 thread option, and the \"Tell the reporter when their issue is\n  done\" template all moved with it. `EmailRecipient` (reporter/assignee/\n  contact) is mailintake''s; automations keeps `PersonRole`\n  (reporter/assignee) in `roles.py`, which is what is left of\n  `email_action.py`.\n- Add participant is participants'' node (`participants/automation.py`). The\n  issue suggested a mailintake → participants weak edge, but the code shows\n  add_participant was never part of Send email — it is its own action, which\n  only SHARED email_action.py''s feature-detection helper. The owner of the\n  noun contributing it needs no edge at all, so no weak edge was added.\n- The `llm` storage rule is ai''s provider on STORAGE_ROUTING_RULE\n  (`ai/storage_rule.py`, `StorageRuleType.LLM`). The routing engine''s\n  \"would the uploader be asked\" prediction no longer branches on CIDR/LLM:\n  a rule type may answer an optional `captured_types`, and one without it\n  (or with no provider) captures nothing. `GET /storage/rule-types` lists the\n  live types; the Storage page offers only those and marks a stored rule of\n  a withdrawn type \"Unavailable · skipped\".\n- Edges: automations drops weak leave/mailintake/participants; attachments\n  drops weak ai. notify/pages/forms stay on automations untouched.\n\nDecisions:\n- The node KEYS are unchanged (`action.send_email`,\n  `action.add_participant`), so stored graphs load and run with no\n  migration; the SPA still renders their built-in forms because the\n  inspector keys on the `action.` prefix. A test writes a graph straight to\n  the row, as the built-ins stored it, and dry-runs it through the new owners.\n- Unavailable owner = the behaviour contributed nodes already had: withdrawn,\n  the node leaves the catalog, cannot be saved, and a stored graph''s node\n  records \"unknown action type ''action.send_email''\" (failed; an applying run\n  is recorded as failed and emits automation.run_failed) while sibling nodes\n  run. A stored llm rule with ai off is skipped like any rule whose type has\n  no provider — the chain falls through to the default host.\n\nSurprises:\n- A contributed action could not render `{{items.*}}`: `ctx.render` passed no\n  item set, so a digest''s `{{items.list}}` would have stayed literal after the\n  move. `ctx.render` now supplies the set (memoised per node), and the context\n  gained `target_item()` and `person(value)` so a plugin action resolves\n  `reporter`/`assignee`/an email exactly as the built-ins do without\n  importing automations.\n- `StorageRuleCreate.rule_type` was the `RuleType` ENUM, so a plugin''s rule\n  type could never be created despite the socket (\"a plugin type is one more\n  registration\"). It is a string validated against the live providers now;\n  RuleType keeps attachments'' own user_choice|cidr.\n- `server/scripts/seed_dev_stack.py` seeded `RuleType.LLM`; it uses\n  `StorageRuleType.LLM` now.\n- automations'' `pages` and `forms` weak edges have no Python import behind\n  them (added by RADD-1365, apparently for the UI); left alone.\n- `web/scripts/storage-email-proof.mjs` fails on main too: it clicks\n  \"Add host\", and the button reads \"New host\".\n\nTests: `test_optional_plugin_withdrawal.py` withdraws leave, mailintake,\nparticipants and ai at runtime (`registries.unregister_plugin`) and pins both\nhalves of each. Existing send_email/add_participant/llm tests now drive the\ncontributed nodes through a real node context.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"841c255111283982321d0056e31c514fcfe593fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/841c255111283982321d0056e31c514fcfe593fc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/0a9e7fd205716f6eadb067733b135195911d0134","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/0a9e7fd205716f6eadb067733b135195911d0134","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDBhOWU3ZmQyMDU3MTZmNmVhZGIwNjc3MzNiMTM1MTk1OTExZDAxMzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/8cbb3a95e046fff2c90abfcd6ca5e6d7db8dc441","sha":"8cbb3a95e046fff2c90abfcd6ca5e6d7db8dc441","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/8cbb3a95e046fff2c90abfcd6ca5e6d7db8dc441"}],"sha":"0a9e7fd205716f6eadb067733b135195911d0134","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/0a9e7fd205716f6eadb067733b135195911d0134"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/8cbb3a95e046fff2c90abfcd6ca5e6d7db8dc441/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T12:16:55Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T12:19:54Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1385] Notify learns page audiences, participants and the mail transport from their plugins through three kernel sockets\n\nWhy: notify is core, and it imported three OPTIONAL plugins - pages (the\nread gate at top level in authorization.py, watchers/readable ids/refs in\npageevents.py, the space picker and labels in options/targets/prefs),\nparticipants (team audience) and mailintake (the transport, and its\nMailFailureReport/SentMailKind at top level) - behind `try: import` guards.\nThose never fire: plugin code is always importable, so a plugin disabled in\nthe plugin manager (withdrawn from `registries`) went on being consulted.\n\nWhat changed:\n- kernel/sockets.py: NOTIFICATION_SUBJECT (NotificationSubjectProvider,\n  keyed by entity type: scope, events, locate, watcher_ids, reader_ids,\n  scope_options, scope_names), NOTIFICATION_AUDIENCE\n  (NotificationAudienceSource.participant_ids) and MAIL_TRANSPORT\n  (MailTransport.configured/send). `sockets.providers` only returns LIVE\n  plugins'' providers, which is the whole point.\n- notify keeps the mechanism. notify/subjects.py replaces pageevents.py:\n  generic non-item fan-out, the mail re-check (`readable`), and the\n  picker/labels for a provider-backed subscription scope. Rows about a\n  subject carry notify-owned subject_type/subject_id beside the provider''s\n  payload. consumer.handles() is the public \"do we act on this\" predicate.\n  planner.plan_page_event -> plan_subject_event.\n- notify/transport.py owns the mail contract: NotificationMail,\n  NotificationMailKind (notification|digest, removed from mailintake''s\n  SentMailKind) and MailFailureReport (moved from mailintake - the retry\n  ladder that needs it is notify''s). mailintake''s transport imports it.\n- Providers: pages/notifications.py (the page subject; refs.py''s three\n  notify read seams moved into it), participants/audience.py (team\n  members), mailintake/notify_transport.py (the transport). Each registers\n  an IntegrationSpec; mailintake now depends_on notify.\n- notify''s weak_depends on participants/mailintake/pages is gone;\n  test_module_contracts passes with no import from notify into them.\n\nDecisions:\n- No transport => no email. The env-relay fallback in notify\n  (_send_direct) is deleted; the relay is the transport''s business\n  (mailintake still falls back to RADD_SMTP_*). Both loops stamp pending\n  rows as undeliverable (mailer.record_undeliverable) instead of holding a\n  day of mail for a plugin that may come back; an UNCONFIGURED transport\n  still waits, as before. The inbox is untouched.\n- The page read gate is ONE provider method (reader_ids) for fan-out and\n  the mail re-check; guard_page is no longer reached from notify.\n- scope_names narrows and labels in one call: the label is the whole of\n  what the subscription gate protects.\n- Internal comments on a non-item subject are gated by\n  comments.can_read_comment (the comments module''s own answer) instead of\n  a hand-rolled space-scoped copy; it also honours per-team restrictions\n  from the DB, which the old copy read from a detail key never set.\n- RuleScope.SPACE and the page_* kinds stay in notify''s vocabulary (no\n  import involved); moving the kinds into pages is a possible follow-up.\n\nSurprising:\n- A page notification''s EMAIL never went through mailintake at all: with\n  item_id None the mailer fell to the env relay, so on a rows-only\n  instance page mail was never delivered. It now goes as itemless plain\n  mail through the transport.\n- Rows written before this change carry no subject stamp and are no longer\n  mailed (the inbox still shows them) - accepted, no backfill (pre-V1).\n\nTests: test_notify_plugin_sockets.py (pages withdrawn: a page comment in\nthe stream plans nothing and raises nothing, a queued page row fails the\nmail re-check; registered: the watcher hears. mailintake withdrawn: the\nrow is in the inbox and both loops record it undeliverable without\ndialling the relay; registered: the same row goes out). Two notify-mailer\ntests that pinned the deleted env-relay path were removed; three tests\nfilter with consumer.handles instead of _HANDLED; the absent-wiki case in\ntest_subscription_options patched `__import__` to raise ImportError - the\nvery idiom this removes - and now withdraws the pages plugin instead, with\na control that spaces exist first.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d858e289dcb28f2caec757a61ab7db231162dead","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/d858e289dcb28f2caec757a61ab7db231162dead"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/8cbb3a95e046fff2c90abfcd6ca5e6d7db8dc441","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/8cbb3a95e046fff2c90abfcd6ca5e6d7db8dc441","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDhjYmIzYTk1ZTA0NmZmZjJjOTBhYmZjZDZjYTVlNmQ3ZGI4ZGM0NDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/c8c54879203620426d2cd0a2c6ca28534fb41f39","sha":"c8c54879203620426d2cd0a2c6ca28534fb41f39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/c8c54879203620426d2cd0a2c6ca28534fb41f39"}],"sha":"8cbb3a95e046fff2c90abfcd6ca5e6d7db8dc441","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/8cbb3a95e046fff2c90abfcd6ca5e6d7db8dc441"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/c8c54879203620426d2cd0a2c6ca28534fb41f39/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T12:01:55Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T12:02:20Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1384] Search sources are contributed: pages provides the documents search shows, ai provides the semantic candidates\n\nThe core search module imported two optional plugins directly — pages\n(search_pages, readable spaces, restricted-result dropping, space names)\nand ai (embedding candidates) — guarded by `DOCS_MODULE in settings.modules`\nand `AI_EMBEDDINGS_MODULE in settings.modules`. That setting is the BOOT\nconfig: a plugin disabled at runtime leaves the kernel registries but stays\nin it, so with Pages switched off /search/deflect and /search/semantic kept\nreturning wiki pages whose routes and UI were gone. The fusion path was\nonly partly covered, by ai.features.plugin_loaded().\n\nTwo kernel sockets now carry them, following TRANSITION_CHECK and\nNON_WORKING_DAYS:\n\n* SEARCH_DOCUMENTS — a SearchDocumentSource (`entity_type`, `search` = the\n  reader-gated FTS ranking, `resolve` = the readable live subset of\n  candidate ids) answering `search.sources.DocumentHit`. pages provides it\n  (`pages/search_source.PageDocuments`) and owns the whole ACL: readable\n  spaces before the limit (RADD-791), restricted pages dropped (RADD-792),\n  space names. pages -> search is the right direction; pages already\n  depended on search.\n* SEMANTIC_CANDIDATES — a SemanticCandidateSource (`enabled`, `candidates`\n  keyed by entity type, never a permission answer). ai provides it\n  (`embeddings/candidates.SemanticCandidates`, items + pages).\n\nsearch keeps the mechanism: request parsing, item FTS, RRF fusion, the\ntime budget and the FTS-only floor, all in the new `search/sources.py`\nconsumer. No document provider = no documents; no live semantic provider =\nplain FTS and Ask mode `enabled: false`. Endpoint shapes are unchanged.\nsearch''s `weak_depends=(\"ai\", \"pages\")` and both module-path constants are\ngone; test_module_contracts holds with no search -> pages/ai import left.\n\nDecided on the way:\n* The reader gate that four page-search surfaces copied (GET /pages/search,\n  the palette searchable, MCP search_pages, deflection) is one function,\n  `search_source.readable_results`, so none of them can drift.\n* The time budget stays where it was (/search only). Deflection keeps using\n  the session after its semantic half, and a cancelled query could leave\n  that session unusable, so it is not budgeted.\n* A document source that raises is logged and skipped, the\n  /search/entities precedent, rather than failing the whole panel.\n* Rejected: reusing SearchableSpec (RADD-1327). It returns palette dicts\n  and cannot resolve semantic candidates by id or carry space names.\n* Dropped pages'' stale `weak_depends=(\"ai\",)` and its dead\n  AI_EMBEDDINGS_MODULE constant, left over from the spec-106 public\n  deflection that RADD-1147 deleted.\n\ntest_search_sources.py runs the same requests over the same rows twice,\nwith the plugin registered and then withdrawn the way the plugin manager\ndoes it: pages withdrawn means no documents even with a semantic source\nstill naming the page; ai withdrawn means /search is plain FTS and Ask mode\nreports disabled.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7cc4edfe5ca77234ba0e069044e05036bd59926d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/7cc4edfe5ca77234ba0e069044e05036bd59926d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/c8c54879203620426d2cd0a2c6ca28534fb41f39","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/c8c54879203620426d2cd0a2c6ca28534fb41f39","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKGM4YzU0ODc5MjAzNjIwNDI2ZDJjZDBhMmM2Y2EyODUzNGZiNDFmMzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/a216d8cc0ace57b4ddbe44859e940e8963f6ec0c","sha":"a216d8cc0ace57b4ddbe44859e940e8963f6ec0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/a216d8cc0ace57b4ddbe44859e940e8963f6ec0c"}],"sha":"c8c54879203620426d2cd0a2c6ca28534fb41f39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/c8c54879203620426d2cd0a2c6ca28534fb41f39"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/a216d8cc0ace57b4ddbe44859e940e8963f6ec0c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T11:30:01Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T11:43:56Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1386] The SLA report is the slas plugin''s own: GET /sla-report, CSAT through a weak edge, and a slas UI remote\n\nreporting is a core module, and its service imported two optional plugins at\nmodule top (slas.report, csat.report) to build the service-desk report — a\nfold that is slas''s logic and only lived in reporting for historical reasons.\nIt also forced the slas <-> reporting soft cycle the comments had to explain.\n\nBackend\n- slas/report.py is now the report: the bookkeeping read, the per-item and\n  per-week folds and CSAT. It folds with reporting''s generic machinery, now\n  public in reporting/service.py (bucket_start/bucket_starts, matching_ids,\n  report_scope), so the edge runs slas -> reporting only.\n- The endpoint is GET /sla-report (Actor, same gates as before). slas''s router\n  has no prefix and its paths are the sla- family (/sla-policies,\n  /sla-queue-items), so /sla-report follows them rather than inventing a\n  /slas prefix. /reports/sla is deleted, no forwarding.\n- CSAT is a weak edge between two optional plugins: weak_depends=(\"csat\",),\n  \"csat\" in registries.plugins checked per request, csat.report imported only\n  after it. A csat disabled at runtime drops the ratings (None/0) without a\n  restart. reporting declares no edge to slas or csat any more.\n- dashboards imported SLA_REPORT_MAX_WEEKS from reporting; it now mirrors the\n  bound locally (SLA_MAX_WEEKS), like VELOCITY_MAX_LAST, since it cannot\n  import an optional plugin.\n- Tests: the two service-level report tests (SLA counters in test_sla_depth,\n  CSAT fold in test_csat) are folded into one that pins every counter for a\n  small fixture with CSAT on, checks an unrelated project sees nothing, and\n  re-runs with the csat plugin unregistered at runtime (CSAT gone, counters\n  unchanged). The HTTP tests and the frozen anonymous inventory point at\n  /sla-report.\n\nFrontend\n- The surprise: SlaCard drew with the host chart kit (ReportCard, StackedBar-\n  and BarChart, ChartLegend, CardBody, ScopeNote, ChartHeightContext), which a\n  remote cannot import, and the SDK has no charts. Rather than grow the SDK,\n  reporting gets a BUNDLED core UI package that owns the kit (moved from\n  web/src/components/charts; host cards import @radd-plugin-ui/reporting/charts)\n  and publishes report-contract.ts: REPORT_SECTION_SLOT (reporting.section,\n  rendered by the project and global reports pages) plus card/chart slots its\n  entry contributes, so a plugin''s report draws with the same kit and the\n  dashboard widget''s plot height. The card slot''s flag is `loading`, because\n  <Slot> reserves `pending` for itself and would have swallowed it.\n- slas/ui is a new remote (ui_api 1.14.0): SlaReportCard, its query and\n  types. It contributes the report to reporting.section and draws the\n  dashboards'' builtin report_sla widget through dashboard.widget (SlaCard was\n  also the widget''s renderer). The CSAT tile shows only while csat is loaded.\n- Host lib entries for the report (query, key, path, types, colours, default\n  weeks) are deleted; a boundary test keeps the host free of the SLA report''s\n  endpoint and the old chart/card paths.\n\nLeft as it was: dashboards still declares report_sla as a BUILTIN widget type\n(enum, config, modal form). Making it a slas-contributed type needs a\nplugin-widget config form — WidgetModal sends {} for plugin types, so an edit\nwould wipe the stored project and window.\n\nEvidence: the whole backend suite (3226 passed, 4 skipped) and 86 frontend\ntests pass; ruff check src is clean; host +\n16 remotes build; web/scripts/sla-report-proof.mjs passes 13 checks against the\nreal backend (remote loaded from /plugins/slas/, tiles equal GET /sla-report on\nthe project page, the global page and a dashboard widget, /reports/sla 404s,\nno console errors, fixture cleaned up); browser-smoke and\nbrowser-issue-features still pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"099ec0988ed473a939702ef3ce85e6360d0b88c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/099ec0988ed473a939702ef3ce85e6360d0b88c2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/a216d8cc0ace57b4ddbe44859e940e8963f6ec0c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/a216d8cc0ace57b4ddbe44859e940e8963f6ec0c","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKGEyMTZkOGNjMGFjZTU3YjRkZGJlNDQ4NTllOTQwZTg5NjNmNmVjMGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/e5fec2f3050ec703473cad61020a84d1d62d572f","sha":"e5fec2f3050ec703473cad61020a84d1d62d572f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/e5fec2f3050ec703473cad61020a84d1d62d572f"}],"sha":"a216d8cc0ace57b4ddbe44859e940e8963f6ec0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/a216d8cc0ace57b4ddbe44859e940e8963f6ec0c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/e5fec2f3050ec703473cad61020a84d1d62d572f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T11:32:40Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T11:43:56Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1390] No host edit per plugin page: settings rows say where they live, nav icons come from one registry\n\nAfter the settings moves, two host lists still had to be edited whenever a plugin gained a page:\n\n- INSTANCE_/PROJECT_HOMED_SECTIONS named the sections ldap, ai, mailintake, sso and others render\n  themselves. General renders by subtraction, so a page missing from the list showed its rows twice.\n- The settings nav''s PascalCase iconByName whitelist gained five names in this wave alone.\n  Automations'' \"Zap\" was never added, so its entry drew the fallback glyph. Meanwhile lib/icons.ts\n  was already the host''s curated, shared registry, with \"zap\" in it.\n\nNow:\n- SettingSpec.page_scopes says at which scopes the owning plugin renders a setting on its own\n  page. Setting rows carry `homed`, and General renders !homed. Against the dev instance the flag\n  reproduces the old lists exactly: 35 instance rows (30 homed, 5 on General), 7 project rows\n  (3 homed), zero mismatches.\n- Manifests name nav icons in kebab-case from lib/icons.ts, which gained the nine names plugins\n  declare. The settings nav, the main sidebar and the rail resolve them there. The main sidebar\n  had drawn Layers for every plugin link, whatever the manifest said.\n- A boundary test refuses a nav icon the registry does not ship.\n\nNot done: groups'' audit link still points at /settings/directory, ldap''s page. The kernel only lets\nan entity''s owner declare its link (a sound rule), and no core page lists groups. The link degrades\nto the \"page unavailable\" notice when ldap is off.\n\nProof: settings-surfaces-proof.mjs, all passing against :8000.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"50a0b601ce452831741648bd42a123cb391a1af4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/50a0b601ce452831741648bd42a123cb391a1af4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/e5fec2f3050ec703473cad61020a84d1d62d572f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/e5fec2f3050ec703473cad61020a84d1d62d572f","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKGU1ZmVjMmYzMDUwZWM3MDM0NzNjYWQ2MTAyMGE4NGQxZDYyZDU3MmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/573c8db29f0881ab5c45d07b6a143a58147b1136","sha":"573c8db29f0881ab5c45d07b6a143a58147b1136","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/573c8db29f0881ab5c45d07b6a143a58147b1136"}],"sha":"e5fec2f3050ec703473cad61020a84d1d62d572f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/e5fec2f3050ec703473cad61020a84d1d62d572f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/573c8db29f0881ab5c45d07b6a143a58147b1136/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T11:23:21Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T11:43:56Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1383] Approval gates are a transition check the approvals plugin contributes through a kernel socket\n\napprovals is an optional plugin (core=False), yet core workflow and items\nhardcoded it: TransitionCheck.REQUIRE_APPROVAL and ApproverKind lived in\nworkflow''s vocabulary, workflow validated and evaluated the rule, and both\nworkflow (snapshot) and items (single update + cross-project move) called\napprovals.service behind `try: import ... except ImportError`. That except\nnever fires: plugin code is always importable, so a plugin disabled at runtime\n- which only withdraws it from the kernel registries - kept running from those\ncall sites.\n\nNow:\n- kernel/sockets.py gains Socket.TRANSITION_CHECK and a TransitionCheckProvider\n  protocol: check key, sort_last, validate (write path, returns the params to\n  store or raises the 409), prepare (per-item data, once per evaluation), a pure\n  failure(params, prepared, to_state_id), and moved (after every state change).\n- workflow evaluates only its own checks (require_field, resolved threads,\n  release) and hands every other key to the live provider (workflow/checks.py is\n  the seam). TransitionRule.check is an open string validated in\n  _validate_rules. workflow.service.state_moved is the public \"moved\" seam; items\n  calls it on both paths instead of importing approvals. The \"approvals\" weak\n  edge is gone from workflow and items.\n- approvals serves require_approval from gate.py (IntegrationSpec on its\n  manifest); validation, name snapshots, the failure sentence and consume moved\n  into it. ApprovalCheck/ApproverKind are its own constants.\n- SPA: workflow''s bundled UI package publishes transition-rule-contract.ts (slot\n  workflow.transition.rule). TransitionsSection renders the slot where the\n  hardcoded approver editor was, keeps contributed rules after its own (approval\n  still sorts last), and the approvals remote contributes the \"Require approval\"\n  editor with SDK DirectorySelect pickers. ApproverEntry and requireApproval\n  left web/src/lib/types.\n\nFail-closed decision: a stored rule whose check has no loaded provider REFUSES\nthe move (''this move requires \"require_approval\", but the plugin that provides\nit is disabled''), even when an approved request is banked. Skipping it would\nquietly open a gate an admin configured. The previous `evaluate` skipped unknown\nchecks, and that unit test now asserts the opposite. Two consequences, both\nhandled:\n- An update may keep such a rule unchanged. Otherwise editing a row''s other\n  rules would force deleting the gate.\n- The transitions editor shows a fail-closed notice with a Remove control for a\n  contributed rule that no loaded editor claims (it reads each contribution''s\n  `match`).\n\nSurprises:\n- The contract prop could not be called `pending`. <Slot> owns a `pending` prop\n  (what to show while remotes load) and keeps it instead of forwarding it, so\n  the editor would never have seen the save state. The prop is named `saving`.\n- An unknown check key on write is now a 409 from _validate_rules instead of the\n  pydantic 422, because a stored rule from a disabled plugin must still READ\n  (TransitionRead shares the model).\n\nVerified: new tests/test_transition_check_socket.py (the real approvals plugin\nunregistered at runtime: fail-closed even with a banked approval, new rule\nrefused, stored rule kept through an edit; re-registered: one approval unlocks\nexactly one move; a mutation back to \"skip\" fails it). Full backend suite green.\nbrowser-resolvable-threads.mjs now loads the actual approvals remote and checks\nlive withdrawal. New real-backend proof approval-rule-editor-proof.mjs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3b40906668dff8608db3bbcbbb71d5d4ca2b8cde","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/3b40906668dff8608db3bbcbbb71d5d4ca2b8cde"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/573c8db29f0881ab5c45d07b6a143a58147b1136","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/573c8db29f0881ab5c45d07b6a143a58147b1136","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDU3M2M4ZGIyOWYwODgxYWI1YzQ1ZDA3YjZhMTQzYTU4MTQ3YjExMzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/f54289a0f4d815ac7414f09d9fcaf2e2f78754e5","sha":"f54289a0f4d815ac7414f09d9fcaf2e2f78754e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/f54289a0f4d815ac7414f09d9fcaf2e2f78754e5"}],"sha":"573c8db29f0881ab5c45d07b6a143a58147b1136","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/573c8db29f0881ab5c45d07b6a143a58147b1136"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/f54289a0f4d815ac7414f09d9fcaf2e2f78754e5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T11:19:18Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T11:43:56Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1389] Server status lists what plugins report; Outbound email reads the sender rows\n\nOn an instance whose mail is configured through sender rows, Server status said Outbound email\nwas Off. The `smtp` capability lived in the core capabilities module and checked\nRADD_SMTP_HOST, the env seed RADD-983 made optional; this dev instance has none and sends mail\nfine. It was the same defect RADD-1265 fixed for send_email, left on the status page.\n\nThe page''s endpoint was the deeper problem. /instance/status lived in the core projects module,\nand its typed schema had sso_enabled, ldap_enabled, ldap_bind_account, smtp_configured and\nai_provider. That made four optional plugins part of a core contract, and the ldap remote read\nthe endpoint just to learn its own bind-account state.\n\n- The capability is mailintake''s `outbound_mail`, read from the snapshot it already keeps of\n  its enabled sender rows.\n- /capabilities rows name their owning plugin, and a check may return a one-line `summary`.\n- /instance/status and InstanceStatusRead are deleted.\n- Server status renders every non-connector capability, linked through its plugin''s settings\n  page, and folds connectors into one row. It refetches on mount instead of relying on an entity\n  tag every plugin would have to know.\n- The Directory page reads the ldap capability.\n\nProof: server-status-proof.mjs, 18/18 against the dev server.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"123a805d82af5c7136b60e4e7b0e57b642e87568","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/123a805d82af5c7136b60e4e7b0e57b642e87568"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/f54289a0f4d815ac7414f09d9fcaf2e2f78754e5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/f54289a0f4d815ac7414f09d9fcaf2e2f78754e5","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKGY1NDI4OWEwZjRkODE1YWM3NDE0ZjA5ZDlmY2FmMmUyZjc4NzU0ZTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/50a5b48b4b2ce6421920191ccd0ec77aa31b2d58","sha":"50a5b48b4b2ce6421920191ccd0ec77aa31b2d58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/50a5b48b4b2ce6421920191ccd0ec77aa31b2d58"}],"sha":"f54289a0f4d815ac7414f09d9fcaf2e2f78754e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/f54289a0f4d815ac7414f09d9fcaf2e2f78754e5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/50a5b48b4b2ce6421920191ccd0ec77aa31b2d58/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T11:10:15Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T11:43:56Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1380] Settings → Sign-in: the SSO provider registry is the sso plugin''s remote, a section of the host''s page\n\nsso is an optional plugin (core=False), yet its whole admin UI — the\nprovider registry, create/edit/test, the signup domain allowlist, starting\naccess and provisioning rules — was host code under\nweb/src/components/settings/signin, with its types, queries and API paths in\nweb/src/lib. A plugin the host carries cannot be withdrawn by disabling it.\n\nWhat changed\n- New remote server/src/radd/modules/sso/ui (modelled on alertmanager''s):\n  ProvidersPanel, ProviderDialog, StartingAccess, StartingRoleDialog (moved,\n  so git keeps their history), plus types.ts / queries.ts owning /sso/providers,\n  /sso/kinds and /sso/provisioning-references. The manifest declares\n  PluginUiManifest(remote=…, ui_api_version=\"1.14.0\") with NO nav item.\n- It contributes a settings.section matched to \"sign-in\", with the domain-list\n  and account-joining explanation that used to be the page''s info banner.\n- Only platform surfaces are imported: host components through the SDK, the\n  Projects picker through @radd-plugin-ui/projects/picker-contract, and a\n  provider''s history through the entity.history slot (all ChangeHistoryPanel did).\n\nDecisions\n- The page stays the HOST''s. Settings → Sign-in also carries the instance MFA\n  policy (signin.mfa), which the CORE auth module declares, not sso. The page\n  cannot go when sso is disabled, so sso adds a section to it and has no page\n  of its own. The layout row lost its plugin: \"sso\" marker, so the tab no longer\n  vanishes with the plugin. Description and banner are now generic. The page''s\n  history link covers scoped_setting only, following Time logging''s precedent\n  (it does not list Leave''s entity). A provider''s own history is still in its\n  edit dialog.\n- settingsPathForPlugin: sso keeps its Plugins-page \"settings\" link without the\n  host naming it. A settings.section key IS the page''s route segment. Settings →\n  Plugins passes each plugin''s registered section keys, and the function falls\n  back, last, to the page at /settings/<key>, whether a host tab or a\n  plugin-contributed one. Side effects: Leave now links to Time logging, where\n  before it had no link. mailintake now links to Monitoring, where its\n  mail-health card lives. A plugin''s own page or table entry still wins, so AI\n  is unchanged.\n- The login page''s provider buttons stay in the host. They render before\n  sign-in, when no remote can load. web/src/lib/types/sso.ts keeps only\n  SsoKind and SsoProviderPublic.\n- Dropped rather than reached for: the panel used to invalidate the host''s\n  instance-status query after a write. A remote cannot name a host query key,\n  and that query carries no entity tag, so Server status reads sso_enabled up\n  to 60 s stale. Alertmanager''s remote has the same behaviour.\n- Moved code no longer uses the raw palette. amber/emerald/red-400 became the\n  status tier (text-status-*-ink, border-status-*/40). Dark mode is identical;\n  light mode now gets the computed ink. The redirect URI''s Copy uses the SDK''s\n  copyText, and shows \"Copied\" only when text was actually copied. Plain-http\n  installs have no Clipboard API.\n\nSurprising on the way\n- Two unit tests read web/src/lib/queries/provisioning.ts as SOURCE\n  (audit-regressions, query-cancellation). They now read the plugin''s\n  queries.ts, as the teams remote''s references already are. Both still assert\n  the realtime refresh on role/project/team frames.\n- The proof''s client-side \"sso withdrawn\" phase first passed through untouched:\n  the host api hands fetch a URL object, not a string. That failure is also how\n  the check was seen to discriminate.\n\nEvidence\n- web/scripts/signin-settings-page-proof.mjs, against a real backend: 14 checks.\n  - MFA and provider sections on one page.\n  - The section is fetched from /plugins/sso/, and no loaded host chunk carries it.\n  - The existing providers render.\n  - A disabled throwaway OIDC provider is created and removed through the UI.\n  - Plugins → sso links to Sign-in.\n  - With sso filtered out of the manifest in-browser only, the page, the tab\n    and the MFA switch remain and the providers do not.\n  - Signed out, /login draws the provider buttons without the remote.\n  - No console errors.\n- plugin-boundaries.test.mjs: a new test refuses /sso/…, \"sso\" and\n  \"sso_provider\" literals in web/src. It would have caught four at the parent.\n- node --test web/scripts/*.test.mjs: 86/86.\n- pytest test_frontend_federation, test_module_contracts and\n  test_sso_providers: 52 passed.\n- browser-settings-ownership, browser-login and browser-plugin-pages still pass.\n- tsc -b, vite build and build-all are clean: 17 bundled plugins, 16 remotes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b1b6230dc21bb7efb2c151925b7f9765ae4a29bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/b1b6230dc21bb7efb2c151925b7f9765ae4a29bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/50a5b48b4b2ce6421920191ccd0ec77aa31b2d58","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/50a5b48b4b2ce6421920191ccd0ec77aa31b2d58","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDUwYTViNDhiNGIyY2U2NDIxOTIwMTkxY2NkMGVjNzdhYTMxYjJkNTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/6eff089fc3261cc1903274c135b9075a919956f9","sha":"6eff089fc3261cc1903274c135b9075a919956f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/6eff089fc3261cc1903274c135b9075a919956f9"}],"sha":"50a5b48b4b2ce6421920191ccd0ec77aa31b2d58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/50a5b48b4b2ce6421920191ccd0ec77aa31b2d58"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/6eff089fc3261cc1903274c135b9075a919956f9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T11:09:51Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T11:43:56Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1382] The Jira and Confluence importers own their pages; Import is a nav group, not a host hub\n\nBoth importers are optional plugins (core=False), yet they lived in the host SPA:\n- their settings pages, about 3,200 lines for Jira and 1,300 for Confluence;\n- their types, queries and API paths;\n- the Import data hub, a host page that named jiraimport and confluenceimport by plugin name,\n  plus a special case in settingsPathForPlugin.\n\nNone of it could be withdrawn with its plugin. This commit folds two agents'' halves into one.\n\n- jiraimport/ui and confluenceimport/ui are new federated remotes. They contribute their pages\n  at the same paths, /settings/jira-import and /settings/confluence-import.\n- Their manifests declare nav items in the \"Import\" group (Jira: DatabaseZap; Confluence:\n  BookUp; admin-only; UI API 1.14.0). The settings sidebar already gives a contributed group its\n  own heading, so Import is a group importers contribute to. The hub, its route and constants,\n  and the special case are deleted, and a new importer needs no host edit.\n- The hub''s procedure line became each page''s description, and the \"← Import data\" back-links\n  are gone.\n- Each remote owns its transport under its own query keys and reads what it maps onto through\n  owners'' public REST or contributions:\n  - Jira: /states, /issue-types, /teams, /users, /projects/by-key, and the fields plugin''s\n    fields.catalog query source.\n  - Confluence: the page-spaces and groups option directories, and GET /pages/extensions.\n  - Rejected: importing another plugin''s query functions. The boundary test allows only\n    contract files (types and data).\n- Files over about 300 lines were split. Raw palette tints became status and callout tokens.\n- Deleted from the host: both routes, components/settings/{jira,confluence}/*,\n  lib/{types,queries}/{jira*,confluence*}, their query keys, API paths, and barrel exports.\n\nProofs: jira-import-page-proof.mjs 18/18 and confluence-import-page-proof.mjs 14/14 on their\nown backends; import-mapping-proof.mjs 4/4 after the merge (its harness now mounts both\nremotes'' sources with the bundled plugins registered).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8384fbe36461fea3cefc3e75f9a32f032b8f9eaf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/8384fbe36461fea3cefc3e75f9a32f032b8f9eaf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/6eff089fc3261cc1903274c135b9075a919956f9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/6eff089fc3261cc1903274c135b9075a919956f9","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDZlZmYwODlmYzMyNjFjYzE5MDMyNzRjMTM1YjkwNzVhOTE5OTU2Zjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/8222e4042fa0629948ce6a1d6dd8447c4170f34a","sha":"8222e4042fa0629948ce6a1d6dd8447c4170f34a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/8222e4042fa0629948ce6a1d6dd8447c4170f34a"}],"sha":"6eff089fc3261cc1903274c135b9075a919956f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/6eff089fc3261cc1903274c135b9075a919956f9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/8222e4042fa0629948ce6a1d6dd8447c4170f34a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T11:09:40Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T11:43:56Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1378] Settings → Email is the mailintake plugin''s own page\n\nmailintake is an optional plugin (core=False), but its settings page lived in\nthe host: a route, a hardcoded Server-group nav entry, eleven components, and\nthe queries, keys, paths and wire types behind them. Disabling the plugin left\na tab whose every fetch 404''d. The page now sits in mailintake''s existing\nremote, like Alertmanager''s (RADD-1370):\n\n- mailintake/ui gains SettingsPage + the sources, senders, routing, signature\n  and automatic-message panels (git-moved, so history follows), api.ts (paths\n  and [\"mail\", ...] query keys) and types.ts. It is contributed as settings.page\n  at /settings/email. Its nav is declared on the manifest (Server, Mail,\n  order 45 so it keeps its old place after Storage, admin-only), and\n  ui_api_version rises to 1.14.0 for ScopedSettings.\n- Automatic messages render through the SDK''s ScopedSettings. Project pickers\n  are the projects plugin''s PROJECT_SELECT_SLOT: a remote cannot import\n  directory-queries, and the picker only loads a bounded catalog when opened,\n  where the old dialogs downloaded every project. The routing list gets the\n  project keys it prints from the SDK''s useProjectsQuery. The test dialog''s raw\n  emerald/red tints are now the house Callout.\n- The host loses the route, RoutePath.settingsEmail, SettingsSection.email,\n  ApiPath.mail*/apiMail*Path, lib/queries/mail-admin.ts, the mail* query keys\n  and the Mail* types. Nothing else in the host used them. The \"email\" entry in\n  INSTANCE_HOMED_SECTIONS stays: General still needs it.\n\nDeleteProjectCard. It linked every blocker with a hint to\nRoutePath.settingsEmail, which was right only because mail was the only\nblocker. I considered keeping a plain \"/settings/email\" link for mail_* kinds,\nbut that still names the plugin''s route in the host. Instead, a blocker''s kind\nis already its owner''s entity type, and mailintake already declares entity\nlinks for mail_source and mail_rule. So projects/router.py resolves each\nblocker through resolve_entity_link, BlockerRead carries that url, and the\ndialog links the hint only when there is one. The heading is now \"Something\nstill depends on this project\", no longer about mail. Server status''s Email\nrow, a second host link into the page that the brief didn''t list, now links\nthrough settingsPathForPlugin(\"mailintake\", manifest). A disabled plugin gives\nno link rather than a dead one.\n\nFound on the way:\n- mail-routing-trace-proof called process.exit inside its try, so its finally\n  (which deletes the two sources it seeds) never ran. Every run left \"Trace\n  proof <stamp>\" sources behind, and two are still on the dev instance. The\n  exit now comes after the finally. Older leftovers were not touched.\n- mail-settings-proof looked for \"Add source\"/\"Add sender\" buttons, which were\n  renamed \"New source\"/\"New sender\" some time ago. It could not have passed\n  before this change.\n- project-delete-proof asserted the old \"routes mail\" heading; it now checks\n  the generic one.\n\nGuard: plugin-boundaries.test.mjs refuses /mail/{sources,senders,rules,kinds}\nand /settings/email literals in web/src, and fails if the deleted files come\nback.\n\nEvidence: email-settings-page-proof.mjs, 25 checks against the real backend.\nIt covers: no email chunk and no page copy in the host build; nav once, after\nStorage; four sections plus the three ScopedSettings rows; the page served\nfrom /plugins/mailintake/; the picker resolving the default project; a rename\nread back over the API; the blocker url; the status-row link; deleting the\nsource through the page; cleanup. Also: mail-settings 18/18, mail-routing-trace\n15/15, email-automatic-messages 9/9 (settings restored), project-delete 17/17.\nMocked: settings-ownership, plugin-pages, plugin-availability,\naudit-entity-links. 86/86 node tests; 50 backend tests (federation, module\ncontracts, kernel, capabilities, sdk, project delete, entity links).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"569403b151168d8b938b9bb0568bfcf3eda5c94e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/569403b151168d8b938b9bb0568bfcf3eda5c94e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/8222e4042fa0629948ce6a1d6dd8447c4170f34a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/8222e4042fa0629948ce6a1d6dd8447c4170f34a","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKDgyMjJlNDA0MmZhMDYyOTk0OGNlNmExZDZkZDg0NDdjNDE3MGYzNGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/f7f17c7554bd3ec18d66fec84815b9cf57f741c2","sha":"f7f17c7554bd3ec18d66fec84815b9cf57f741c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/f7f17c7554bd3ec18d66fec84815b9cf57f741c2"}],"sha":"8222e4042fa0629948ce6a1d6dd8447c4170f34a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/8222e4042fa0629948ce6a1d6dd8447c4170f34a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/f7f17c7554bd3ec18d66fec84815b9cf57f741c2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T11:08:37Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T11:43:56Z","email":"hussein@hjarrar.com","name":"Hussein Jarrar"},"message":"[RADD-1381] Settings → Directory is the ldap plugin''s own remote; the host keeps no page, route or vocabulary for it\n\nThe Directory page (connection, user sync + AD import with spec-88 duplicate\nresolution, group browse, mirrored groups and their role grants) lived in the\nhost SPA although ldap is an optional plugin, so disabling ldap left a host\npage whose every fetch 404''d, and the host carried ldap''s endpoint paths,\nquery keys and import types. RADD-1377 gave the SDK the three surfaces the\npage needed (ScopedSettings, RoleGrants, toast), so it can move now.\n\n- ldap/ui is a new remote (UI API 1.14.0) contributing settings.page at the\n  same /settings/directory path; the nav entry is on the ldap manifest\n  (Server group, FolderTree, admin-only, order 55 = between Email and\n  Sign-in). The plugin owns its paths, query keys and import types; the host\n  lost the route, RoutePath.settingsDirectory, SettingsSection.directory,\n  the ldap ApiPath/queryKeys/queries, the Directory*/Import* types and the\n  eleven SettingKey.ldap* constants nothing read. DirectorySyncResult stays\n  in teams.ts: the Teams panel''s per-team reconcile uses it.\n- The three sections render through ScopedSettings, a mirrored group''s\n  grants through RoleGrants, pushToast became toast. The StatusPill import\n  from instance.tsx became the plugin''s own StatusRow; the host''s StatusPill\n  stays for the Server page (now module-local, its only user).\n- Links into the page no longer name it: the Server-status LDAP row and the\n  Users page''s \"Import from AD\" point at settingsPathForPlugin(\"ldap\",\n  manifest), so both disappear with the plugin instead of dead-ending.\n- The /settings/groups redirect (RADD-931''s retired tab) was a legacy path\n  naming the page; deleted with SettingsSection.groups, and the cleanup\n  proof''s check for it removed.\n- Along the way: raw palette (sky/amber/emerald/red) became status tokens and\n  SDK Chips; the hand-rolled row action buttons are kit Buttons; \"Add to\n  team\" picks through the Teams plugin''s teams/directory option source\n  instead of an unpaged /teams list; ImportGroupsDialog''s in-dialog search\n  mode was dead (every caller passed preselected groups) and is gone; a group\n  import now also refreshes the mirror table; the \"back to Server settings\"\n  link claimed the page had no nav tab, which has been false since RADD-931,\n  and is gone.\n- A boundary test refuses /ldap/* and /settings/directory literals in\n  web/src and the old files'' return.\n\nEvidence: directory-settings-page-proof.mjs, 23 checks against a real backend\nand the live AD (nav once under Server and ordered, remote loaded from\n/plugins/ldap/, no host chunk, status + all three tabs'' settings, last-run\nlines, live group browse, mirrored groups expanding to role grants, import\ndialog searching and closing with nothing selected, a group-sync-interval\nedit saved from the page and Reset back, no console errors); 86 frontend\ntests; 102 federation/contract/ldap/directory/capability tests plus 96\nkernel/sdk/plugin/route tests; browser-settings-ownership,\nbrowser-directory-contributions and browser-plugin-pages pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"53ec7b0e832e96abbc3b2624fbf99694cdbdba01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/trees/53ec7b0e832e96abbc3b2624fbf99694cdbdba01"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/git/commits/f7f17c7554bd3ec18d66fec84815b9cf57f741c2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116394085?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hjarrar","id":116394085,"login":"hjarrar","node_id":"U_kgDOBvAIZQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hjarrar","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/f7f17c7554bd3ec18d66fec84815b9cf57f741c2","node_id":"C_kwDOUWhBVdoAKGY3ZjE3Yzc1NTRiZDNlYzE4ZDY2ZmVjODQ4MTViOWNmNTdmNzQxYzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Radd-HQ/Radd/commit/9f306c276df1df0d0da9023ab2c680f731a2de3d","sha":"9f306c276df1df0d0da9023ab2c680f731a2de3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/9f306c276df1df0d0da9023ab2c680f731a2de3d"}],"sha":"f7f17c7554bd3ec18d66fec84815b9cf57f741c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits/f7f17c7554bd3ec18d66fec84815b9cf57f741c2"}],"requestUrl":"https://api.github.com/repos/Radd-HQ/Radd/commits?per_page=100&page=1&sha=85e0931add24d91ecaef1324eec71c23f381a2f7&since=2025-03-31T23%3A59%3A59.000Z&until=2026-10-08T16%3A20%3A01.669Z"}');
