owers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blazux","id":16634590,"login":"blazux","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NjM0NTkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commits/35b667727b64d82569711c0866cd927e695bde47/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T23:02:05Z","email":"vincent.blazutti@protonmail.com","name":"Blazux"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T23:02:05Z","email":"vincent.blazutti@protonmail.com","name":"Blazux"},"message":"README: multi-client responsiveness (issue #9) and re-measured kernel numbers after PR #10\n\n- New section under Throughput and concurrency: why a decoding client drops\n  to 0.2 tok/s while other clients prefill (vLLM''s single-step chunked prefill\n  at ~2,400 tok/s: one decode token per 8,192-token step, plus cold n-gram\n  lookups), the --long-prefill-token-threshold sweep measured on the GX10\n  (none / 2048 / 1024 / 512: decoding client 0.2 -> 0.5 -> 1.0 -> 1.7 tok/s,\n  single-stream 8k prefill -0 / ? / -36% / -49%), and the guidance: default\n  stays 8,192 for a single main user; 1024 (or 512) plus GPU_MEM=0.75,\n  PREWARM=1, small swap and SEQS=4 for several interactive agents. Reported\n  by @kutovoy.\n- Deterministic top-k numbers re-measured with the 2026-09-07 kernel pin\n  (PR #10, @jschmied): 4/4 deterministic, decode 31.8 tok/s, prefill 2,488 /\n  2,996 tok/s, needle 46.3 s. Dockerfile comment and HOW-IT-WORKS updated.\n- EXTRA row in the tuning table now shows the two useful examples.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"be33567005226ac04edf7e39876d2656ce9fd24a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/git/trees/be33567005226ac04edf7e39876d2656ce9fd24a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/git/commits/35b667727b64d82569711c0866cd927e695bde47","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16634590?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blazux","id":16634590,"login":"blazux","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NjM0NTkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commit/35b667727b64d82569711c0866cd927e695bde47","node_id":"C_kwDOUXaI9doAKDM1YjY2NzcyN2I2NGQ4MjU2OTcxMWMwODY2Y2Q5MjdlNjk1YmRlNDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commit/0022e36465ae9803c24eb7ae5ac59672be47ad18","sha":"0022e36465ae9803c24eb7ae5ac59672be47ad18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commits/0022e36465ae9803c24eb7ae5ac59672be47ad18"}],"sha":"35b667727b64d82569711c0866cd927e695bde47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commits/35b667727b64d82569711c0866cd927e695bde47"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commits/0022e36465ae9803c24eb7ae5ac59672be47ad18/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T15:32:19Z","email":"juergenschmied70@gmail.com","name":"Jürgen Schmied"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T15:32:19Z","email":"juergenschmied70@gmail.com","name":"Jürgen Schmied"},"message":"patch 8: bump the deterministic top-k pin (correctness fix + the kernel got much faster)\n\nThe pin was from 2026-09-03. Two of the changes since are correctness, not speed:\n\n* Signed zero. -0.0 and +0.0 are numerically equal but have different bit patterns, and the radix\n  select orders on the bit pattern, so the pinned kernel can still order two equal scores\n  inconsistently -- in the patch whose whole purpose is to remove that. Now canonicalised.\n* A deterministic low-shared-memory fallback (force_single_cta). The pinned version has no\n  deterministic path when the row does not fit the cooperative launch.\n\nAnd a launcher bug that would have bitten this image: the chunk was sized from the opt-in shared\nmemory rather than the opt-in minus the kernel''s own static __shared__, so the request exceeded the\ncap and the launch was REJECTED for every row of 24576 or 49152 elements at 32 or 64 rows. Long\ncontexts on the QSA path reach those widths.\n\nSpeed, GB10, ratio to the stock kernel over a 43-shape grid: was 1.25-4.31x, now 0.74-2.14x, with\n18 cells at or below stock. The prefill numbers in the README were measured against the old version\nand should improve; I did not touch them, since you should measure your own.\n\nVerified the way this Dockerfile builds it -- build_det.py over a copy of patches/kernel-det --\nDET_ARCH=121a clean and 210/210 on the determinism/exactness suite, plus a 120a cross-compile for\nthe RTX 5090 path documented above. Both new checksums verified against the live raw URLs.\n\nKM4_SHA (patch 9) is unchanged -- that file has not moved since your pin.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011SuBgdp87NbfLbiigmzn1z","tree":{"sha":"d12a11d1300de661637ada6ef7eab123ac7bfe1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/git/trees/d12a11d1300de661637ada6ef7eab123ac7bfe1f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/git/commits/0022e36465ae9803c24eb7ae5ac59672be47ad18","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commit/0022e36465ae9803c24eb7ae5ac59672be47ad18","node_id":"C_kwDOUXaI9doAKDAwMjJlMzY0NjVhZTk4MDNjMjRlYjdhZTVhYzU5NjcyYmU0N2FkMTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commit/656cdb075b57671c9bd6807b57f630fb3c1641fe","sha":"656cdb075b57671c9bd6807b57f630fb3c1641fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commits/656cdb075b57671c9bd6807b57f630fb3c1641fe"}],"sha":"0022e36465ae9803c24eb7ae5ac59672be47ad18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commits/0022e36465ae9803c24eb7ae5ac59672be47ad18"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16634590?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blazux","id":16634590,"login":"blazux","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NjM0NTkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commits/656cdb075b57671c9bd6807b57f630fb3c1641fe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T23:10:23Z","email":"vincent.blazutti@protonmail.com","name":"Blazux"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T23:10:23Z","email":"vincent.blazutti@protonmail.com","name":"Blazux"},"message":"serve.sh: make the post-start check actually pass on a running container; clean up after a failed docker run\n\nFollow-up to the three commits cherry-picked from sternnick/qwen3.8-Flash-DGX\n(fix/measured-sizes, fix/ple-mmap-guard, fix/scripts-preflight):\n\n- The new start check compared the whole ''status exit=N oom=B'' string with\n  ''running'', so it reported ''!! not running'' and exited 1 on every launch,\n  including a healthy one (the container kept running in the background).\n  Match on the status word only.\n- If docker run itself fails (port already bound, ...) set -e exited before\n  the check and left a Created container behind; a trap removes it now.\n- README: fix the ****...**** typo in the disk requirement, finalize the\n  credit line in the update section.\n\nTested on the GX10: the public recipe (NVFP4, defaults) boots from the\naudit image via scripts/serve.sh, smoke-test passes (metrics-proven\nprefix-cache hit 0 -> 8000 tokens, deterministic, guard counter 0), the\ncheck accepts the running container, and a busy-port failure leaves no\ncontainer.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e69b7a8c826e1c32c759ecceea0d3123ba41cbc6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/git/trees/e69b7a8c826e1c32c759ecceea0d3123ba41cbc6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/git/commits/656cdb075b57671c9bd6807b57f630fb3c1641fe","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16634590?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blazux","id":16634590,"login":"blazux","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NjM0NTkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commit/656cdb075b57671c9bd6807b57f630fb3c1641fe","node_id":"C_kwDOUXaI9doAKDY1NmNkYjA3NWI1NzY3MWM5YmQ2ODA3YjU3ZjYzMGZiM2MxNjQxZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commit/0d68a9f5ead6b105d73c44fbb873233df4c90fb9","sha":"0d68a9f5ead6b105d73c44fbb873233df4c90fb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commits/0d68a9f5ead6b105d73c44fbb873233df4c90fb9"}],"sha":"656cdb075b57671c9bd6807b57f630fb3c1641fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commits/656cdb075b57671c9bd6807b57f630fb3c1641fe"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commits/0d68a9f5ead6b105d73c44fbb873233df4c90fb9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T10:05:03Z","email":"nick@local","name":"nick"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T22:51:37Z","email":"vincent.blazutti@protonmail.com","name":"Blazux"},"message":"fix(scripts): resolve the snapshot from refs, fail when the container does not start, prove the prefix-cache hit\n\n1. snapshot selection. serve.sh:57 and prepare-hybrid.sh:24 both picked\n   ''ls -d snapshots/*/ | grep -v -fp8hybrid | head -1'', i.e. whatever sorts\n   first. A cache holding two revisions (a pinned commit plus refs/main) then\n   serves a different checkpoint than the one HF points at, and the two scripts\n   can disagree with each other. Read refs/main or refs/master first and fall\n   back to newest-by-mtime; both scripts now use the same rule.\n\n2. serve.sh printed ''starting on :PORT'' after docker run -d without checking\n   anything: a busy port or a missing image leaves a dead container and an\n   exit-0 script. Probe the state, dump the last log lines and exit 1.\n\n3. smoke-test.sh judged prefix caching by wall time (dt2 < dt/2). With the PLE\n   table on NVMe that is exactly the wrong instrument - the README itself says\n   a second pass is 2-3x faster once the rows are in the page cache\n   (docs/HOW-IT-WORKS.md:139), so a server with PREFIX_CACHE=0 can print\n   ''prefix-cache HIT''. Read vllm:prefix_cache_hits_total from /metrics instead\n   and fall back to timing with an explicit caveat when /metrics is absent.\n\n(cherry picked from commit 9bc5f767c858c7369f81427922e585331c6dad7d)","tree":{"sha":"609478749de6f308160a2bd04a1801e6c5b28c35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/git/trees/609478749de6f308160a2bd04a1801e6c5b28c35"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/git/commits/0d68a9f5ead6b105d73c44fbb873233df4c90fb9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16634590?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blazux","id":16634590,"login":"blazux","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NjM0NTkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commit/0d68a9f5ead6b105d73c44fbb873233df4c90fb9","node_id":"C_kwDOUXaI9doAKDBkNjhhOWY1ZWFkNmIxMDVkNzNjNDRmYmI4NzMyMzNkZjRjOTBmYjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commit/0431883f05fccd5afb0702be2324977d4b086e87","sha":"0431883f05fccd5afb0702be2324977d4b086e87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commits/0431883f05fccd5afb0702be2324977d4b086e87"}],"sha":"0d68a9f5ead6b105d73c44fbb873233df4c90fb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commits/0d68a9f5ead6b105d73c44fbb873233df4c90fb9"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commits/0431883f05fccd5afb0702be2324977d4b086e87/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T09:58:27Z","email":"nick@local","name":"nick"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T22:51:37Z","email":"vincent.blazutti@protonmail.com","name":"Blazux"},"message":"fix(ple_mmap): range guard used a padded bound; drop the __cols__ dict hack\n\nThe last PLE shard is partial, so parts * shard_size is larger than rows_total.\nBoth guards compared ids against shard_size * len(mm) while printing rows_total,\nso an id in [rows_total, parts * shard_size) got past the guard and blew up later\nin self.mm[si] with an unrelated ''list index out of range'' instead of the intended\nmessage. Compare against rows_total, which is what the message already promises.\n\nAlso stop smuggling the column count through a string key ''__cols__'' injected into\na dict[int, tuple] and popped by the caller: _find_shards returns it as a fourth\nelement, which also corrects the stale 3-tuple scale_entry docstring and type hints\n(the code has been building a 4-tuple).\n\nAdded case exercises the inline and the multi-task pooled gather with an id past\nthe last row. It does NOT fail on main - the fixture''s table is an exact fit\n(8 x 12500 == rows_total), so no id can sit in the padded window; the test locks\nthe guard to the value its own message prints, it is not a regression demo.\n\n(cherry picked from commit b74a7a3df6dcfde7dda55c58477e68be501efb31)","tree":{"sha":"28b17caffbaa0802eb06e6c1faf7b358b43197f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/git/trees/28b17caffbaa0802eb06e6c1faf7b358b43197f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/git/commits/0431883f05fccd5afb0702be2324977d4b086e87","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16634590?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blazux","id":16634590,"login":"blazux","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NjM0NTkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commit/0431883f05fccd5afb0702be2324977d4b086e87","node_id":"C_kwDOUXaI9doAKDA0MzE4ODNmMDVmY2NkNWFmYjA3MDJiZTIzMjQ5NzdkNGIwODZlODc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commit/daa3a11a8ffcad70b1a83db6f118c96557b68fbb","sha":"daa3a11a8ffcad70b1a83db6f118c96557b68fbb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commits/daa3a11a8ffcad70b1a83db6f118c96557b68fbb"}],"sha":"0431883f05fccd5afb0702be2324977d4b086e87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commits/0431883f05fccd5afb0702be2324977d4b086e87"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commits/daa3a11a8ffcad70b1a83db6f118c96557b68fbb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T09:53:22Z","email":"nick@local","name":"nick"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T22:51:37Z","email":"vincent.blazutti@protonmail.com","name":"Blazux"},"message":"docs: correct checkpoint and PLE table sizes against the published repo\n\nMeasured from the Hugging Face Hub API for RadixArk/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4\n(419 files, 135,253,622,894 B): total 125.96 GiB = 135.3 GB; the 10\nmodel-plefp8-*.safetensors shards sum to 47.68 GiB = 51.2 GB.\n\n- 122 GiB -> 126 GiB (README:8,108; HOW-IT-WORKS:14,17; download-weights.sh:2)\n- 44 GiB / 47 GiB table -> 48 GiB everywhere; the docs'' own row math at\n  HOW-IT-WORKS:13 (16 x 20M x 160 B fp8) is 47.68 GiB, so 44 GiB was wrong\n- free-space guidance 130 GB -> 140 GB: the download alone is 135.3 GB\n- the two links to #optional-fp8-kv-cache-1m-context pointed at a heading that\n  does not exist in README.md; they now target the real section in docs/\n\n(cherry picked from commit 8b7743867ad7429349ef88f94b5a4623df9c8fcc)","tree":{"sha":"df2ddbf9c9ef42b0e390a4047e87b71f358e1b7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/git/trees/df2ddbf9c9ef42b0e390a4047e87b71f358e1b7c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/git/commits/daa3a11a8ffcad70b1a83db6f118c96557b68fbb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16634590?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blazux","id":16634590,"login":"blazux","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NjM0NTkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commit/daa3a11a8ffcad70b1a83db6f118c96557b68fbb","node_id":"C_kwDOUXaI9doAKGRhYTNhMTFhOGZmY2FkNzBiMWE4M2RiNmYxMThjOTY1NTdiNjhmYmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commit/b76890d5a033dd00166c792393d39cf908f56034","sha":"b76890d5a033dd00166c792393d39cf908f56034","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commits/b76890d5a033dd00166c792393d39cf908f56034"}],"sha":"daa3a11a8ffcad70b1a83db6f118c96557b68fbb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commits/daa3a11a8ffcad70b1a83db6f118c96557b68fbb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16634590?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blazux","id":16634590,"login":"blazux","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NjM0NTkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commits/b76890d5a033dd00166c792393d39cf908f56034/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T12:14:58Z","email":"vincent.blazutti@protonmail.com","name":"Blazux"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T12:14:58Z","email":"vincent.blazutti@protonmail.com","name":"Blazux"},"message":"Audit follow-ups (issue #8, by @sternnick): checksummed upstream fetches, e4m3-only fp8-KV guard, GPU_MEM=0.80 default, docs\n\n- Dockerfile: every file fetched from jschmied/qwen38-flash-next-gb10 is now\n  pinned by sha256 as well as by commit (ADD --checksum, one file per ADD);\n  the license notes are updated (that repo is Apache-2.0 since 2026-09-05).\n- src/patch_qsa_fp8_kv.py: the decode guard admitted float8_e5m2 while the\n  mqa launch only sets the quant mode for e4m3 — the guard now accepts e4m3 only.\n- scripts/serve.sh: GPU_MEM defaults to 0.80, which is what the README already\n  recommended for long-running service (0.85 drifted into swap after a day).\n- scripts/smoke-test.sh: the decode line says end-to-end and that it includes\n  TTFT, so it is not quoted as steady-state decode.\n- README: VLLM_PLE_MMAP_CHUNK documented, a note on the unauthenticated 0.0.0.0\n  binding and --api-key via EXTRA, credit in the Update section.\n- HOW-IT-WORKS: make explicit that the Mamba bounds guard is a leftover safety\n  net and that its counter has been 0 since the block_size fix.\n\nSize corrections and script fixes from the same audit land as PRs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"79b48275592fe582cf97cb38e7bc071c6727d277","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/git/trees/79b48275592fe582cf97cb38e7bc071c6727d277"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/git/commits/b76890d5a033dd00166c792393d39cf908f56034","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16634590?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blazux","id":16634590,"login":"blazux","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NjM0NTkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commit/b76890d5a033dd00166c792393d39cf908f56034","node_id":"C_kwDOUXaI9doAKGI3Njg5MGQ1YTAzM2RkMDAxNjZjNzkyMzkzZDM5Y2Y5MDhmNTYwMzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commit/89b852fb6b086c454b602f39d3ce86a76d6a507d","sha":"89b852fb6b086c454b602f39d3ce86a76d6a507d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commits/89b852fb6b086c454b602f39d3ce86a76d6a507d"}],"sha":"b76890d5a033dd00166c792393d39cf908f56034","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commits/b76890d5a033dd00166c792393d39cf908f56034"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16634590?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blazux","id":16634590,"login":"blazux","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NjM0NTkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commits/89b852fb6b086c454b602f39d3ce86a76d6a507d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T23:54:11Z","email":"vincent.blazutti@protonmail.com","name":"Blazux"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T23:54:11Z","email":"vincent.blazutti@protonmail.com","name":"Blazux"},"message":"Optional M%4 padding for the blockwise-fp8 GEMM (patch 9, by @jschmied): PAD_M4=1, for hybrid mode with prefix caching off\n\nThe preview image''s sm_12x blockwise-fp8 cutlass dispatch sends any GEMM whose\nrow count is not a multiple of 4 (or <= 64) down a swap_ab path that is ~1.7x\nslower below 2,048 rows and ~10x above (kernel micro-bench on a GX10; fixed\nupstream in C++ by vllm#52775 after this image was cut). Only the hybrid mode''s\nfp8 side layers use this GEMM.\n\n- Dockerfile: fetch @jschmied''s fp8_m4pad_patch.py at a pinned commit and apply\n  it at build; it pads M to a multiple of 4 inside an opaque custom op.\n- scripts/serve.sh: PAD_M4 knob, default 0. The variable is always passed\n  because the patch defaults to ON on sm_12x when it is unset.\n- README / HOW-IT-WORKS: use case and measurements. With PREFIX_CACHE=1 (default)\n  the Mamba align mode clips prefill chunks to the 1,600-token block, so the\n  large chunks are already 4-aligned and the patch is a no-op (same-session A/B:\n  8k 3.33 -> 3.24 s, 32k 11.63 -> 10.97 s, misaligned-last-chunk prompts at\n  3.60-3.69 s either way). With PREFIX_CACHE=0 it is worth about -40% TTFT at 8k.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d70b70cce6490b79f4876e6ff55c62f87f348a5b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/git/trees/d70b70cce6490b79f4876e6ff55c62f87f348a5b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/git/commits/89b852fb6b086c454b602f39d3ce86a76d6a507d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16634590?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blazux","id":16634590,"login":"blazux","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NjM0NTkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commit/89b852fb6b086c454b602f39d3ce86a76d6a507d","node_id":"C_kwDOUXaI9doAKDg5Yjg1MmZiNmIwODZjNDU0YjYwMmYzOWQzY2U4NmE3NmQ2YTUwN2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commit/4b723de2e2c465d866738b57ae64bde6e8c07744","sha":"4b723de2e2c465d866738b57ae64bde6e8c07744","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commits/4b723de2e2c465d866738b57ae64bde6e8c07744"}],"sha":"89b852fb6b086c454b602f39d3ce86a76d6a507d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commits/89b852fb6b086c454b602f39d3ce86a76d6a507d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16634590?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blazux","id":16634590,"login":"blazux","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NjM0NTkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/commits/4b723de2e2c465d866738b57ae64bde6e8c07744/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T18:06:57Z","email":"vincent.blazutti@protonmail.com","name":"Blazux"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T18:06:57Z","email":"vincent.blazutti@protonmail.com","name":"Blazux"},"message":"Deterministic persistent_topk kernel (patch 8, by @jschmied, vllm#55122): deterministic greedy at full prefill speed\n\n- Dockerfile: fetch @jschmied''s kernel sources at a pinned commit and compile\n  them with the image''s nvcc at build time (_C_det.so, ~12 s), wire the QSA\n  block selection to it behind VLLM_QSA_DET_TOPK=1 via his qsadet_patch.py.\n  His repo carries no license file, so the sources are fetched at build\n  rather than vendored; attribution in the Dockerfile and README.\n- scripts/serve.sh: DET_TOPK=1 is the new default, EXACT_TOPK=0 (the exact\n  torch.topk path stays as a fallback and wins when set).\n- README / HOW-IT-WORKS: Update section dated 2026-09-03, Deterministic top-k\n  section rewritten around the kernel, tuning table, credits, 3-way numbers.\n\nMeasured on the GX10 (hybrid, MTP=2, prefix caching, YaRN 500k):\n4/4 prompts deterministic, first-token logprobs identical; decode 32.5 tok/s,\nprefill 2,436 tok/s at 8k / 2,904 at 32k, needle 92k in 48 s — vs 1,476 /\n1,794 / 69 s with the exact torch.topk fix, i.e. the whole prefill penalty\nis gone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"924ab1c378f394ae1d9fd647e0c31ba884a1b18f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/git/trees/924ab1c378f394ae1d9fd647e0c31ba884a1b18f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shinrali/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVIDIA-Hybrid-Single-Spark/git/commits/4b723de2e2c465d866738b57ae64bde6e8c07744","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16634590?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blazux/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/blazux","id":16634590,"login":"blazux","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NjM0NTkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com